1
00:01:12,688 --> 00:01:14,896
<i>I aspired to reach
the pinnacle of wrestling.</i>

2
00:01:15,896 --> 00:01:16,980
But I couldn't make it.

3
00:01:18,813 --> 00:01:21,521
However, I hope my child will one day
represent our country in wrestling.

4
00:01:24,021 --> 00:01:25,604
If I'm married to you,
it won't happen.

5
00:01:25,605 --> 00:01:26,563
You may leave.

6
00:01:27,646 --> 00:01:29,479
Why are you doubting your ability?

7
00:01:29,480 --> 00:01:30,937
It's not like you're
too old to achieve it.

8
00:01:30,938 --> 00:01:32,146
I will help you achieve it.

9
00:01:35,063 --> 00:01:35,938
Are you serious?

10
00:01:37,730 --> 00:01:38,980
I swear on our unborn child.

11
00:01:56,813 --> 00:01:57,937
RAILWAY QUARTERS

12
00:01:57,938 --> 00:02:00,896
Hey, the water tanker has arrived!
Hurry up!

13
00:02:02,938 --> 00:02:04,688
Hey! Everyone, be patient
and fill your pots.

14
00:02:05,938 --> 00:02:08,145
It's been four days since the metro
pipe broke, and it's still not fixed.

15
00:02:08,146 --> 00:02:09,229
Damn you!

16
00:02:09,230 --> 00:02:11,854
Filling one pot alone
feels like a huge task.

17
00:02:11,855 --> 00:02:13,270
And someone's here with so many pots!

18
00:02:13,271 --> 00:02:14,395
Who the hell are you?

19
00:02:14,396 --> 00:02:18,980
<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

20
00:02:19,105 --> 00:02:21,271
<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

21
00:02:21,438 --> 00:02:23,854
- Sister, make way.
<i>- Take it easy, buddy</i>

22
00:02:23,855 --> 00:02:25,980
Step aside, sister.
Auntie, step aside.

23
00:02:28,521 --> 00:02:32,645
<i>Will life stop
While it's racing ahead?</i>

24
00:02:32,646 --> 00:02:33,563
Hey, don't shove me!

25
00:02:34,063 --> 00:02:36,480
Sister, I'm getting late.
Hey, help her get up.

26
00:02:37,021 --> 00:02:38,020
Come on, fill up your pots.

27
00:02:38,021 --> 00:02:42,271
{\an8}<i>Problems chase us every day
Will they ever let go?</i>

28
00:02:44,980 --> 00:02:47,146
{\an8}<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

29
00:02:50,105 --> 00:02:54,646
{\an8}<i>Who created this divide
Between men's and women's work, dear?</i>

30
00:02:54,813 --> 00:02:59,313
{\an8}<i>He who understands
The woman he loves lives like a King</i>

31
00:02:59,438 --> 00:03:01,563
{\an8}<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

32
00:03:01,855 --> 00:03:03,645
<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

33
00:03:03,646 --> 00:03:06,271
{\an8}<i>Don't take it too hard, buddy</i>

34
00:03:06,563 --> 00:03:08,771
<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

35
00:03:08,938 --> 00:03:10,896
<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

36
00:03:11,271 --> 00:03:13,605
<i>Take it easy, buddy</i>

37
00:03:14,146 --> 00:03:15,021
Mathi!

38
00:03:15,688 --> 00:03:16,563
Mathi!

39
00:03:17,021 --> 00:03:18,605
Sweetie, wake up.
It's getting late for school.

40
00:03:19,396 --> 00:03:20,895
Come on, wake up.
It's getting late.

41
00:03:20,896 --> 00:03:23,313
- Please give me two minutes, Pa.
- Your two minutes are very long.

42
00:03:23,438 --> 00:03:24,479
- Come on, wake up.
- I'm still sleepy, Pa.

43
00:03:24,480 --> 00:03:25,355
No more excuses. Wake up!

44
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:26,938
Be a sweetheart.

45
00:03:27,730 --> 00:03:30,105
<i>Love has no barriers</i>

46
00:03:32,480 --> 00:03:34,855
<i>Duty seeks no reward</i>

47
00:03:37,188 --> 00:03:41,230
<i>A smile turns
Everything into joy</i>

48
00:03:41,896 --> 00:03:45,437
<i>To a hopeful heart,
Even stones seem like sugar</i>

49
00:03:45,438 --> 00:03:48,437
Dad, don't forget to buy an eraser
on our way to school.

50
00:03:48,438 --> 00:03:50,312
How many erasers would you lose?

51
00:03:50,313 --> 00:03:52,688
It's not like an eraser is a big item.

52
00:03:53,063 --> 00:03:54,063
It's a tiny item.

53
00:03:54,396 --> 00:03:55,480
It's bound to get lost.

54
00:03:55,646 --> 00:03:57,105
Fine, I'll buy you one.

55
00:03:57,813 --> 00:03:59,188
Dad, lock up quick.
Let's leave.

56
00:03:59,563 --> 00:04:00,688
Did your husband leave for work?

57
00:04:00,896 --> 00:04:03,105
- He--
- No! Why do you ask?

58
00:04:03,771 --> 00:04:05,646
Nothing, I just asked.

59
00:04:06,021 --> 00:04:07,145
With so many houses around,

60
00:04:07,146 --> 00:04:09,021
why do you specifically
ask my wife about it?

61
00:04:09,313 --> 00:04:10,646
{\an8}Why shouldn't I suspect you?

62
00:04:11,021 --> 00:04:12,230
{\an8}Sir, why would you ask such a thing?

63
00:04:12,855 --> 00:04:15,979
{\an8}Isn't it normal to ask someone
whether you've left for work?

64
00:04:15,980 --> 00:04:17,145
{\an8}You're making a big deal about it.

65
00:04:17,146 --> 00:04:19,730
{\an8}A man who is a house husband…

66
00:04:20,021 --> 00:04:21,605
{\an8}goes to a newlywed woman,

67
00:04:21,938 --> 00:04:24,521
{\an8}and inquiring if the husband is home
or at work isn't normal.

68
00:04:24,938 --> 00:04:28,438
{\an8}In my case, I'm a TTR on the train, and
it takes me 3 days to get home from work.

69
00:04:28,563 --> 00:04:30,688
{\an8}During these three days,
my heart keeps beating fast.

70
00:04:31,730 --> 00:04:33,729
{\an8}- Damn, he left!
<i>- Mani, did you switch on the motor?</i>

71
00:04:33,730 --> 00:04:35,188
{\an8}<i>I just switched on the motor.</i>

72
00:04:35,355 --> 00:04:36,771
{\an8}- Hey, watchman, come over here.
- Sir!

73
00:04:37,355 --> 00:04:38,562
{\an8}- I'm assigning you a task.
- Sir.

74
00:04:38,563 --> 00:04:41,271
{\an8}- Watch the CCTV 24 hours carefully.
- Okay, Sir.

75
00:04:41,438 --> 00:04:44,438
{\an8}If someone is entering another flat
besides their own…

76
00:04:44,771 --> 00:04:45,812
{\an8}inform me.

77
00:04:45,813 --> 00:04:47,354
{\an8}Sir, why are you beating around the bush?

78
00:04:47,355 --> 00:04:50,730
{\an8}It's my duty to catch him
and your wife red-handed.

79
00:04:50,855 --> 00:04:52,479
{\an8}Don't worry about it and head to work.

80
00:04:52,480 --> 00:04:53,355
{\an8}I'll handle it.

81
00:04:53,605 --> 00:04:55,938
What?
You'll catch them red-handed, you say?

82
00:05:00,896 --> 00:05:02,021
Come on, hurry up!

83
00:05:03,021 --> 00:05:04,188
Once again, you're late to school.

84
00:05:04,396 --> 00:05:05,771
This is not right, sweetie.

85
00:05:06,146 --> 00:05:07,187
What's not right?

86
00:05:07,188 --> 00:05:09,688
You woke up a child from deep sleep.

87
00:05:09,813 --> 00:05:13,646
It's better for a child
to arrive late than

88
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:15,396
to be forced
to arrive at school too early.

89
00:05:15,605 --> 00:05:17,937
If you keep talking like this you'll
get beatings from your Teacher.

90
00:05:17,938 --> 00:05:18,813
Hurry up!

91
00:05:20,438 --> 00:05:21,313
Madam!

92
00:05:23,646 --> 00:05:25,188
- Bye, bye.
- Bye, I'll see you in the evening.

93
00:05:26,688 --> 00:05:27,813
Where are you leaving?

94
00:05:28,146 --> 00:05:29,855
We have a Parents-Teacher meeting today.

95
00:05:29,980 --> 00:05:31,855
No, teacher,
today I have a wrestling match to go to.

96
00:05:32,021 --> 00:05:33,104
I'm already running late.

97
00:05:33,105 --> 00:05:34,105
I'll finish it and come back.

98
00:05:34,230 --> 00:05:35,937
I can't wait for you.

99
00:05:35,938 --> 00:05:37,813
Now that you're here,
attend the meeting, and you may leave.

100
00:05:40,313 --> 00:05:41,188
So, tell me, teacher.

101
00:05:41,313 --> 00:05:43,271
What do I even say?
See for yourself.

102
00:05:46,813 --> 00:05:48,188
She failed in all the subjects.

103
00:05:48,730 --> 00:05:50,813
She can't even finish a rhyme.

104
00:05:51,855 --> 00:05:53,813
Her homework is always incomplete.

105
00:05:54,021 --> 00:05:55,855
Do you make any effort
to help her study at home?

106
00:05:56,105 --> 00:05:58,480
Do you make any effort
to help her study at school?

107
00:05:58,813 --> 00:06:00,355
Do you even realize what you're saying?

108
00:06:00,646 --> 00:06:01,980
No matter how much effort we put in,

109
00:06:02,105 --> 00:06:04,313
it never seems enough to survive
in today's highly competitive world.

110
00:06:05,230 --> 00:06:06,230
Okay, Teacher. What else?

111
00:06:07,271 --> 00:06:08,146
What else?

112
00:06:08,688 --> 00:06:09,980
She's very talkative!

113
00:06:10,230 --> 00:06:12,313
She's always yapping during the class.

114
00:06:12,521 --> 00:06:14,563
She's becoming a bad influence
on the other students.

115
00:06:16,521 --> 00:06:17,896
Last week I checked my blood pressure.

116
00:06:18,480 --> 00:06:20,562
- It's beyond 200 now.
- Oh, no!

117
00:06:20,563 --> 00:06:22,313
I truly can't take this anymore.

118
00:06:22,563 --> 00:06:24,105
Didn't you mention the same
during the last PTA meeting?

119
00:06:24,271 --> 00:06:25,271
I don't see anything new.

120
00:06:25,896 --> 00:06:27,146
Should I sign here?

121
00:06:28,980 --> 00:06:30,771
- Here, go sign it!
- Thank you, Teacher.

122
00:06:31,938 --> 00:06:34,479
I have a wrestling match to go to.
So I cut the line.

123
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:35,604
Sorry, sorry. I'm leaving.

124
00:06:35,605 --> 00:06:36,604
Bye! Everyone, bye.

125
00:06:36,605 --> 00:06:37,480
- Bye!
- Bye!

126
00:06:37,605 --> 00:06:39,688
Is he a wrestler?

127
00:06:39,855 --> 00:06:40,730
Don't be fooled!

128
00:06:41,313 --> 00:06:44,521
Even a wrestler won't mention
about a match so many times.

129
00:06:44,813 --> 00:06:47,271
He's not a wrestler, but his wife is.

130
00:06:47,438 --> 00:06:51,730
Keerthi! Keerthi!

131
00:06:52,063 --> 00:06:53,063
Come on, start!

132
00:07:03,771 --> 00:07:05,396
<i>Fierce wrestling</i>

133
00:07:10,771 --> 00:07:12,313
<i>Fierce wrestling</i>

134
00:07:12,938 --> 00:07:14,646
Come on, Keerthi. Come on, Keerthi.
Come on. Come on.

135
00:07:17,313 --> 00:07:18,271
Defend!

136
00:07:18,771 --> 00:07:19,646
Coach!

137
00:07:22,855 --> 00:07:24,688
Hold her down. Lock! Lock!

138
00:07:25,230 --> 00:07:26,521
Hey, flip her! Flip her!

139
00:07:27,563 --> 00:07:29,021
Come on, flip her.

140
00:07:37,355 --> 00:07:38,271
Did you see that move?

141
00:07:38,980 --> 00:07:39,855
Come on!

142
00:07:41,771 --> 00:07:43,188
<i>Fierce wrestling</i>

143
00:07:45,230 --> 00:07:47,480
Come on, Keerthi! Come on!
Hold her down!

144
00:07:48,105 --> 00:07:51,813
Come on, come on! Break the lock.

145
00:07:52,563 --> 00:07:53,563
<i>Fierce</i>

146
00:07:56,105 --> 00:07:57,021
<i>Wrestling</i>

147
00:07:59,230 --> 00:08:02,146
Yayy! Hey! Hey!

148
00:08:09,896 --> 00:08:10,771
<i>Fierce</i>

149
00:08:13,313 --> 00:08:14,188
<i>Wrestling</i>

150
00:08:21,021 --> 00:08:22,563
<i>Fierce wrestling</i>

151
00:08:31,188 --> 00:08:33,813
I thought you'd lose
when she locked you in.

152
00:08:34,105 --> 00:08:36,063
Thank goodness you broke her hold
and attacked her.

153
00:08:36,188 --> 00:08:37,770
What did they say during the PTA meeting?

154
00:08:37,771 --> 00:08:39,270
Nothing much to say, though.

155
00:08:39,271 --> 00:08:40,229
They said she's a good girl.

156
00:08:40,230 --> 00:08:41,563
She's studying well.

157
00:08:41,730 --> 00:08:43,605
Also, she's the teacher's pet.

158
00:08:44,021 --> 00:08:44,938
Phew!

159
00:08:45,521 --> 00:08:47,355
- She's her mother's daughter.
- Of course!

160
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:49,230
Congratulations, Keerthi!

161
00:08:49,396 --> 00:08:50,980
- Well played!
- Thank you, Coach.

162
00:08:51,771 --> 00:08:53,688
Veera, why are you carrying
so many bottles?

163
00:08:53,855 --> 00:08:55,021
This is ABC juice.

164
00:08:55,521 --> 00:08:59,063
And this is mixed-nut juice,
exclusively prepared by me.

165
00:08:59,438 --> 00:09:01,271
And this is millet flour porridge
for lunch.

166
00:09:01,938 --> 00:09:05,230
If a wife has a husband like him,
she'll be unstoppable.

167
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:07,021
You're really gifted, Keerthi.

168
00:09:07,438 --> 00:09:08,646
- Bye.
- Okay, Coach.

169
00:09:16,313 --> 00:09:17,855
- Who is it?
- My aunt from hometown.

170
00:09:18,396 --> 00:09:20,521
- Hi, auntie, how are you?
- I'm doing well, Veera!

171
00:09:20,813 --> 00:09:22,563
How are Keerthi and Mathi?

172
00:09:22,688 --> 00:09:24,396
No complaints, they're doing very well.

173
00:09:24,563 --> 00:09:28,021
Coming Sunday, Subbaraj's son
is getting married at the temple.

174
00:09:28,355 --> 00:09:30,063
<i>As it's our relative's wedding…</i>

175
00:09:30,438 --> 00:09:32,355
your uncle invited you
and your family to attend it.

176
00:09:32,480 --> 00:09:33,979
Why didn't he call himself?

177
00:09:33,980 --> 00:09:35,770
<i>You know your uncle very well.</i>

178
00:09:35,771 --> 00:09:36,938
You must attend the wedding.

179
00:09:37,313 --> 00:09:38,188
Okay, auntie!

180
00:09:38,938 --> 00:09:39,938
What was the call about?

181
00:09:40,688 --> 00:09:42,605
There's a wedding happening
in the hometown, thus the invitation.

182
00:09:43,313 --> 00:09:44,855
Fine, I'm leaving. I'm running late.

183
00:09:45,355 --> 00:09:47,145
People in society
will be waiting for me.

184
00:09:47,146 --> 00:09:48,438
Hey, what song are you playing today?

185
00:10:29,188 --> 00:10:30,896
So soon, it reached 50,000 likes.

186
00:10:31,980 --> 00:10:33,021
Forget about the likes.

187
00:10:33,646 --> 00:10:34,813
Did you read the comments?

188
00:10:35,146 --> 00:10:36,438
There's one comment…

189
00:10:36,605 --> 00:10:40,063
"They may be old,
but these aunties look ravishing."

190
00:10:40,396 --> 00:10:43,521
"I must kidnap them all
and take them to Andaman Island."

191
00:10:43,688 --> 00:10:45,521
That's nothing.
I read another comment.

192
00:10:45,771 --> 00:10:48,479
"Who's that beauty
in a black saree in the front?"

193
00:10:48,480 --> 00:10:50,687
"Her husband must be a lucky fellow."

194
00:10:50,688 --> 00:10:51,771
Who was in black saree?

195
00:10:51,896 --> 00:10:54,480
Who else do you think?
It's Partha's wife.

196
00:10:55,230 --> 00:10:57,438
Reels like this ruin many families.

197
00:10:58,855 --> 00:11:00,605
Veera is the root cause of this problem.

198
00:11:00,896 --> 00:11:05,146
He's doing weird things
in the name of exercise and aerobics.

199
00:11:05,313 --> 00:11:07,105
He does not stop with just exercise.

200
00:11:07,396 --> 00:11:08,812
How to make onion sambhar.

201
00:11:08,813 --> 00:11:11,355
How to knead flour for chapatis.
He teaches it all.

202
00:11:11,646 --> 00:11:13,021
I can even make peace with these things.

203
00:11:13,188 --> 00:11:14,605
The other day I was returning from work…

204
00:11:15,021 --> 00:11:16,645
Do you know what he was teaching my wife?

205
00:11:16,646 --> 00:11:19,688
What is that "stone, paper, scissors"
you play with your daughter?

206
00:11:19,813 --> 00:11:21,063
It's an easy game.

207
00:11:21,188 --> 00:11:22,145
This is stone.

208
00:11:22,146 --> 00:11:23,187
This is paper.

209
00:11:23,188 --> 00:11:24,063
And this is scissor.

210
00:11:24,396 --> 00:11:25,730
Stone, paper, scissors.

211
00:11:26,396 --> 00:11:27,313
Shall we play?

212
00:11:28,105 --> 00:11:29,813
Stone, paper, scissors.

213
00:11:34,605 --> 00:11:35,854
What are you guys doing?

214
00:11:35,855 --> 00:11:37,687
I'm paper, and he's scissors.

215
00:11:37,688 --> 00:11:38,813
He's scissoring me.

216
00:11:38,938 --> 00:11:39,813
Scissoring?

217
00:11:42,313 --> 00:11:43,895
If we want these problems to end,

218
00:11:43,896 --> 00:11:45,938
- we need to persuade him to start working.
- I agree!

219
00:11:46,063 --> 00:11:48,229
That's why I spent 5,000 rupees
to throw this party.

220
00:11:48,230 --> 00:11:49,105
I understand.

221
00:11:50,021 --> 00:11:51,855
He's living happily with his wife.

222
00:11:52,230 --> 00:11:54,563
I won't spare him. Wait and watch.

223
00:11:54,813 --> 00:11:56,480
I have lot of work in the morning.
I have to go to bed early--

224
00:12:01,021 --> 00:12:01,896
Oh, my!

225
00:12:12,855 --> 00:12:13,813
Here I come.

226
00:12:25,855 --> 00:12:27,770
What happened, Dad?

227
00:12:27,771 --> 00:12:29,687
Nothing, dear.
Mom dropped the glass.

228
00:12:29,688 --> 00:12:32,271
It's become a habit now.

229
00:12:32,480 --> 00:12:33,355
You go back to sleep.

230
00:12:37,146 --> 00:12:39,063
How many times should I tell you?

231
00:12:39,563 --> 00:12:41,855
Not to sneak up on me
and kiss me on my neck.

232
00:12:42,855 --> 00:12:43,855
I like it.

233
00:12:46,980 --> 00:12:48,730
Dad, please don't sing.

234
00:12:48,938 --> 00:12:50,355
Okay, okay, I won't sing.

235
00:12:50,563 --> 00:12:51,604
Shall I tell you a story?

236
00:12:51,605 --> 00:12:53,020
I don't want to hear a story.

237
00:12:53,021 --> 00:12:55,438
But I want a younger brother, though.

238
00:12:55,646 --> 00:12:56,771
Younger brother, you say?

239
00:12:59,521 --> 00:13:00,770
Ask Mom! Ask Mom!

240
00:13:00,771 --> 00:13:03,188
- Mom!
- You're not getting a younger brother.

241
00:13:03,646 --> 00:13:05,480
- Shut up and sleep.
- Why not?

242
00:13:06,396 --> 00:13:11,188
My classmates Deepak, Darshan, Diya,
and others have a younger brother.

243
00:13:11,438 --> 00:13:12,645
I want a brother too.

244
00:13:12,646 --> 00:13:13,896
That too, I want it tomorrow.

245
00:13:14,438 --> 00:13:17,771
It's not a product you can get overnight
delivery on from Amazon or Flipkart.

246
00:13:18,396 --> 00:13:19,271
Go back to sleep!

247
00:13:19,896 --> 00:13:21,480
It doesn't happen overnight, dear.

248
00:13:21,646 --> 00:13:22,687
It will take Pathu Maasam.

249
00:13:22,688 --> 00:13:25,438
- What do you mean by Pathu Maasam?
- It means 10 months.

