00:27:25,980 --> 00:27:27,771
But you went there
and beat up four people.

508
00:27:29,771 --> 00:27:32,813
The daughter and
father deserve each other.

509
00:27:33,105 --> 00:27:37,813
Darshan and Deepak mocked,
calling Dad a house husband.

510
00:27:37,938 --> 00:27:39,730
That's why I beat them up.

511
00:27:39,938 --> 00:27:41,980
There's nothing wrong with calling him
a house husband.

512
00:27:43,563 --> 00:27:44,896
Let them say it.

513
00:27:45,146 --> 00:27:46,479
Why would you cause problem?

514
00:27:46,480 --> 00:27:49,188
My father is a wrestler just like you.

515
00:27:49,313 --> 00:27:50,188
Check this out.

516
00:27:50,646 --> 00:27:52,313
He defeated a coach!

517
00:27:52,896 --> 00:27:55,521
It's cute for you to think
that what he did was wrestling.

518
00:27:55,730 --> 00:27:57,230
It's just a fight.

519
00:27:57,396 --> 00:27:59,520
That coach spoke ill about me.

520
00:27:59,521 --> 00:28:01,271
So, out of anger, he beat him up.

521
00:28:02,105 --> 00:28:04,646
Back in the hometown,
the President uncle told me,

522
00:28:04,771 --> 00:28:08,771
not to call Dad a house husband,
but to call him a wrestler.

523
00:28:08,896 --> 00:28:10,105
Hey, don't say it.

524
00:28:10,563 --> 00:28:12,188
You must not say
things like that to your mother.

525
00:28:12,355 --> 00:28:14,855
Now I see where my daughter gets it from.

526
00:28:15,355 --> 00:28:18,896
Listen, you may listen to anyone
in this world, but not that man.

527
00:28:19,146 --> 00:28:22,438
He hails from a group
that glorifies patriarchy.

528
00:28:23,105 --> 00:28:24,688
Why would you indulge a child
with such conversation?

529
00:28:24,855 --> 00:28:26,395
She wishes to call her Dad a wrestler.

530
00:28:26,396 --> 00:28:27,396
So be it.

531
00:28:27,855 --> 00:28:30,605
It's our duty as parents
to bring her clarity on matters.

532
00:28:31,313 --> 00:28:33,771
If we fail to do it,
this will be the result.

533
00:28:34,146 --> 00:28:36,980
Listen, dear, your Dad is a house husband.

534
00:28:37,438 --> 00:28:39,188
There's nothing wrong with it.

535
00:28:39,646 --> 00:28:40,521
Understand?

536
00:28:44,188 --> 00:28:45,063
Vani!

537
00:28:45,730 --> 00:28:46,646
Step aside!

538
00:28:47,063 --> 00:28:48,563
Why is he bringing water to our house?

539
00:28:48,730 --> 00:28:51,105
You won't move a muscle,
but you find faults in him.

540
00:28:51,605 --> 00:28:52,480
Annoying!

541
00:28:54,813 --> 00:28:57,605
<i>Goodness gracious, my girl!</i>

542
00:28:57,813 --> 00:28:59,480
I made your favorite brinjal curry.

543
00:28:59,646 --> 00:29:01,021
You'd better finish it all.
Okay?

544
00:29:01,146 --> 00:29:03,605
<i>No way
Not this troublemaker</i>

545
00:29:03,813 --> 00:29:05,812
<i>He's a sly rogue
Who keeps putting on an act</i>

546
00:29:05,813 --> 00:29:06,770
This is cheating!

547
00:29:06,771 --> 00:29:07,646
Thank you.

548
00:29:08,521 --> 00:29:09,521
Where is he coming from?

549
00:29:10,230 --> 00:29:11,855
I ran out of sugar for coffee.

550
00:29:12,105 --> 00:29:14,230
Why can't you have coffee without sugar?

551
00:29:14,480 --> 00:29:16,396
You have country sugar.
It tastes good!

552
00:29:16,521 --> 00:29:19,395
- Country sugar?
<i>- Hey! Hey! House husband</i>

553
00:29:19,396 --> 00:29:21,937
<i>My BP shoots up seeing you!</i>

554
00:29:21,938 --> 00:29:23,730
- Are you making chapatis?
- Yes!

555
00:29:24,146 --> 00:29:25,312
Why knead the dough so late?

556
00:29:25,313 --> 00:29:27,395
"Longing to Fly" serial was playing.

557
00:29:27,396 --> 00:29:29,105
I lost track of time watching it.

558
00:29:41,230 --> 00:29:42,438
- Hi, Sir!
- Hello!

559
00:29:43,438 --> 00:29:45,271
I'm going to create an ID
called "House Husband"

560
00:29:45,438 --> 00:29:47,771
I'll keep posting
until he finds an actual job.

561
00:29:48,146 --> 00:29:51,355
In our country, there are fewer
people who work out of passion

562
00:29:51,521 --> 00:29:53,355
than those who work out of humiliation.

563
00:29:53,480 --> 00:29:54,355
Oh!

564
00:29:56,980 --> 00:29:58,646
{\an8}- House Husband?
- Hey, show me the video.

565
00:29:58,896 --> 00:30:01,479
Veera, your reels are going viral.
Awesome!

566
00:30:01,480 --> 00:30:03,646
Sir, I watched your reels.
They're fantastic!

567
00:30:04,355 --> 00:30:05,812
- Veera!
- Yes, Auntie!

568
00:30:05,813 --> 00:30:08,021
- Your reels are getting a greater reach.
- Thanks!

569
00:30:08,313 --> 00:30:09,729
{\an8}He's a perfect example of a good husband.

570
00:30:09,730 --> 00:30:11,313
{\an8}- First let's…
- Comment on the video.

571
00:30:12,313 --> 00:30:14,230
{\an8}Just because I told our daughter
that you're a house husband

572
00:30:14,438 --> 00:30:15,980
{\an8}you're started making such reels.

573
00:30:16,438 --> 00:30:17,937
{\an8}I swear I'm not making them.

574
00:30:17,938 --> 00:30:19,479
I have nothing to do with it.

575
00:30:19,480 --> 00:30:20,688
I don't know who is making them.

576
00:30:21,563 --> 00:30:23,855
{\an8}Every reel is gaining a lot of views.

577
00:30:24,146 --> 00:30:25,730
Soon we'll be making money from it.

578
00:30:26,855 --> 00:30:28,770
- Shall we continue this as a business?
- It's a good idea.

579
00:30:28,771 --> 00:30:29,646
{\an8}I ought to!

580
00:30:30,688 --> 00:30:33,771
{\an8}Among the dishes you make,
which is your wife's favorite dish?

581
00:30:34,646 --> 00:30:35,646
Come with me!

582
00:30:38,938 --> 00:30:41,980
{\an8}<i>Hey! Hey! House husband</i>

583
00:30:45,980 --> 00:30:48,438
- It's outstanding, Sir.
- Thank you!

584
00:30:49,980 --> 00:30:53,980
Keerthi will be taking part
in the upcoming South Indian Tournament.

585
00:30:54,521 --> 00:30:56,855
Another player from the same academy
can compete for Team B.

586
00:30:57,396 --> 00:30:58,938
I have suggested your name.

587
00:31:00,063 --> 00:31:01,020
Thank you, Coach!

588
00:31:01,021 --> 00:31:02,646
To hell with your thanks!

589
00:31:03,730 --> 00:31:07,812
This time, you must defeat Keerthi
in the first round.

590
00:31:07,813 --> 00:31:09,521
That's how you'd be thanking me.

591
00:31:10,813 --> 00:31:13,021
First round? How's it possible?

592
00:31:13,980 --> 00:31:15,146
Leave that to me.

593
00:31:21,896 --> 00:31:24,355
Sweetie, who’s this at your school
with all that gorgeous thick hair?

594
00:31:25,855 --> 00:31:27,771
Look up! She's my teacher!

595
00:31:32,480 --> 00:31:33,563
Your teacher?

596
00:31:43,646 --> 00:31:44,771
Why is she coming towards me?

597
00:31:44,938 --> 00:31:48,020
I watched your reels.
Very interesting!

598
00:31:48,021 --> 00:31:48,979
You too?

599
00:31:48,980 --> 00:31:50,355
I don't know who's making them, Teacher.

600
00:31:50,813 --> 00:31:53,146
Forget about it.
Where in Kerala are you from?

601
00:31:53,355 --> 00:31:54,230
Cochin!

602
00:31:54,563 --> 00:31:55,563
Are you a Malayali?

603
00:31:56,230 --> 00:31:57,105
Half Malayali!

604
00:31:59,063 --> 00:32:00,063
That's interesting!

605
00:32:00,313 --> 00:32:01,271
What's your name?

606
00:32:01,396 --> 00:32:02,271
Meenu.

607
00:32:02,438 --> 00:32:03,730
Your eyes reveal your name.

608
00:32:05,855 --> 00:32:07,438
If you don't mind,
may I ask you something?

609
00:32:07,896 --> 00:32:08,771
Go ahead!

610
00:32:09,521 --> 00:32:10,855
Are yours original?

611
00:32:11,063 --> 00:32:12,646
What? What do you mean?

612
00:32:13,230 --> 00:32:15,146
No-- I meant, is your hair original?

613
00:32:15,521 --> 00:32:16,480
Phew!

614
00:32:20,230 --> 00:32:21,105
Hold it.

615
00:32:22,771 --> 00:32:24,021
I don't mind. Hold it.

616
00:32:25,021 --> 00:32:26,145
- Pull it.
- Sure?

617
00:32:26,146 --> 00:32:27,146
You may pull and check.

618
00:32:33,813 --> 00:32:35,605
- Okay?
- They're original.

619
00:32:35,938 --> 00:32:38,895
I heard that during a fight,
someone pulled your wife’s hair

620
00:32:38,896 --> 00:32:41,230
and it came off in front of the crowd,
humiliating her.

621
00:32:47,938 --> 00:32:50,771
So, I reckon you suspect
everyone may have fake hair.

622
00:32:51,063 --> 00:32:53,730
However, don't keep checking people's hair
as you did just now.

623
00:32:57,688 --> 00:32:58,563
I'm leaving!

624
00:33:00,188 --> 00:33:01,063
Hey, Sweetie--

625
00:33:01,396 --> 00:33:02,646
Why is she getting angry?

626
00:33:03,938 --> 00:33:05,688
<i>Let's go together. That'd be best.</i>

627
00:33:06,230 --> 00:33:08,105
Oh, please wait for me to arrive there.

628
00:33:08,438 --> 00:33:09,980
Okay, I'll call you back later.

629
00:33:10,230 --> 00:33:11,105
I'm hanging up.

630
00:33:11,563 --> 00:33:15,896
You speak to your mother
and grandma in Malayalam.

631
00:33:16,438 --> 00:33:18,688
But I don't see you
speaking in Malayalam to Dad.

632
00:33:18,813 --> 00:33:19,688
Why is it, Mom?

633
00:33:20,105 --> 00:33:21,980
Your father doesn't know Malayalam.

634
00:33:22,230 --> 00:33:23,229
Who said so?

635
00:33:23,230 --> 00:33:25,271
He speaks Malayalam well at school.

636
00:33:25,563 --> 00:33:27,396
In Malayalam, you say?
With whom?

637
00:33:27,938 --> 00:33:29,105
He speaks to my Teacher.

638
00:33:30,521 --> 00:33:33,188
- Teacher?
- Yeah, my new Teacher.

639
00:33:33,938 --> 00:33:35,020
Is she a Malayali?

640
00:33:35,021 --> 00:33:37,188
I hear her say she's from Cochin.

641
00:33:40,771 --> 00:33:41,688
Is she married?

642
00:33:42,188 --> 00:33:43,188
No!

643
00:33:46,938 --> 00:33:48,188
How does she look?

644
00:33:48,521 --> 00:33:49,771
She's beautiful.

645
00:33:52,355 --> 00:33:53,980
How beautiful?

646
00:33:55,605 --> 00:33:57,813
She's more beautiful than you.
Enough?

647
00:33:59,021 --> 00:33:59,896
Oh!

648
00:34:01,980 --> 00:34:03,730
How long has this been going on?

649
00:34:03,896 --> 00:34:05,438
It's been just a few days.

650
00:34:10,563 --> 00:34:11,521
Does she have hair?

651
00:34:11,855 --> 00:34:14,271
- Of course, she has hair, Mom.
- Nah!

652
00:34:15,230 --> 00:34:18,355
Like you see thick and fluffy hair
in oil advertisements…

653
00:34:18,646 --> 00:34:20,730
Does she have long hair?

654
00:34:21,980 --> 00:34:22,855
Turn around.

655
00:34:24,563 --> 00:34:26,063
Turn around, I'll show you.

656
00:34:29,063 --> 00:34:30,438
Her hair runs till here.

657
00:34:36,105 --> 00:34:38,520
Now I understand
why the rat is running naked.

658
00:34:38,521 --> 00:34:40,563
And why your Dad is speaking in Malayalam.

659
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:42,563
Let him come home.

660
00:34:42,730 --> 00:34:44,937
No matter how many years pass by
his brain is still stuck in it.

661
00:34:44,938 --> 00:34:46,396
Oh, God, you've gone mad, Mom.

662
00:34:46,813 --> 00:34:48,563
The moment he sees a woman
with long hair.

663
00:34:49,188 --> 00:34:50,480
What on earth is going on in my house?

664
00:34:57,521 --> 00:34:58,771
So, what are you up to?

665
00:35:00,688 --> 00:35:01,937
How does it matter to you?

666
00:35:01,938 --> 00:35:03,145
You have someone to talk to now.

667
00:35:03,146 --> 00:35:04,021
Go and speak to her.

668
00:35:04,605 --> 00:35:06,520
What are you saying?
I don't understand.

669
00:35:06,521 --> 00:35:08,355
Of course, you wouldn't
understand me anymore.

670
00:35:08,646 --> 00:35:09,896
- What?
- Bloody man.

671
00:35:10,105 --> 00:35:11,146
Loafing around.

672
00:35:14,271 --> 00:35:15,646
Why is she looking at the hair?

673
00:35:21,396 --> 00:35:22,396
Come on, we're running late.

674
00:35:23,563 --> 00:35:24,855
Come on, get on the bike.

675
00:35:25,438 --> 00:35:26,395
Why?

676
00:35:26,396 --> 00:35:27,980
Stop asking questions
and get on the bike.

677
00:35:28,271 --> 00:35:29,980
Hereafter,
I'll be dropping you off at school.

678
00:35:32,230 --> 00:35:34,563
Does that mean
Dad will pick me up in the evening?

679
00:35:37,646 --> 00:35:39,396
Your Dad is an expert pick-up artist!

680
00:35:39,896 --> 00:35:41,271
Get on the bike, girl!

681
00:35:42,396 --> 00:35:43,688
- What happened?
- I don't know.

682
00:35:45,188 --> 00:35:46,480
What did I even pick up?

683
00:35:51,396 --> 00:35:52,271
Get off the bike.

684
00:35:55,313 --> 00:35:56,230
{\an8}Who is your Teacher?

685
00:35:59,813 --> 00:36:00,688
There she is.

686
00:36:02,480 --> 00:36:04,604
- Everyone, please work hard.
- Yes, Ma'am.

687
00:36:04,605 --> 00:36:05,605
Or else it'll be difficult.

688
00:36:05,813 --> 00:36:06,770
Okay?

689
00:36:06,771 --> 00:36:08,271
- Okay, bye!
- Thank you, Ma'am.

690
00:36:09,938 --> 00:36:11,230
She's not more beautiful than I am.

691
00:36:14,521 --> 00:36:16,021
Hi, Mathi!

692
00:36:16,438 --> 00:36:17,438
Didn't your Dad come to drop you off?

693
00:36:18,688 --> 00:36:20,813
Dad won't be coming.
Hereafter, Mom will be coming.

694
00:36:32,188 --> 00:36:33,063
Let's go!

695
00:36:38,855 --> 00:36:40,313
Why did you stop running?

696
00:36:41,396 --> 00:36:43,146
Enough, Coach.
I am not able to continue.

697
00:36:44,355 --> 00:36:46,480
You'll be taking part
in the South Indian Tournament.

698
00:36:47,021 --> 00:36:50,271
Even if the players are from Andhra,
Karnataka, and Telangana,

699
00:36:50,688 --> 00:36:52,438
the winner will be Keerthi.

700
00:36:54,230 --> 00:36:57,105
You're the only wrestler
who can fight her head-on.

701
00:36:58,063 --> 00:37:00,938
Still, you have lost to her seven times.

702
00:37:01,813 --> 00:37:03,605
She'll win and move to Delhi.

703
00:37:03,938 --> 00:37:05,646
But you'll be left circling locally.

704
00:37:07,605 --> 00:37:09,355
Do you want to go to Delhi
or remain local?

705
00:37:17,230 --> 00:37:22,313
And now, I request our respected
Principal Ma'am to present the prizes.

706
00:37:24,063 --> 00:37:25,605
Niranjan, swimming.

707
00:37:28,021 --> 00:37:29,563
- Well done.
- Hey, Keerthi!

708
00:37:29,980 --> 00:37:31,313
The head of your office is calling you.

709
00:37:31,480 --> 00:37:32,813
Oh! I'll meet her.

710
00:37:35,563 --> 00:37:36,980
G. Prashanth, carrom.

711
00:37:37,396 --> 00:37:39,313
- That's my son.
- That's great!

712
00:37:39,688 --> 00:37:40,771
Hold this and look at the camera.

713
00:37:41,146 --> 00:37:42,105
Very cute!

714
00:37:44,313 --> 00:37:46,687
Where's your daughter?
Didn't she participate in any sport?

715
00:37:46,688 --> 00:37:48,271
Naseer, long jump.

716
00:37:49,855 --> 00:37:51,605
Listen, where's Mathi?

717
00:37:52,396 --> 00:37:54,479
- Surprise!
- Thank you so much, sir and ma'am,

718
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:55,938
for your lovely gestures.

719
00:37:56,313 --> 00:38:00,813
Finally, our little stars
from first grade, B section,

720
00:38:01,063 --> 00:38:02,063
are ready!

721
00:38:02,521 --> 00:38:05,396
A big applause for all of them!

722
00:38:35,313 --> 00:38:36,188
Hey!

723
00:38:36,563 --> 00:38:38,062
What's this?
Why is she dancing like this?

724
00:38:38,063 --> 00:38:39,480
This is how one could dance to this song.

725
00:39:13,980 --> 00:39:15,980
Your daughter has got great moves!

726
00:39:16,271 --> 00:39:17,146
Super!

727
00:39:31,188 --> 00:39:33,396
Even the laziest parents' kids
are winning prizes in sports.

728
00:39:33,521 --> 00:39:34,521
But you couldn't do it.

729
00:39:34,813 --> 00:39:37,188
How could you not participate
in any sports activity?

730
00:39:37,730 --> 00:39:40,813
But you can dance like a pro
with all that jazz.

731
00:39:41,855 --> 00:39:43,396
I don't know what to do with you.

732
00:39:46,855 --> 00:39:48,396
Kids generally love to dance.

733
00:39:48,896 --> 00:39:49,937
Why are you getting worked up?

734
00:39:49,938 --> 00:39:51,521
I'm not stopping her from dancing.

735
00:39:51,688 --> 00:39:53,396
But she's the daughter
of a State Champion.

736
00:39:53,646 --> 00:39:57,396
It's embarrassing for me when my
daughter doesn't participate in any sport.

737
00:39:59,105 --> 00:40:00,479
She's just in 1st grade now.

738
00:40:00,480 --> 00:40:01,645
Why hurry her with sports?

739
00:40:01,646 --> 00:40:04,105
Sports should be cultivated
from a young age.

740
00:40:04,230 --> 00:40:06,230
If you can't bend when you're 5,
you can't bend when you're 50.

741
00:40:07,771 --> 00:40:08,646
Sir!

742
00:40:09,230 --> 00:40:11,021
Yes, Teacher.

743
00:40:11,813 --> 00:40:13,771
Today, your daughter nailed it.

744
00:40:14,438 --> 00:40:16,521
- Thank you, Teacher.
- She danced well.

745
00:40:16,813 --> 00:40:18,105
Even Simran can't beat her.

746
00:40:18,521 --> 00:40:22,146
I couldn't believe
that she possesses a hidden talent.

747
00:40:22,438 --> 00:40:24,063
{\an8}Please tell her mother.
She's yelling at us.

748
00:40:24,980 --> 00:40:27,438
You come to the school
only on the Annual Day.

749
00:40:27,605 --> 00:40:29,438
Please don't take me wrong.

750
00:40:29,563 --> 00:40:31,687
Your daughter may be bad at studies…

751
00:40:31,688 --> 00:40:33,230
but she's great at dancing.

752
00:40:34,063 --> 00:40:38,063
If you send her regularly for practice
and train her well

753
00:40:38,230 --> 00:40:40,396
she'll win a title
on the Jodi No.1 reality show.

754
00:40:40,605 --> 00:40:42,355
{\an8}Did you say she's bad at studies?

755
00:40:42,521 --> 00:40:44,104
{\an8}You sound as if you're unaware of it.

756
00:40:44,105 --> 00:40:45,854
I thought you were aware of everything.

757
00:40:45,855 --> 00:40:47,062
Teacher, please don't tell her.

758
00:40:47,063 --> 00:40:49,271
{\an8}Hasn't your husband shown you
her report card yet?

759
00:40:52,021 --> 00:40:53,313
If you aren't aware, let me tell you.

760
00:40:53,563 --> 00:40:54,605
Very talkative!

761
00:41:04,855 --> 00:41:05,771
I'm leaving, Sir.

762
00:41:24,021 --> 00:41:27,438
It's my fault
that I didn't check up on her activities.

763
00:41:28,230 --> 00:41:29,730
From now on, I'll take care of her.

764
00:41:31,021 --> 00:41:33,896
Listen, starting tomorrow,
you'll begin a new life.

765
00:41:34,355 --> 00:41:35,813
Be ready at 06:00 a.m.

766
00:41:39,771 --> 00:41:41,063
New life as in?

767
00:41:56,438 --> 00:41:58,521
Uncle, the South Indian Tournament
is coming up.

768
00:41:58,730 --> 00:42:00,146
I am determined to win it.

769
00:42:00,896 --> 00:42:04,105
I don't have the time to
keep a tab on her activities.

770
00:42:04,813 --> 00:42:06,355
I can't trust anyone, either.

771
00:42:06,771 --> 00:42:08,813
- I understand.
- That's why I asked you to come over.

772
00:42:09,105 --> 00:42:10,105
Good decision!

773
00:42:10,230 --> 00:42:11,980
I forged you into a commendable wrestler.

774
00:42:12,313 --> 00:42:15,146
It's my responsibility
to forge your daughter into a champion

775
00:42:16,188 --> 00:42:17,145
Are you rattled?

776
00:42:17,146 --> 00:42:18,771
You haven't seen my training.

777
00:42:19,563 --> 00:42:20,521
You'll watch soon!

778
00:42:21,271 --> 00:42:22,396
Hey, ready!

779
00:42:23,605 --> 00:42:24,646
<i>Poor baby!</i>

780
00:42:24,896 --> 00:42:27,063
<i>Hey, Mummy, please</i>

781
00:42:27,521 --> 00:42:29,395
<i>You know
I'm a dummy piece</i>

782
00:42:29,396 --> 00:42:30,520
- Welcome, Madam.
- My daughter,

783
00:42:30,521 --> 00:42:31,854
Mathimalar. She's in 1st grade.

784
00:42:31,855 --> 00:42:33,646
- You must coach her.
- Sure, I'll coach her.

785
00:42:34,063 --> 00:42:35,395
Does that mean I'm not her coach?

786
00:42:35,396 --> 00:42:38,855
My mother didn't call
you here to train me.

787
00:42:39,230 --> 00:42:42,355
She called you here to be my nanny.

788
00:42:42,521 --> 00:42:46,563
<i>Like ice in the sun,
I couldn't last</i>

789
00:42:47,355 --> 00:42:51,438
<i>Like jam on a bun
I disappeared without a trace</i>

790
00:42:52,105 --> 00:42:56,230
<i>Like ice in the sun,
I couldn't last</i>

791
00:42:56,980 --> 00:43:01,021
<i>Like jam on a bun
I disappeared without a trace</i>

792
00:43:01,146 --> 00:43:03,521
Mathi! Mathi!
You're late for the training.

793
00:43:04,146 --> 00:43:05,021
Hurry up!

794
00:43:06,563 --> 00:43:08,729
<i>Are you a professional tormentor?</i>

795
00:43:08,730 --> 00:43:10,895
<i>Or are you
Adolf Hitler's granddaughter?</i>

796
00:43:10,896 --> 00:43:11,771
Come on!

797
00:43:11,938 --> 00:43:13,605
NO!

798
00:43:14,563 --> 00:43:15,688
Come on! Come on, fast!

799
00:43:17,396 --> 00:43:19,812
Mom, I'm very tired.

800
00:43:19,813 --> 00:43:21,979
Can we skip training today?

801
00:43:21,980 --> 00:43:23,895
You're a great actor like your father.

802
00:43:23,896 --> 00:43:26,980
<i>Chill, Chill, Chill
Mummy Chill</i>

803
00:43:27,105 --> 00:43:32,771
<i>I Say Chill, Chill, Chill
Mummy Chill, Chill, Chill</i>

804
00:43:33,521 --> 00:43:35,730
- Hurry up! How long would you take?
- Wait! Wait!

805
00:43:36,105 --> 00:43:37,396
Watch out! It's very hot!

806
00:43:37,688 --> 00:43:39,563
Here you go!
Millet ball with onions.

807
00:43:39,855 --> 00:43:40,854
This is your morning diet!

808
00:43:40,855 --> 00:43:42,146
She's too young to be on a diet.

809
00:43:42,271 --> 00:43:45,063
No stone becomes a statue
without enduring the craft of the chisel.

810
00:43:45,230 --> 00:43:48,021
It's obvious the chisel never touched you.

811
00:43:52,105 --> 00:43:53,521
<i>Hey, Mummy please</i>

812
00:43:56,396 --> 00:43:57,271
Left!

813
00:43:57,813 --> 00:43:58,688
Right!

814
00:44:02,605 --> 00:44:04,646
I scream in pain and ask to be let go.

815
00:44:04,855 --> 00:44:06,563
But she never let go of me.

816
00:44:07,063 --> 00:44:08,563
You're bound to get hurt in wrestling.

817
00:44:08,688 --> 00:44:09,938
Why are you making a big deal out of it?

818
00:44:10,271 --> 00:44:14,230
Dad, is she really my birth mother?

819
00:44:16,355 --> 00:44:20,188
<i>Harry Potter, I'm your daughter
Enough with the torture!</i>

820
00:44:21,105 --> 00:44:23,063
<i>Why does a rabbit need boxing?</i>

821
00:44:23,438 --> 00:44:24,687
<i>Why does a lion need dancing?</i>

822
00:44:24,688 --> 00:44:26,605
Dad, my legs are really hurting a lot.

823
00:44:26,813 --> 00:44:28,563
I don't want to go for training tomorrow.

824
00:44:28,771 --> 00:44:30,938
Please don't say that.
Your mother will get angry.

825
00:44:31,855 --> 00:44:34,396
Why only her?
Even I know how to get angry.

826
00:44:34,605 --> 00:44:39,395
<i>I Say Chill, Chill, Chill
Mummy Chill, Chill, Chill</i>

827
00:44:39,396 --> 00:44:40,480
Mathi, come!

828
00:44:40,646 --> 00:44:42,105
I'm coming.
Hold your horses!

829
00:44:42,396 --> 00:44:45,105
- What happened, Teacher?
- She's down with a fever.

830
00:44:45,563 --> 00:44:46,480
- Is it?
- Yeah!

831
00:44:47,813 --> 00:44:49,730
<i>You know
I'm a dummy piece</i>

832
00:44:49,938 --> 00:44:52,188
<i>Hey, Mummy please</i>

833
00:44:52,605 --> 00:44:54,813
<i>You know
I'm a dummy piece</i>

834
00:44:56,313 --> 00:44:57,730
She was doing well in the morning.

835
00:44:58,105 --> 00:44:59,354
How come she's down with a fever now?

836
00:44:59,355 --> 00:45:00,855
She complained last night about leg pain.

837
00:45:01,105 --> 00:45:02,646
She was feeling a bit
under the weather in the morning.

838
00:45:02,938 --> 00:45:04,771
I reckon her legs weren't hurting
while dancing.

839
00:45:05,688 --> 00:45:08,480
Didn't you use to say, "When we
do something we love, it doesn't hurt."

840
00:45:10,396 --> 00:45:11,271
Oh!

841
00:45:12,021 --> 00:45:14,188
So, she likes dancing but not wrestling.

842
00:45:14,438 --> 00:45:15,313
Right?

843
00:45:15,563 --> 00:45:17,645
Whether she likes it or not
is the issue here.

844
00:45:17,646 --> 00:45:20,270
Is she learning wrestling at 6
to become a champion?

845
00:45:20,271 --> 00:45:21,605
Why are you torturing the child?

846
00:45:21,730 --> 00:45:22,646
Torturing, you say?

847
00:45:23,980 --> 00:45:25,896
No one can become a champion overnight.

848
00:45:26,063 --> 00:45:27,396
It takes years of penance to achieve.

849
00:45:28,230 --> 00:45:32,438
In China, they start training
as early as age 3 or 4.

850
00:45:32,563 --> 00:45:35,063
That's why that country tops the Olympics.

851
00:45:35,771 --> 00:45:40,354
But in India, parents like you
coddle their children…

852
00:45:40,355 --> 00:45:41,896
and that results in no medals
for our country.

853
00:45:45,355 --> 00:45:46,438
I'll call you later.

854
00:45:50,980 --> 00:45:52,480
Please bear this in mind.

855
00:45:52,688 --> 00:45:54,313
Times have changed.

856
00:45:54,605 --> 00:45:56,896
The current generation
takes everything lightly.

857
00:45:57,105 --> 00:46:00,188
However, when they encounter
a minor setback, they can't bear it.

858
00:46:00,563 --> 00:46:02,063
Willpower has gone for a toss!

859
00:46:02,521 --> 00:46:05,480
Only sports can instill discipline
and willpower in a person.

860
00:46:06,105 --> 00:46:08,271
Look, Veera, I'm repeating myself,

861
00:46:08,563 --> 00:46:11,063
enough spoiling her
with your love and pampering.

862
00:46:11,480 --> 00:46:13,271
If we let it continue,
she'll turn into you.

863
00:46:14,813 --> 00:46:17,313
I'll take care of her education
and career.

864
00:46:18,396 --> 00:46:19,646
You handle the household.

865
00:46:28,105 --> 00:46:30,438
Veera, is there a problem?

866
00:46:39,688 --> 00:46:40,980
She went overboard, Coach.

867
00:46:41,480 --> 00:46:43,188
She's accusing me of saying
our daughter will become like me.

868
00:46:43,480 --> 00:46:45,105
Why can't she turn out like me?

869
00:46:45,563 --> 00:46:46,563
{\an8}Let it go, Veera.

870
00:46:46,730 --> 00:46:48,188
{\an8}Stress is the root cause of the problem.

871
00:46:48,855 --> 00:46:49,938
{\an8}What are you saying?

872
00:46:50,938 --> 00:46:52,980
{\an8}See, It's not just Keerthi…

873
00:46:53,605 --> 00:46:56,855
Any sports champion
experiences high stress.

874
00:46:57,021 --> 00:46:59,230
However, those who can't handle the stress

875
00:46:59,480 --> 00:47:02,146
have disappeared from sports
without a trace.

876
00:47:03,271 --> 00:47:05,063
I don't understand what you're saying.

877
00:47:06,271 --> 00:47:08,813
You see, Keerthi gets angry a lot.

878
00:47:08,980 --> 00:47:10,105
You're right, Coach.

879
00:47:10,230 --> 00:47:12,521
{\an8}Stress is the main factor behind anger.

880
00:47:12,938 --> 00:47:14,188
{\an8}When you get angry, your BP shoots up.

881
00:47:14,605 --> 00:47:17,771
If BP shoots up,
it'll cause more health problems.

882
00:47:18,855 --> 00:47:21,021
If that happens,
then she must forget about wrestling.

883
00:47:21,146 --> 00:47:22,021
Oh, no!

884
00:47:22,521 --> 00:47:24,730
Of course!
Health is important for players.

885
00:47:24,896 --> 00:47:25,855
That's crucial!

886
00:47:26,813 --> 00:47:29,813
Now what do we do, Coach?
Matches are lined up for her.

887
00:47:30,063 --> 00:47:31,771
How do we bring down
her stress and anger?

888
00:47:32,313 --> 00:47:35,188
If you attend counseling,
everything will be alright.

889
00:47:35,938 --> 00:47:38,313
What's counseling?
And where do we attend it?

890
00:47:39,396 --> 00:47:41,896
There's a famous psychiatrist
named Benjamin Kutty.

891
00:47:43,855 --> 00:47:45,605
{\an8}<i>You guys consult him,
and everything will be alright.</i>

892
00:47:47,396 --> 00:47:48,521
Tell it's for the child.

893
00:47:48,730 --> 00:47:50,188
{\an8}Only then will Keerthi step out.

894
00:47:52,146 --> 00:47:53,146
You're right, Coach!

895
00:47:53,646 --> 00:47:55,313
You two, please step outside for a while.

896
00:47:56,021 --> 00:47:56,896
Why?

897
00:47:57,396 --> 00:47:58,604
I don't know what's going to happen.

898
00:47:58,605 --> 00:48:00,313
Why are you sending them outside?

899
00:48:00,438 --> 00:48:03,063
- They both need counseling.
- I will get to it.

900
00:48:03,355 --> 00:48:04,230
Please sit down.

901
00:48:09,230 --> 00:48:11,938
Do you know what Sigmund Freud quoted?

902
00:48:12,230 --> 00:48:13,605
{\an8}"Anger is a messenger."

903
00:48:13,938 --> 00:48:14,813
It means…

904
00:48:15,188 --> 00:48:17,855
Anger is nothing but a messenger.

905
00:48:18,313 --> 00:48:19,980
It's trying to convey something to us.

906
00:48:20,271 --> 00:48:22,020
Doctor, why are you explaining it to me?

907
00:48:22,021 --> 00:48:23,980
The water inside the pressure cooker…

908
00:48:24,480 --> 00:48:27,563
{\an8}keeps boiling up like this.

909
00:48:27,896 --> 00:48:29,188
{\an8}If the cooker is faulty…

910
00:48:29,980 --> 00:48:30,855
{\an8}it'll explode!

911
00:48:31,355 --> 00:48:32,771
{\an8}It bursts!

912
00:48:33,271 --> 00:48:35,312
Hey, idiot!
Have you gone mad?

913
00:48:35,313 --> 00:48:37,521
Don't you get it? I have no issues.

914
00:48:41,105 --> 00:48:43,563
Every patient who comes here
claims the same.

915
00:48:43,730 --> 00:48:45,855
Once we start the treatment
everything will be fine.

916
00:48:48,896 --> 00:48:50,480
{\an8}- Get lost!
- Come on, catch her!

917
00:48:51,021 --> 00:48:53,730
No, no, no!
Don't be silly like a kid!

918
00:48:54,021 --> 00:48:55,230
Hey, hold her properly.

919
00:48:55,688 --> 00:48:58,438
- Let go of me.
- It's nothing. It's a small injection.

920
00:49:03,438 --> 00:49:04,563
Oh, no!

921
00:49:10,230 --> 00:49:11,313
Let go of me!

922
00:49:22,938 --> 00:49:24,021
<i>What do you think of yourself?</i>

923
00:49:24,480 --> 00:49:26,771
I took you to a psychiatrist
to get your anger under control.

924
00:49:27,230 --> 00:49:28,855
There you broke his furniture
and caused chaos.

925
00:49:30,188 --> 00:49:32,521
So that's your plan
to control my anger?

926
00:49:33,438 --> 00:49:35,812
Does my concern for my daughter
look like anger to you?

927
00:49:35,813 --> 00:49:36,854
Dear, calm down.

928
00:49:36,855 --> 00:49:38,354
Didn't you lie that it's for our child?

929
00:49:38,355 --> 00:49:40,146
Our child has no issues.

930
00:49:40,855 --> 00:49:42,396
It's you who has been
short-tempered lately.

931
00:49:43,105 --> 00:49:44,605
And your anger is affecting her.

932
00:49:44,938 --> 00:49:47,896
A child should be afraid of
at least one parent.

933
00:49:48,271 --> 00:49:49,271
She's not afraid of you.

934
00:49:49,438 --> 00:49:50,895
That's why I'm being the strict parent.

935
00:49:50,896 --> 00:49:53,271
Just because you're a champion
doesn't mean you're right.

936
00:49:53,438 --> 00:49:54,855
Life is different from sports.

937
00:49:55,105 --> 00:49:57,813
To me, sports and life are the same.

938
00:49:58,271 --> 00:49:59,730
I'm saying this to benefit your career.

939
00:50:00,146 --> 00:50:01,313
Why don't you understand?

940
00:50:04,605 --> 00:50:06,271
You'll understand when you face defeat.

941
00:50:06,646 --> 00:50:08,188
You never seem to understand.

942
00:50:08,480 --> 00:50:09,563
What did you just say now?

943
00:50:11,188 --> 00:50:13,313
"I'll understand when I face defeat."

944
00:50:14,688 --> 00:50:15,855
So, you want me to lose?

945
00:50:16,813 --> 00:50:17,730
Isn't that what you want?

946
00:50:18,605 --> 00:50:19,895
That's not how I meant it.

947
00:50:19,896 --> 00:50:21,146
What did you mean then?

948
00:50:21,313 --> 00:50:22,396
Keerthi, let it go!

949
00:50:22,771 --> 00:50:24,230
- He did not mean it that way…
- He…

950
00:50:24,355 --> 00:50:26,438
- Did you not hear him?
- I did!

951
00:50:26,563 --> 00:50:28,105
"I'll understand when I face defeat."

952
00:50:28,355 --> 00:50:29,354
Do you want me to lose?

953
00:50:29,355 --> 00:50:30,812
- Answer me!
- He said it in a flow.

954
00:50:30,813 --> 00:50:32,355
That doesn't mean he could say anything.

955
00:50:33,021 --> 00:50:35,105
I think I'm going mad!

956
00:50:35,480 --> 00:50:37,396
That's why I took you to the psychiatrist.

957
00:50:43,105 --> 00:50:45,605
As it is,
being a husband to a woman isn’t easy.

958
00:50:45,980 --> 00:50:48,146
I can't even begin to imagine
if it's a sportswoman…

959
00:50:48,896 --> 00:50:51,146
Hmm… I wonder how you manage.

960
00:50:53,480 --> 00:50:55,021
Why don't we try another technique?

961
00:50:55,605 --> 00:50:59,730
There's a medicine in Ayurveda to
bring anger and stress under control.

962
00:51:00,146 --> 00:51:01,980
It doesn't matter.
She wouldn't come anywhere now.

963
00:51:02,271 --> 00:51:03,813
She doesn't have to come anywhere.

964
00:51:04,105 --> 00:51:05,021
Then how's it possible?

965
00:51:12,063 --> 00:51:14,480
{\an8}It's 3,500 rupees for the medicine.

966
00:51:14,896 --> 00:51:16,146
{\an8}How do we take this?

967
00:51:16,355 --> 00:51:17,980
{\an8}You can mix it in your food.

968
00:51:18,105 --> 00:51:19,563
{\an8}Or you could mix it in the milk.

969
00:51:21,438 --> 00:51:23,480
How does it work
when we consume this medicine?

970
00:51:24,646 --> 00:51:25,980
For that, you must study
medicine for 5 years.

971
00:51:26,271 --> 00:51:27,146
Would you like to?

972
00:51:31,521 --> 00:51:32,813
{\an8}Yes, Doctor, how are you?

973
00:51:33,271 --> 00:51:34,646
You met them at the temple, is it?

974
00:51:34,980 --> 00:51:35,937
Bye, Doctor.

975
00:51:35,938 --> 00:51:37,980
Only after visiting
other rituals would follow.

976
00:51:38,605 --> 00:51:41,146
Let me know how you got lucky.
I've been trying for 15 years.

977
00:51:57,438 --> 00:51:58,313
Aren't you eating?

978
00:51:58,521 --> 00:52:00,271
I'll eat later. You eat now.

979
00:52:00,813 --> 00:52:01,938
Here, have some egg.

980
00:52:05,313 --> 00:52:06,188
It tastes good!

981
00:52:07,188 --> 00:52:08,063
Keerthi!

982
00:52:08,813 --> 00:52:11,688
It's a good thing you started
training your daughter at an early age.

983
00:52:11,813 --> 00:52:12,770
Very good!

984
00:52:12,771 --> 00:52:14,480
But my husband is against it.

985
00:52:14,855 --> 00:52:16,605
Don't take me wrong.

986
00:52:16,938 --> 00:52:19,105
But your husband is uneducated.

987
00:52:19,480 --> 00:52:21,313
We should make him understand
the importance of it.

988
00:52:21,563 --> 00:52:22,480
Lock, lock me.

989
00:52:22,896 --> 00:52:24,063
Move quickly. Ready?

990
00:52:24,396 --> 00:52:25,271
Good! Good!

991
00:52:25,730 --> 00:52:26,938
Keep moving. Keep Moving.

992
00:52:27,063 --> 00:52:28,230
Concentrate! Concentrate!

993
00:52:34,105 --> 00:52:35,355
Isn't it unrefined cane sugar?

994
00:52:36,230 --> 00:52:37,771
Then why does it taste weird?

995
00:52:38,063 --> 00:52:39,396
It's organic.
That's how it will taste.

996
00:52:47,146 --> 00:52:48,813
Keerthi, your lunch is ready.

997
00:52:53,480 --> 00:52:54,563
What happened?

998
00:52:55,855 --> 00:52:57,563
This is our hereditary plate.

999
00:52:58,313 --> 00:52:59,521
Hereditary plate?

1000
00:53:01,271 --> 00:53:02,980
Good, good, good. Come on!

1001
00:53:05,563 --> 00:53:07,646
What happened, Keerthi?
Are you okay?

1002
00:53:13,146 --> 00:53:14,855
What are you mixing in the milk?

1003
00:53:16,480 --> 00:53:18,521
For the past two days,
my stomach has been upset.

1004
00:53:18,688 --> 00:53:21,146
Me too. I have diarrhea.

1005
00:53:21,438 --> 00:53:22,771
Let me try if this helps.

1006
00:53:26,813 --> 00:53:28,063
It's delicious!

1007
00:53:33,521 --> 00:53:35,105
Come on, lock him.
Lock him!

1008
00:53:39,271 --> 00:53:40,771
Please let me practice with girls.

1009
00:53:41,313 --> 00:53:43,646
Keerthi not only practices in the academy.

1010
00:53:43,771 --> 00:53:45,854
But at home,
she practices with her husband.

1011
00:53:45,855 --> 00:53:48,313
That's why she is able to
win matches against girls.

1012
00:53:48,896 --> 00:53:50,855
Do you wish to go to Delhi or not?

1013
00:53:52,188 --> 00:53:53,146
<i>Wait I'll get it for you.</i>

1014
00:53:57,396 --> 00:53:59,438
She's not eating.
Do we have pickles?

1015
00:53:59,980 --> 00:54:00,855
Wait a second.

1016
00:54:02,771 --> 00:54:04,855
- Where did I keep it?
- What is this?

1017
00:54:09,355 --> 00:54:11,188
It's a herbal powder.

1018
00:54:12,480 --> 00:54:13,896
Mathi often catches a cold.

1019
00:54:14,188 --> 00:54:15,354
It's for her immunity.

1020
00:54:15,355 --> 00:54:17,355
Oh! Why did you store it
in a ceramic jar?

1021
00:54:17,771 --> 00:54:19,480
If we leave it outside,
ants will spoil it.

1022
00:54:19,730 --> 00:54:20,813
- So, I stored it in there.
- Oh!

1023
00:54:21,980 --> 00:54:22,855
Here you go.

1024
00:54:25,730 --> 00:54:27,063
That was a close call.

1025
00:54:37,896 --> 00:54:39,771
Coach, the medications are working well.

1026
00:54:50,313 --> 00:54:51,188
{\an8}Let's go!

1027
00:54:53,146 --> 00:54:54,271
{\an8}Wait, I'm getting a call.

1028
00:54:55,438 --> 00:54:56,313
Who's calling?

1029
00:54:57,105 --> 00:54:57,980
Hello!

1030
00:54:58,646 --> 00:54:59,730
Yeah, it's me, Veera.

1031
00:55:00,355 --> 00:55:01,230
When?

1032
00:55:02,688 --> 00:55:03,896
Okay, I'll think about it.

1033
00:55:04,438 --> 00:55:05,438
Who was it, Dad?

1034
00:55:05,980 --> 00:55:08,396
A cooking show is taking place
in Coimbatore tomorrow.

1035
00:55:08,771 --> 00:55:10,145
If I win this competition

1036
00:55:10,146 --> 00:55:12,230
I will get the "Best Cook Award"
of this district.

1037
00:55:12,563 --> 00:55:15,770
{\an8}They chose me as a contestant
based on my Behindwoods interview.

1038
00:55:15,771 --> 00:55:16,937
{\an8}Hey, that's great!

1039
00:55:16,938 --> 00:55:18,687
{\an8}That cooking show is my favorite.

1040
00:55:18,688 --> 00:55:21,396
I cook well.
Take me as well. Please!

1041
00:55:22,105 --> 00:55:23,396
Unfortunately, even I can't make it.

1042
00:55:23,646 --> 00:55:25,146
Keerthi has a match tomorrow.

1043
00:55:25,313 --> 00:55:27,355
Will Dad appear on TV?

1044
00:55:27,480 --> 00:55:28,563
Definitely!

1045
00:55:28,771 --> 00:55:30,896
That show is every household's favorite.

1046
00:55:31,188 --> 00:55:33,229
And your Dad will appear
on every TV in every home.

1047
00:55:33,230 --> 00:55:36,104
{\an8}Why not, Dad?
You go ahead and take part in the show.

1048
00:55:36,105 --> 00:55:37,688
Hey, it's Mom's match tomorrow.

1049
00:55:37,855 --> 00:55:40,230
Mom has matches all year.

1050
00:55:40,355 --> 00:55:43,355
Moreover, it's not like it's final.

1051
00:55:43,480 --> 00:55:44,771
It's just the first round.

1052
00:55:45,230 --> 00:55:48,020
For me, you must take part in this show

1053
00:55:48,021 --> 00:55:49,521
and win a prize, Dad.

1054
00:55:50,105 --> 00:55:51,646
Why are you so enthused about it?

1055
00:55:52,105 --> 00:55:55,230
So, I could ask Deepak and Darshan,

1056
00:55:55,688 --> 00:55:59,687
"My Dad was on TV.
Were your Dads ever on TV?"

1057
00:55:59,688 --> 00:56:00,730
Everyone's got their own agenda.

1058
00:56:01,563 --> 00:56:04,313
Promise me that you'll win the prize.

1059
00:56:04,813 --> 00:56:05,688
Do it!

1060
00:56:07,480 --> 00:56:08,771
Fine, no need for a promise.

1061
00:56:09,105 --> 00:56:12,021
I will do my best
to take part in the show.

1062
00:56:12,271 --> 00:56:13,146
Okay?

1063
00:56:19,480 --> 00:56:20,646
Let's tell Mom about it.

1064
00:56:23,063 --> 00:56:24,104
Don't tell her yet.

1065
00:56:24,105 --> 00:56:25,438
If you do, she won't let you go.

1066
00:56:25,688 --> 00:56:27,688
If we don't tell her,
she'll yell at me when she sees me on TV.

1067
00:56:27,813 --> 00:56:29,355
When she yells, we'll handle it.

1068
00:56:29,521 --> 00:56:31,020
What are you guys whispering about?

1069
00:56:31,021 --> 00:56:31,896
Why aren't we leaving yet?

1070
00:56:32,230 --> 00:56:34,021
You take Keerthi and go ahead.

1071
00:56:34,146 --> 00:56:35,520
I'll bring Mathi and follow you later.

1072
00:56:35,521 --> 00:56:36,396
Okay!

1073
00:56:36,980 --> 00:56:38,479
Dear, let's go.

1074
00:56:38,480 --> 00:56:39,646
Let them go first.

1075
00:56:42,938 --> 00:56:44,980
- She left! Let's go now.
- Come on, let's go!

1076
00:56:45,480 --> 00:56:46,355
Keerthi!

1077
00:56:46,521 --> 00:56:48,980
We're getting ready to watch your match.

1078
00:56:49,105 --> 00:56:50,438
You must rock it today.

1079
00:56:50,563 --> 00:56:51,645
Thanks, Auntie.

1080
00:56:51,646 --> 00:56:53,105
- All the best, Keerthi!
- Bye!

1081
00:56:56,896 --> 00:56:57,979
<i>Hi, Hello, Vanakkam!</i>

1082
00:56:57,980 --> 00:57:01,605
You're watching Your Kovai Kitchen.
Taste of Coimbatore.

1083
00:57:03,605 --> 00:57:04,729
- Welcome, Sir.
- Where do I leave my phone?

1084
00:57:04,730 --> 00:57:05,938
- Leave it here.
- Over here?

1085
00:57:07,563 --> 00:57:08,438
Let's go!

1086
00:57:09,188 --> 00:57:10,855
And the final contestant for the day…

1087
00:57:11,063 --> 00:57:12,437
Let's welcome, Veera

1088
00:57:12,438 --> 00:57:14,271
and Meenu!

1089
00:57:17,188 --> 00:57:20,645
Not bad, you came to our show
with your wife and kid.

1090
00:57:20,646 --> 00:57:21,937
Oh, she's not my wife.

1091
00:57:21,938 --> 00:57:23,688
- She's my daughter's class teacher.
- Oh!

1092
00:57:23,980 --> 00:57:26,105
Why did you bring your
daughter's teacher to stir gravy?

1093
00:57:26,396 --> 00:57:27,730
She's here for moral support.

1094
00:57:28,063 --> 00:57:29,354
They have a good understanding.

1095
00:57:29,355 --> 00:57:30,937
But it may cause a
misunderstanding in their family.

1096
00:57:30,938 --> 00:57:35,479
<i>South Indian Wrestling Tournament
is about to begin.</i>

1097
00:57:35,480 --> 00:57:41,020
<i>First to fight are Regina in red tracks
and Keerthi in Blue tracks.</i>

1098
00:57:41,021 --> 00:57:42,021
{\an8}Come on, start!

1099
00:57:42,146 --> 00:57:45,562
{\an8}<i>The umpire has blown the whistle
to kick start the fight.</i>

1100
00:57:45,563 --> 00:57:47,479
- Come on, Keerthi.
<i>- Both are putting up an equal fight.</i>

1101
00:57:47,480 --> 00:57:50,062
- Keerthi, come on!
<i>- Which fighter will score the first point?</i>

1102
00:57:50,063 --> 00:57:51,813
Don't let go of the grip.
Slam her!

1103
00:57:53,355 --> 00:57:54,562
That's about it!

1104
00:57:54,563 --> 00:57:58,188
<i>Keerthi is leading by 4 points
after using the back throw technique.</i>

1105
00:57:58,521 --> 00:58:01,813
<i>Keerthi continues to show her prowess.</i>

1106
00:58:02,105 --> 00:58:04,480
<i>She's leading with 4 points.</i>

1107
00:58:04,896 --> 00:58:06,896
Your time starts now!

1108
00:58:08,855 --> 00:58:10,312
Hey, everyone, make sure
you're with your own wives.

1109
00:58:10,313 --> 00:58:12,105
Here you go.
The vegetables are out there.

1110
00:58:12,396 --> 00:58:13,313
Here, wear it.

1111
00:58:22,021 --> 00:58:24,479
{\an8}<i>-Both are attacking each other.</i>
- Hold her down.

1112
00:58:24,480 --> 00:58:26,479
<i>Regina is going for a flip throw.</i>

1113
00:58:26,480 --> 00:58:30,146
<i>Regina did a flip throw
and scored 4 points, tying the score.</i>

1114
00:58:30,521 --> 00:58:31,563
Nice one!

1115
00:58:33,063 --> 00:58:37,813
<i>Keerthi and Regina are at 4 point each.</i>

1116
00:58:38,063 --> 00:58:39,771
<i>Red, 4. Blue, 4</i>

1117
00:58:41,813 --> 00:58:43,563
<i>- Keerthi is trying to attack.</i>
- Come on!

1118
00:58:43,688 --> 00:58:47,146
- Come on!
<i>- Regina has locked Keerthi from behind.</i>

1119
00:58:47,271 --> 00:58:48,980
<i>Now Keerthi makes her counter move…</i>

1120
00:58:49,896 --> 00:58:53,563
<i>- Keerthi is now leading…</i>
- That was an amazing slam!

1121
00:59:01,146 --> 00:59:04,645
<i>Not sure why Keerthi is staggering.</i>

1122
00:59:04,646 --> 00:59:07,605
<i>Only 1 minutes and 30 seconds are left.</i>

1123
00:59:07,771 --> 00:59:10,520
<i>Right now Keerthi is at 8 points.</i>

1124
00:59:10,521 --> 00:59:13,230
<i>And Regina is at 4 points.</i>

1125
00:59:16,813 --> 00:59:18,730
Wow! It smells yummy!

1126
00:59:18,980 --> 00:59:20,395
Yes, I ground it in Ammi (grinder).

1127
00:59:20,396 --> 00:59:22,855
- She meant yummy, not Ammi.
- Dad, hurry up.

1128
00:59:23,563 --> 00:59:26,605
You have the last 30 minutes left
to finish cooking.

1129
00:59:26,855 --> 00:59:27,812
Hurry up, Teacher.

1130
00:59:27,813 --> 00:59:28,688
Oh, no!

1131
00:59:29,188 --> 00:59:30,146
Hey, hey!

1132
00:59:30,355 --> 00:59:31,230
Careful!

1133
00:59:31,563 --> 00:59:32,438
Dear!

1134
00:59:33,938 --> 00:59:34,938
Attack her!

1135
00:59:36,188 --> 00:59:37,063
Attack!

1136
00:59:37,230 --> 00:59:39,980
<i>Keerthi's uncle is encouraging her.</i>

1137
00:59:40,438 --> 00:59:41,688
Don't lose your grip.

1138
00:59:45,396 --> 00:59:49,271
<i>Regina mustering up her strength,
with front lock and threw her away.</i>

1139
00:59:49,396 --> 00:59:51,187
<i>With this Regina has gained 4 points.</i>

1140
00:59:51,188 --> 00:59:57,063
<i>Once again the points are equal at 8 each.</i>

1141
00:59:57,605 --> 01:00:00,188
<i>Regina once again does the Dhobi Throw.</i>

1142
01:00:00,355 --> 01:00:03,020
<i>Regina scores another 4 points,
making her score 12 now.</i>

1143
01:00:03,021 --> 01:00:04,605
Get up! Get up!

1144
01:00:05,105 --> 01:00:06,979
<i>Regina is in the lead now.</i>

1145
01:00:06,980 --> 01:00:07,896
Oh, no!

1146
01:00:08,980 --> 01:00:09,855
Keerthi!

1147
01:00:11,396 --> 01:00:12,271
Get up!

1148
01:00:12,396 --> 01:00:16,271
<i>Will the undefeated champion
Keerthi recover?</i>

1149
01:00:21,896 --> 01:00:25,230
<i>Time has ended
and the umpire has blown the whistle.</i>

1150
01:00:25,396 --> 01:00:29,895
<i>Based on the points Regina has been
declared as the winner of this match.</i>

1151
01:00:29,896 --> 01:00:30,980
Yes!

1152
01:00:44,605 --> 01:00:45,730
Oh, no!

1153
01:00:59,896 --> 01:01:00,855
Don't cry!

1154
01:01:01,146 --> 01:01:02,480
We'll make it up in the next tournament.

1155
01:01:03,313 --> 01:01:04,521
What happened, Keerthi?

1156
01:01:04,730 --> 01:01:05,979
This is not your game!

1157
01:01:05,980 --> 01:01:07,146
It's very disappointing.

1158
01:01:07,313 --> 01:01:08,313
I don't understand either.

1159
01:01:08,521 --> 01:01:09,896
She's unlikely to lose like this.

1160
01:01:10,105 --> 01:01:11,105
Let it go, dear.

1161
01:01:11,730 --> 01:01:12,646
- Coach!
- Yeah!

1162
01:01:18,146 --> 01:01:20,313
No! There's been a mistake.

1163
01:01:20,605 --> 01:01:21,688
This report does not belong to Keerthi.

1164
01:01:21,938 --> 01:01:23,396
Coach, this is Keerthi's report.

1165
01:01:23,730 --> 01:01:24,771
Why? Why happened?

1166
01:01:26,438 --> 01:01:28,313
Players usually undergo a dope test.

1167
01:01:28,563 --> 01:01:31,271
Keerthi's report states
there were steroids in her bloodstream.

1168
01:01:36,271 --> 01:01:40,021
Keerthi, did you take any painkillers
over the past couple of days?

1169
01:01:43,021 --> 01:01:46,437
Did you make any changes
to your food supplements?

1170
01:01:46,438 --> 01:01:49,187
No, Sir.
She follows a home-cooked diet.

1171
01:01:49,188 --> 01:01:51,438
Does that mean there were any changes
made in the home-cooked diet?

1172
01:01:52,146 --> 01:01:53,980
Son-in-law is the one who cooks at home.

1173
01:01:54,688 --> 01:01:55,895
He…

1174
01:01:55,896 --> 01:01:57,730
Where's Veera?
How come he's not here?

1175
01:01:59,896 --> 01:02:00,771
Wait!

1176
01:02:09,563 --> 01:02:11,355
It's ringing, but he's not answering.

1177
01:02:11,896 --> 01:02:13,146
I wonder where he went.

1178
01:02:22,021 --> 01:02:22,896
What are you looking for?

1179
01:02:27,396 --> 01:02:28,771
Tell me. I'll find it for you.

1180
01:02:29,563 --> 01:02:30,480
Keerthi!

1181
01:02:38,771 --> 01:02:40,063
Why are there so many packets?

1182
01:02:45,230 --> 01:02:46,188
<i>What's this?</i>

1183
01:02:47,438 --> 01:02:48,355
<i>Herbal powder.</i>

1184
01:02:55,105 --> 01:02:56,437
Ask them to test this thing.

1185
01:02:56,438 --> 01:02:57,730
I would like to know what's in it.

1186
01:03:00,980 --> 01:03:02,105
<i>Your time is up!</i>

1187
01:03:18,438 --> 01:03:19,605
Here, take a look at it.

1188
01:03:20,063 --> 01:03:20,938
Look!

1189
01:03:23,896 --> 01:03:25,438
Your suspicion was right.

1190
01:03:26,021 --> 01:03:27,813
Steroids has been mixed in that powder.

1191
01:03:29,605 --> 01:03:30,646
What happened, Keerthi?

1192
01:03:34,438 --> 01:03:35,896
The report says it's positive.

1193
01:03:43,730 --> 01:03:44,980
<i>It tastes weird.</i>

1194
01:03:45,105 --> 01:03:46,271
<i>It's organic.
It's supposed to taste like it.</i>

1195
01:03:47,063 --> 01:03:48,355
I can't believe Veera could do this.

1196
01:03:48,480 --> 01:03:50,771
He's the first person to wish
for Keerthi's victory.

1197
01:03:51,188 --> 01:03:52,771
How could you all suspect him?

1198
01:03:52,896 --> 01:03:54,730
Hey, shut up! Take a look at this.

1199
01:03:55,646 --> 01:03:57,229
I had many videos,
so I missed out on this.

1200
01:03:57,230 --> 01:03:58,771
{\an8}Look at him mixing meds in food.

1201
01:04:03,063 --> 01:04:04,813
What more proof do we need?

1202
01:04:06,188 --> 01:04:08,563
He'd be the first to show up
at Keerthi's matches.

1203
01:04:08,688 --> 01:04:09,688
But he did not come today.

1204
01:04:10,188 --> 01:04:11,646
Also, he's not answering his phone.

1205
01:04:12,855 --> 01:04:14,688
<i>Your father is indeed a house husband.</i>

1206
01:04:15,021 --> 01:04:16,855
<i>If it continues she'll end up like you.</i>

1207
01:04:19,813 --> 01:04:21,563
<i>You'll understand when you face defeat.</i>

1208
01:04:23,646 --> 01:04:27,730
He could not face you.
So, he went into hiding.

1209
01:04:28,313 --> 01:04:29,270
- I called him many times.
- Sir!

1210
01:04:29,271 --> 01:04:30,146
He didn't answer.

1211
01:04:30,271 --> 01:04:32,479
Sir, he did not disappear.
Look over here.

1212
01:04:32,480 --> 01:04:33,438
<i>Here, taste this as well.</i>

1213
01:04:34,230 --> 01:04:36,688
- Please try this salad.
- I don't eat vegetarian food today.

1214
01:04:39,855 --> 01:04:40,854
What are these dishes called?

1215
01:04:40,855 --> 01:04:43,854
Raw Tamarind Rasam,
Fish fry, parboiled red rice

1216
01:04:43,855 --> 01:04:46,104
Millet ball, Chintamani chicken gravy

1217
01:04:46,105 --> 01:04:47,563
Coconut cakes and pickled chicken.

1218
01:04:50,313 --> 01:04:53,605
In today's competition,
everyone did their best.

1219
01:04:53,813 --> 01:04:55,355
The competition was tough.

1220
01:04:55,521 --> 01:04:58,438
But in a competition,
there's only one winner.

1221
01:04:58,688 --> 01:05:02,313
Veera and Meenu
are the title winners today.

1222
01:05:03,105 --> 01:05:05,480
Yayy!

1223
01:05:08,730 --> 01:05:10,355
Oh, no!

1224
01:05:11,980 --> 01:05:12,855
Yes!

1225
01:05:15,938 --> 01:05:18,480
<i>Veera, how do you manage
to cook such tasty dishes?</i>

1226
01:05:18,646 --> 01:05:20,688
My wife Keerthi is my inspiration to cook.

1227
01:05:21,230 --> 01:05:23,646
I want my wife to scale heights in sports.

1228
01:05:23,855 --> 01:05:26,605
So I sent her to the ground
and took charge of the kitchen.

1229
01:05:26,813 --> 01:05:29,521
<i>I researched nutritious food
and started cooking for her.</i>

1230
01:05:29,688 --> 01:05:30,771
<i>No matter what I cook</i>

1231
01:05:30,938 --> 01:05:32,521
<i>she eats it without asking any questions.</i>

1232
01:05:33,771 --> 01:05:35,063
She trusts me a lot.

1233
01:05:35,271 --> 01:05:37,355
- But you broke her trust.
<i>- To be blessed with a husband like Veera</i>

1234
01:05:37,605 --> 01:05:38,895
<i>his wife is a lucky person.</i>

1235
01:05:38,896 --> 01:05:39,979
<i>All the best, Veera!</i>

1236
01:05:39,980 --> 01:05:41,355
<i>- You're the real winner.</i>
- Keerthi!

1237
01:05:42,105 --> 01:05:43,271
Thank you! Thank you!

1238
01:06:04,313 --> 01:06:06,563
Keerthi, I won a title
in the cooking show.

1239
01:06:07,271 --> 01:06:08,563
They gave me the "Best Cook" award.

1240
01:06:12,230 --> 01:06:13,938
After what you did,
how dare you show off your award?

1241
01:06:15,480 --> 01:06:16,730
- What are you looking at?
- What's happening?

1242
01:06:16,938 --> 01:06:18,605
What happened? What did I do?

1243
01:06:18,813 --> 01:06:20,355
You don't know what you did?

1244
01:06:21,021 --> 01:06:22,021
Hand it to me.

1245
01:06:23,521 --> 01:06:24,521
See what you've done.

1246
01:06:24,938 --> 01:06:28,062
<i>At the very first round
of the South India Wrestling Tournament</i>

1247
01:06:28,063 --> 01:06:30,438
<i>wrestler Keerthi lost to wrestler Regina.</i>

1248
01:06:30,730 --> 01:06:31,937
How did you lose?

1249
01:06:31,938 --> 01:06:34,020
<i>A blood test taken
after the match reported</i>

1250
01:06:34,021 --> 01:06:36,562
<i>that Keerthi had taken
a performance drug.</i>

1251
01:06:36,563 --> 01:06:38,980
<i>This news has rattled the world of sports.</i>

1252
01:06:40,396 --> 01:06:41,396
Performance drug?

1253
01:06:46,771 --> 01:06:50,771
<i>Wrestler Keerthi is banned for a year
for using a performance drug.</i>

1254
01:06:52,063 --> 01:06:53,688
<i>The Sports Federation has issued an order.</i>

1255
01:06:59,688 --> 01:07:01,230
Keerthi, what does it mean?

1256
01:07:03,355 --> 01:07:04,730
Keerthi!

1257
01:07:05,313 --> 01:07:06,313
Damn you!

1258
01:07:11,938 --> 01:07:13,230
Isn't this what you expected?

1259
01:07:14,605 --> 01:07:17,396
When you said
only defeat will teach me a lesson…

1260
01:07:17,938 --> 01:07:20,146
I thought you said it in a fit of anger.

1261
01:07:21,730 --> 01:07:26,230
But I never expected you to do this to me.

1262
01:07:26,521 --> 01:07:27,645
I did not, Keerthi.

1263
01:07:27,646 --> 01:07:28,688
In the end,

1264
01:07:29,271 --> 01:07:32,480
you still are holding on to that male ego.

1265
01:07:33,688 --> 01:07:37,146
Your male ego
has ruined my career for good.

1266
01:07:38,646 --> 01:07:40,480
How do I explain it to you?

1267
01:07:42,188 --> 01:07:43,229
Keethy, I did not…

1268
01:07:43,230 --> 01:07:44,896
Who would in this world…

1269
01:07:46,146 --> 01:07:48,896
would mix steroids in his wife's food?

1270
01:07:49,021 --> 01:07:50,021
Steroid?

1271
01:07:51,021 --> 01:07:53,271
I don't want to see you anymore.

1272
01:07:54,896 --> 01:07:56,604
- Go away!
- Keerthi, hear me out.

1273
01:07:56,605 --> 01:07:58,313
I didn't know how steroids got mixed
into that medicine.

1274
01:07:58,521 --> 01:08:00,021
Leave my daughter and me alone.

1275
01:08:01,105 --> 01:08:01,980
Sweetie!

1276
01:08:02,146 --> 01:08:04,021
Keerthi! Keerthi!

1277
01:08:16,355 --> 01:08:18,646
Keerthi, I don't know
what really happened.

1278
01:08:18,813 --> 01:08:20,438
I didn't do it on purpose.

1279
01:08:20,855 --> 01:08:21,730
Keerthi!

1280
01:09:09,980 --> 01:09:12,605
I thought Veera was a good husband.
How could he do this to you?

1281
01:09:12,938 --> 01:09:14,438
When it comes to a husband,
there is no good or bad.

1282
01:09:14,605 --> 01:09:15,813
A husband is always a bad person.

1283
01:09:16,230 --> 01:09:18,521
He always put up an act
encouraging the wife

1284
01:09:18,688 --> 01:09:20,563
and stabbed her in the back
at her crucial moment in life.

1285
01:09:21,563 --> 01:09:22,563
<i>Well done, Son!</i>

1286
01:09:23,105 --> 01:09:25,480
{\an8}Until now, I misunderstood you.

1287
01:09:25,688 --> 01:09:28,230
That you've become henpecked
like the rest of the men.

1288
01:09:28,646 --> 01:09:29,646
But you struck her at the right time.

1289
01:09:29,855 --> 01:09:31,521
I'm proud of you!

1290
01:09:32,063 --> 01:09:33,063
You got it wrong, Uncle.

1291
01:09:33,271 --> 01:09:34,687
I did not do it on purpose.

1292
01:09:34,688 --> 01:09:37,563
Even if you did it on purpose,
there's nothing wrong with it.

1293
01:09:37,896 --> 01:09:40,646
Women like her deserve this behavior.
Truly deserve it.

1294
01:09:41,730 --> 01:09:43,855
We had a grandfather, Kanniappan.

1295
01:09:43,980 --> 01:09:46,230
He used to work in Burma.
You may have heard about him.

1296
01:09:46,355 --> 01:09:47,771
- I have!
- Yeah!

1297
01:09:47,896 --> 01:09:49,480
How do you think his wife died?

1298
01:09:50,188 --> 01:09:53,896
The Karupatti Halwa he brought
every time he returned from Burma…

1299
01:09:54,021 --> 01:09:58,771
used it as a spread on the bread
laced with poison and killed her.

1300
01:10:01,771 --> 01:10:02,896
To be honest.

1301
01:10:03,188 --> 01:10:07,938
I'm just afraid of the Police; if not,
I would've poisoned my wife long ago.

1302
01:10:08,521 --> 01:10:09,521
But you did it!

1303
01:10:09,938 --> 01:10:11,896
You proved you're that
from Kanniappan's bloodline.

1304
01:10:12,813 --> 01:10:13,730
I appreciate it!

1305
01:10:14,438 --> 01:10:16,396
A husband may endure anything.

1306
01:10:16,605 --> 01:10:20,480
But he will never endure
his wife surpassing him in life.

1307
01:10:20,646 --> 01:10:22,270
It's a different case with the wives.

1308
01:10:22,271 --> 01:10:27,605
They always wish their husbands would earn
more than other men and achieve success.

1309
01:10:27,730 --> 01:10:30,355
Because wives are always the martyrs.

1310
01:10:31,605 --> 01:10:33,646
Who is a martyr?
Who the hell is a martyr?

1311
01:10:34,021 --> 01:10:36,146
The men who toil through
blood and sweat every day,

1312
01:10:36,271 --> 01:10:37,813
facing humiliation from
complete strangers,

1313
01:10:37,980 --> 01:10:40,395
and still carrying on
to provide for their families

1314
01:10:40,396 --> 01:10:43,729
this is not the story of one man,
but of millions of men.

1315
01:10:43,730 --> 01:10:44,813
Do you call these men martyrs?

1316
01:10:45,063 --> 01:10:48,312
Sitting idle at home,
eating three square meals a day,

1317
01:10:48,313 --> 01:10:51,270
binge-watching serials,
liking random Instagram posts,

1318
01:10:51,271 --> 01:10:52,937
and growing as stout as a stone mortar.

1319
01:10:52,938 --> 01:10:53,896
Or do you call these women martyrs?

1320
01:10:54,396 --> 01:10:57,896
My husband said taking care
of the kids is a mother's job.

1321
01:10:58,146 --> 01:11:00,604
Really?
Then why do I need you in this house?

1322
01:11:00,605 --> 01:11:02,479
I asked him to leave and divorced him.

1323
01:11:02,480 --> 01:11:03,771
- Divorce?
- Of course!

1324
01:11:03,938 --> 01:11:07,730
In this world,
if a dog is praised for its gratitude,

1325
01:11:08,146 --> 01:11:10,271
then a husband is branded as ungrateful.

1326
01:11:10,396 --> 01:11:12,021
- Do you agree?
- Yes!

1327
01:11:12,271 --> 01:11:14,396
Be strong. We're with you.

1328
01:11:14,730 --> 01:11:18,020
Your husband will claim he gave
you the medicine to calm your temper.

1329
01:11:18,021 --> 01:11:19,188
Don't even let him near you.

1330
01:11:19,563 --> 01:11:22,563
Sattam, that Ayurvedic doctor gave
her medicine to control her temper.

1331
01:11:22,813 --> 01:11:25,313
I have never seen a fool worse than you.

1332
01:11:25,480 --> 01:11:26,938
- Why would you say that?
- What do you expect?

1333
01:11:27,146 --> 01:11:29,646
You believed that a medicine
could control a wife's temper.

1334
01:11:29,855 --> 01:11:30,938
How do I even begin to explain?

1335
01:11:31,896 --> 01:11:34,896
They may even find a cure
for AIDS and cancer in the future.

1336
01:11:35,063 --> 01:11:37,938
Humanity can split atoms
and explore galaxies,

1337
01:11:38,063 --> 01:11:39,438
but a wife's anger remains unsolved.

1338
01:11:39,730 --> 01:11:41,230
If they ever achieve a breakthrough,

1339
01:11:41,355 --> 01:11:43,770
humanity might go extinct
like the dinosaurs.

1340
01:11:43,771 --> 01:11:46,855
For the first time since you became
a lawyer, you spoke like a true one.

1341
01:11:47,271 --> 01:11:48,188
Have a drink!

1342
01:11:48,896 --> 01:11:50,396
- Cheers!
- Cheers, Brother!

1343
01:11:51,105 --> 01:11:52,438
Oh, God, these men!

1344
01:12:00,188 --> 01:12:01,896
Veera! Veera!

1345
01:12:08,688 --> 01:12:10,188
Freshen up. Let's eat.

1346
01:12:22,105 --> 01:12:23,813
I don't know what happened, Auntie.

1347
01:12:24,855 --> 01:12:27,938
That doesn't mean
you leave your wife and kid behind.

1348
01:12:30,605 --> 01:12:32,688
Do you know what she accused me of?

1349
01:12:33,896 --> 01:12:36,396
I'm-- I'm still holding on to male ego.

1350
01:12:37,813 --> 01:12:39,521
And that I destroyed her career.

1351
01:12:40,563 --> 01:12:41,855
Do you know how it hurt me?

1352
01:12:42,521 --> 01:12:44,855
You did it for her well-being,
but it backfired.

1353
01:12:45,855 --> 01:12:47,855
The time and circumstances
are against you.

1354
01:12:48,980 --> 01:12:50,730
You claim that you're unaware
of what happened.

1355
01:12:50,980 --> 01:12:52,480
Then, how do you expect
Keerthi to understand?

1356
01:12:53,646 --> 01:12:55,355
Go, meet her and speak to her.

1357
01:12:56,146 --> 01:12:57,146
Console her!

1358
01:13:02,855 --> 01:13:04,230
You carry on, I'll wait here.

1359
01:13:17,396 --> 01:13:19,230
In a day, everything went topsy-turvy.

1360
01:13:19,563 --> 01:13:21,605
You've become the common enemy
of women everywhere.

1361
01:13:22,730 --> 01:13:25,355
In the game of Snakes and Ladders,
the ladder takes you up.

1362
01:13:25,688 --> 01:13:28,230
However, the snake
will be sitting right next to it.

1363
01:13:28,396 --> 01:13:29,730
Stopping yapping like an idiot.

1364
01:13:29,896 --> 01:13:31,188
- Where are my wife and kid?
- Idiot?

1365
01:13:31,355 --> 01:13:32,312
Why is the house locked?

1366
01:13:32,313 --> 01:13:34,146
She went to her mother's house
in Palakkad.

1367
01:13:34,521 --> 01:13:36,562
- Why don't you mind your business?
- He asked.

1368
01:13:36,563 --> 01:13:37,854
- Why are you acting like a fool?
- Fool?

1369
01:13:37,855 --> 01:13:40,854
- Why are you yelling at me?
- Dare you I'd leave to my mother's place.

1370
01:13:40,855 --> 01:13:42,105
- Won't I get angry?
- Get inside the house.

1371
01:13:43,938 --> 01:13:46,770
If you go over there now,
it'll only fuel more anger.

1372
01:13:46,771 --> 01:13:47,730
Let's not go, Veera.

1373
01:13:49,896 --> 01:13:51,187
- One more bit.
- Enough!

1374
01:13:51,188 --> 01:13:54,313
I thought men from Tamil Nadu
are good and I got her married.

1375
01:13:54,563 --> 01:13:56,271
But he ruined everything.

1376
01:13:56,688 --> 01:13:58,188
What's happening, God?

1377
01:13:58,480 --> 01:14:00,188
- Shut up old woman.
- Hey!

1378
01:14:00,646 --> 01:14:02,521
You don't know anything about my father.

1379
01:14:02,730 --> 01:14:04,980
You shouldn't disrespect elders.
Please eat.

1380
01:14:06,355 --> 01:14:07,230
Dad!

1381
01:14:45,021 --> 01:14:46,980
Keerthi… Keerthi!

1382
01:14:50,313 --> 01:14:51,188
Keerthi.

1383
01:14:52,730 --> 01:14:53,979
Keerthi, wait a minute.

1384
01:14:53,980 --> 01:14:56,188
You already ruined it all.
Why are you here now?

1385
01:14:56,605 --> 01:14:57,855
I did not ruin anything, Granny.

1386
01:14:58,271 --> 01:15:00,188
It was unintentional.

1387
01:15:00,605 --> 01:15:02,562
Why haven't you invited him
into the house?

1388
01:15:02,563 --> 01:15:04,604
- Please come in, son-in-law.
- Brother, what are you doing?

1389
01:15:04,605 --> 01:15:05,937
Hey, stop right there!

1390
01:15:05,938 --> 01:15:07,312
Don't you have any shame?

1391
01:15:07,313 --> 01:15:09,479
Are you planning to host a feast for him?

1392
01:15:09,480 --> 01:15:11,895
- Hey, stop talking nonsense!
- Brother, you shut up!

1393
01:15:11,896 --> 01:15:16,354
You ought to have him arrested
for what he did to Keerthi.

1394
01:15:16,355 --> 01:15:17,437
Have him arrested?!

1395
01:15:17,438 --> 01:15:19,479
- I dare you to file a complaint!
- Calm down.

1396
01:15:19,480 --> 01:15:21,187
Did you bring a lawyer to threaten us?

1397
01:15:21,188 --> 01:15:22,645
I will bring a lawyer too.

1398
01:15:22,646 --> 01:15:24,562
- Listen--
- He did not come here as a lawyer.

1399
01:15:24,563 --> 01:15:25,771
He's here as my friend.

1400
01:15:25,980 --> 01:15:28,605
Sure, he's your friend!
But isn't he also a lawyer?

1401
01:15:28,730 --> 01:15:30,479
He's always roaming around
wearing a uniform.

1402
01:15:30,480 --> 01:15:32,145
- Hey, don't you dare disrespect me!
- Damn you!

1403
01:15:32,146 --> 01:15:34,187
- What are you…
- Oh, so you want me to respect you?!

1404
01:15:34,188 --> 01:15:36,479
- That's how I'll speak to you!
- Please hear me out.

1405
01:15:36,480 --> 01:15:37,937
- Uncle, calm down.
- I'll disrespect you even more!

1406
01:15:37,938 --> 01:15:39,270
If you are real men…

1407
01:15:39,271 --> 01:15:41,312
Keerthi, what's wrong with you?

1408
01:15:41,313 --> 01:15:43,980
Why don't you stop them?
There's quite a scene outside!

1409
01:15:44,313 --> 01:15:46,020
- Hey, watch your mouth!
- Uncle, please don't!

1410
01:15:46,021 --> 01:15:47,062
Uncle, please calm down.

1411
01:15:47,063 --> 01:15:49,271
- Please hear me out.
- Get out of here!

1412
01:15:55,896 --> 01:15:56,813
Oh, God!

1413
01:15:57,480 --> 01:15:58,687
- Uncle--
- Hey!

1414
01:15:58,688 --> 01:16:01,187
Son-in-law, why did you slap him?

1415
01:16:01,188 --> 01:16:02,480
I didn't slap him on purpose.

1416
01:16:03,105 --> 01:16:04,313
I slapped him by mistake.

1417
01:16:04,938 --> 01:16:07,270
"I mixed the medicine by mistake.
I slapped him by mistake."

1418
01:16:07,271 --> 01:16:08,730
How many more mistakes
will you make unintentionally?

1419
01:16:09,146 --> 01:16:11,146
I came here seeking peace
for a couple of days.

1420
01:16:11,480 --> 01:16:12,896
But you couldn't leave me alone!

1421
01:16:13,313 --> 01:16:15,813
Keerthi, please hear me out once--

1422
01:16:17,771 --> 01:16:19,605
I've had enough of trusting you.

1423
01:16:19,855 --> 01:16:21,479
I'm not ready to trust you anymore.

1424
01:16:21,480 --> 01:16:22,980
Don't create any trouble.
Get out of here.

1425
01:16:59,813 --> 01:17:03,396
<i>The number you have dialed
is presently not reachable.</i>

1426
01:17:08,271 --> 01:17:09,271
Did you go to the clinic?

1427
01:17:09,438 --> 01:17:11,395
Yeah, there's been a mix-up
with the medicines.

1428
01:17:11,396 --> 01:17:14,230
Only if the Doctor explains it to her
will Keerthi believe me.

1429
01:17:14,813 --> 01:17:17,105
The clinic is locked,
and the doctor is missing too.

1430
01:17:17,646 --> 01:17:20,355
Since Keerthi's case
became sensational news,

1431
01:17:20,521 --> 01:17:23,813
I think the doctor went underground
to avoid a police case.

1432
01:17:24,313 --> 01:17:26,105
He's a very famous Doctor in that area.

1433
01:17:26,480 --> 01:17:29,605
Even I'm confused about
what went wrong with the medicines.

1434
01:17:30,730 --> 01:17:33,146
Coach, please explain the confusion
about the medicines to Keerthi.

1435
01:17:33,355 --> 01:17:34,771
She would believe you.

1436
01:17:36,896 --> 01:17:37,771
Sure, Veera!

1437
01:17:38,396 --> 01:17:40,730
I'll speak to Keerthi.
Please go home.

1438
01:17:41,771 --> 01:17:42,855
Okay, Coach.

1439
01:17:47,313 --> 01:17:48,730
Who gave you permission to go to Palakkad?

1440
01:17:49,188 --> 01:17:53,063
You've gone from begging your wife
to begging her entire family.

1441
01:17:53,480 --> 01:17:56,312
If we're the ones in the wrong,
we have to be submissive, Uncle.

1442
01:17:56,313 --> 01:17:57,563
You've gone mad!

1443
01:17:58,105 --> 01:18:00,021
Husbands should be dominant!

1444
01:18:00,230 --> 01:18:01,938
If we keep being submissive

1445
01:18:02,063 --> 01:18:05,605
the wives will bury the husbands
deep underground.

1446
01:18:06,146 --> 01:18:08,062
How do you suggest we fix this?

1447
01:18:08,063 --> 01:18:09,855
When a fight breaks out
between a husband and a wife

1448
01:18:10,063 --> 01:18:12,395
staying silent
will eventually solve the problem.

1449
01:18:12,396 --> 01:18:13,354
There's nothing we could do.

1450
01:18:13,355 --> 01:18:14,729
Only in our country

1451
01:18:14,730 --> 01:18:17,480
does the husband-and-wife quarrel
continue like local riots.

1452
01:18:17,980 --> 01:18:20,896
Why do husband and wife
often end up fighting?

1453
01:18:21,188 --> 01:18:22,813
You're very innocent.

1454
01:18:23,188 --> 01:18:24,563
Isn't it obvious?

1455
01:18:24,980 --> 01:18:26,855
- Which is our country?
- India.

1456
01:18:27,063 --> 01:18:30,188
- Did India and Germany ever fight?
- No!

1457
01:18:30,313 --> 01:18:32,813
Did India and Australia ever fight?

1458
01:18:33,521 --> 01:18:35,480
- No!
- Who do we fight with?

1459
01:18:35,605 --> 01:18:36,979
With Pakistan and China.

1460
01:18:36,980 --> 01:18:38,188
Where are they located?

1461
01:18:38,396 --> 01:18:40,563
- They're our neighboring countries.
- That's the issue!

1462
01:18:41,646 --> 01:18:43,730
When we're closer, it's always an issue.

1463
01:18:43,938 --> 01:18:47,480
It does not necessarily have to be
India-Pakistan or India-China.

1464
01:18:47,646 --> 01:18:49,105
It's enough if you're a husband and wife.

1465
01:18:49,438 --> 01:18:51,479
- Brother, did you hear the news?
- What news?

1466
01:18:51,480 --> 01:18:53,520
In the upcoming elections, the Panchayat
President seat is reserved for women.

1467
01:18:53,521 --> 01:18:54,896
Who gave them the right to do it?

1468
01:18:55,021 --> 01:18:56,520
I'm the only President of this Panchayat.

1469
01:18:56,521 --> 01:18:57,480
I will contest in the elections.

1470
01:18:57,646 --> 01:18:59,771
I challenge the election commission.

1471
01:18:59,896 --> 01:19:01,146
Stop talking like an idiot.

1472
01:19:01,355 --> 01:19:02,771
Only ladies can contest
in the ladies' constituency.

1473
01:19:02,938 --> 01:19:04,521
Do you mean
that I have become a woman?

1474
01:19:04,730 --> 01:19:06,480
If you speak nonsense,
they'll lock you up in prison.

1475
01:19:07,313 --> 01:19:08,687
Let's contest
from a different constituency.

1476
01:19:08,688 --> 01:19:10,604
- That's part of Tamil Nadu as well.
- Yeah, right!

1477
01:19:10,605 --> 01:19:13,270
No one from our constituency would
vote for you because of your behavior.

1478
01:19:13,271 --> 01:19:14,563
Yet you expect votes
from different constituencies.

1479
01:19:14,813 --> 01:19:17,854
Hey, we'll bribe them with money,
briyani, and liquor.

1480
01:19:17,855 --> 01:19:19,146
That won't work out.

1481
01:19:19,605 --> 01:19:21,979
I've been in power for the past 10 years.

1482
01:19:21,980 --> 01:19:22,937
What do I do now?

1483
01:19:22,938 --> 01:19:24,396
Why don't you let your wife contest?

1484
01:19:24,730 --> 01:19:26,605
All the women will vote for her.

1485
01:19:26,896 --> 01:19:30,146
Do you expect me
to make my wife the President

1486
01:19:30,313 --> 01:19:32,021
and then stay home like an imbecile?

1487
01:19:32,146 --> 01:19:34,854
I'd rather drink poison and die.

1488
01:19:34,855 --> 01:19:36,355
Auntie will be the President for namesake.

1489
01:19:36,480 --> 01:19:37,896
But you will be calling the shots.

1490
01:19:39,063 --> 01:19:41,063
This is what's happening
in many ladies' constituencies.

1491
01:19:42,271 --> 01:19:43,146
What do you say, Sattam?

1492
01:19:43,938 --> 01:19:45,230
Veera is right about it.

1493
01:19:45,813 --> 01:19:47,645
Our only choice now is your wife.

1494
01:19:47,646 --> 01:19:48,521
There's no other option.

1495
01:19:52,896 --> 01:19:54,521
Welcome, Uncle.
This way.

1496
01:19:54,938 --> 01:19:55,938
Please sign this form.

1497
01:19:57,355 --> 01:20:00,438
Do you know how to sign,
or would a thumbprint do?

1498
01:20:00,646 --> 01:20:02,395
- I know how to sign.
- Fine, go ahead.

1499
01:20:02,396 --> 01:20:05,230
Don't sign incorrectly
and humiliate my legacy.

1500
01:20:06,230 --> 01:20:07,895
I have to teach her everything.

1501
01:20:07,896 --> 01:20:09,021
- Hello?
<i>- Dad!</i>

1502
01:20:09,396 --> 01:20:10,313
- My ill fate.
- Mathi!

1503
01:20:12,938 --> 01:20:15,355
- How are you?
- We're back home.

1504
01:20:15,563 --> 01:20:18,145
- I have to go to school tomorrow.
<i>- Yeah!</i>

1505
01:20:18,146 --> 01:20:20,438
So, Mom brought me back home.

1506
01:20:20,563 --> 01:20:24,730
- Did you eat?
- Yeah, I ate.

1507
01:20:25,021 --> 01:20:27,438
Hey, Mathi, who are you speaking to?

1508
01:20:28,021 --> 01:20:30,230
I'm speaking to my friend Vinoth.

1509
01:20:30,438 --> 01:20:32,271
I don't trust you. Let me check.

1510
01:20:33,105 --> 01:20:34,855
Come on, give me my phone.

1511
01:20:36,188 --> 01:20:37,105
You were telling the truth.

1512
01:20:37,605 --> 01:20:38,480
Fine, speak to him.

1513
01:20:39,271 --> 01:20:42,063
Okay, it's getting very crowded out here.

1514
01:20:42,230 --> 01:20:43,979
I'll meet you during lunch break tomorrow.

1515
01:20:43,980 --> 01:20:44,937
- Did you call me a crowd?
- Okay?

1516
01:20:44,938 --> 01:20:45,813
Okay.

1517
01:20:56,855 --> 01:20:58,188
Dad!

1518
01:20:58,938 --> 01:20:59,896
Come to me, dear!

1519
01:21:05,355 --> 01:21:07,271
Sambhar rice! Here, take a bite.

1520
01:21:11,105 --> 01:21:12,895
Eat faster.
Or lunch break will end soon.

1521
01:21:12,896 --> 01:21:14,688
Why don't you have a spoon as well?

1522
01:21:15,146 --> 01:21:16,938
- Why?
- Eat!

1523
01:21:20,896 --> 01:21:22,146
There's no salt.

1524
01:21:22,271 --> 01:21:23,688
This is nothing, Dad.

1525
01:21:23,813 --> 01:21:26,563
In the morning, another mayhem happened.

1526
01:21:26,730 --> 01:21:27,730
Mayhem, you say?

1527
01:21:28,813 --> 01:21:29,980
Hurry up!

1528
01:21:32,896 --> 01:21:34,563
Hey, what are you doing?

1529
01:21:34,688 --> 01:21:37,146
When I drop the <i>idlis</i> my father makes

1530
01:21:37,271 --> 01:21:39,313
it'll stick to the plate.

1531
01:21:39,563 --> 01:21:42,521
But Mom's <i>idlis</i> are bouncing.

1532
01:21:42,688 --> 01:21:44,438
Is it an <i>idli</i> or a ball?

1533
01:21:46,605 --> 01:21:47,563
Where's chutney?

1534
01:21:47,938 --> 01:21:50,146
There's no chutney.
Sugar will do. Eat now.

1535
01:21:50,355 --> 01:21:53,938
Dad used to make two chutneys for <i>idlis.</i>

1536
01:21:54,896 --> 01:21:56,980
Coconut chutney and tomato chutney.

1537
01:21:57,313 --> 01:22:00,646
Be thankful that I'm making <i>idlis</i> for you
despite my busy schedule.

1538
01:22:00,896 --> 01:22:02,271
And you're demanding 4 chutneys.

1539
01:22:02,688 --> 01:22:04,354
I don't care if you eat or not.

1540
01:22:04,355 --> 01:22:05,271
You're overdoing it.

1541
01:22:05,646 --> 01:22:07,188
<i>Idlis</i> with sugar are tasty.

1542
01:22:07,438 --> 01:22:08,438
Good combination.

1543
01:22:09,063 --> 01:22:11,980
Mom's cooking is horrible, Dad.

1544
01:22:12,188 --> 01:22:15,188
Please get back with Mom
so that I can eat tasty food.

1545
01:22:22,563 --> 01:22:24,937
- Why didn't you finish your lunch?
- I did finish it.

1546
01:22:24,938 --> 01:22:25,938
You haven't touched your lunch.

1547
01:22:26,188 --> 01:22:27,145
Oh, no!

1548
01:22:27,146 --> 01:22:30,896
My friend brought chicken,
so I ate that.

1549
01:22:31,771 --> 01:22:33,855
- Chicken made you forget sambhar rice.
- Oh, God, I'm caught.

1550
01:22:34,063 --> 01:22:36,520
I woke up early to make you lunch.

1551
01:22:36,521 --> 01:22:38,521
This is for you and this is for me.

1552
01:22:38,896 --> 01:22:40,230
Yayy!

1553
01:22:43,563 --> 01:22:45,563
How do you manage to eat that food?

1554
01:22:45,688 --> 01:22:47,896
It's my wife's cooking.
It'll be delicious.

1555
01:22:48,813 --> 01:22:51,604
- Please have some, Teacher.
- No, Teacher, that's my Mom's cooking.

1556
01:22:51,605 --> 01:22:52,604
Hey, don't be a brat!

1557
01:22:52,605 --> 01:22:54,271
Mom, what are you even doing?

1558
01:22:54,438 --> 01:22:56,813
You can't even braid my hair.

1559
01:22:57,688 --> 01:23:00,021
Dad used to create art with my braids.

1560
01:23:00,230 --> 01:23:02,688
If you bring up your father again,
I'll kill you.

1561
01:23:03,521 --> 01:23:04,563
Dad, my foot!

1562
01:23:05,146 --> 01:23:06,021
Here you go!

1563
01:23:12,563 --> 01:23:15,312
Isn't her mother coming here
every day to pick her up?

1564
01:23:15,313 --> 01:23:16,355
Why don't you talk to her?

1565
01:23:16,771 --> 01:23:20,063
If she knows I'm coming here,
she won't send Mathi to school.

1566
01:23:29,188 --> 01:23:31,355
Please vote for the Bucket symbol…

1567
01:23:31,563 --> 01:23:32,855
<i>Vote for Bucket symbol!</i>

1568
01:23:33,105 --> 01:23:34,271
Vote for Bucket symbol!

1569
01:23:34,438 --> 01:23:36,145
{\an8}Vote for Bucket and support Padma--

1570
01:23:36,146 --> 01:23:39,937
{\an8}President, you're here
to ask to vote for your wife.

1571
01:23:39,938 --> 01:23:40,895
{\an8}Yes!

1572
01:23:40,896 --> 01:23:44,188
{\an8}But if you have your nephew by your side,
who betrayed his wife

1573
01:23:44,396 --> 01:23:45,688
how do you expect us to vote?

1574
01:23:46,605 --> 01:23:47,480
{\an8}Uncle!

1575
01:23:47,813 --> 01:23:51,187
{\an8}Son! If you're here, no
woman is going to vote for us.

1576
01:23:51,188 --> 01:23:52,312
You better scram from here.

1577
01:23:52,313 --> 01:23:53,813
{\an8}We'll discuss the rest at home.

1578
01:23:53,938 --> 01:23:54,896
{\an8}Step down!

1579
01:23:55,646 --> 01:23:58,063
{\an8}Your wish is our wish.

1580
01:23:58,188 --> 01:24:01,104
{\an8}Please support Padma Rathinam
and vote for her.

1581
01:24:01,105 --> 01:24:02,771
{\an8}I sincerely request you to support us.

1582
01:24:17,521 --> 01:24:23,812
Hail, Chief!

1583
01:24:23,813 --> 01:24:24,980
Thank you all!

1584
01:24:26,146 --> 01:24:27,480
Where is the President?

1585
01:24:28,313 --> 01:24:30,313
I don't know Hindi.
Talk to me in English.

1586
01:24:30,438 --> 01:24:31,521
Where is Padma?

1587
01:24:32,271 --> 01:24:33,813
Why is he asking about my wife?

1588
01:24:34,313 --> 01:24:36,438
Brother, BDO has come down.

1589
01:24:36,563 --> 01:24:39,145
He might report to the higher officials.
Ask your wife to come right away.

1590
01:24:39,146 --> 01:24:40,437
Why should she come here?

1591
01:24:40,438 --> 01:24:41,771
I'm the President here.

1592
01:24:41,896 --> 01:24:43,687
Ask him to talk to me.

1593
01:24:43,688 --> 01:24:47,438
Just for a day. It's a formality.
Ask her to come.

1594
01:24:49,396 --> 01:24:50,646
Here, take it.

1595
01:24:53,688 --> 01:24:54,563
Come.

1596
01:24:55,938 --> 01:24:58,313
It's my wife, Padma.
Speak to her.

1597
01:24:58,855 --> 01:25:01,813
Do you know the key roles and
responsibilities of a Panchayat President?

1598
01:25:05,813 --> 01:25:07,313
- Why not?
- No, why not?

1599
01:25:07,813 --> 01:25:08,688
She's uneducated.

1600
01:25:10,646 --> 01:25:12,105
Administrative functions.

1601
01:25:12,355 --> 01:25:14,729
Financial Management
of the village administration.

1602
01:25:14,730 --> 01:25:16,605
Welfare and development programs.

1603
01:25:17,355 --> 01:25:21,146
And dispute resolution,
and also public representation.

1604
01:25:21,646 --> 01:25:24,146
Panchayat President
is a sole executive power

1605
01:25:24,355 --> 01:25:26,730
which holds the integrity
and the development of the Village.

1606
01:25:27,146 --> 01:25:28,895
Okay, okay, if you know so much

1607
01:25:28,896 --> 01:25:30,980
why would you let someone else
run the office?

1608
01:25:31,396 --> 01:25:34,938
You're well aware of how our system works.

1609
01:25:35,563 --> 01:25:37,271
What would women do in this situation?

1610
01:25:37,438 --> 01:25:39,605
Hey, she's speaking in Hindi.

1611
01:25:40,938 --> 01:25:42,813
I'm yet to recover from the shock
of her speaking English.

1612
01:25:42,980 --> 01:25:45,230
I thought she never studied
beyond 4th grade.

1613
01:25:45,480 --> 01:25:46,980
But she's excelling in every language.

1614
01:25:47,480 --> 01:25:48,355
Come in.

1615
01:25:48,730 --> 01:25:49,605
Step aside.

1616
01:25:53,938 --> 01:25:54,895
{\an8}Please sit.

1617
01:25:54,896 --> 01:25:59,355
{\an8}PRESIDENT

1618
01:26:00,021 --> 01:26:00,896
{\an8}Sign!

1619
01:26:01,313 --> 01:26:03,438
R. PADMA

1620
01:26:04,646 --> 01:26:05,521
{\an8}Who is he?

1621
01:26:07,771 --> 01:26:08,771
My husband.

1622
01:26:08,896 --> 01:26:09,813
House husband?

1623
01:26:12,438 --> 01:26:13,313
{\an8}Yes!

1624
01:26:13,563 --> 01:26:16,395
{\an8}For the next 5 years,
he must not step inside this office.

1625
01:26:16,396 --> 01:26:18,063
If he steps in, we'll get him arrested.

1626
01:26:18,438 --> 01:26:20,063
{\an8}- Understand? All the best!
- Alright!

1627
01:26:20,230 --> 01:26:21,230
{\an8}Thank you.

1628
01:26:28,855 --> 01:26:31,812
{\an8}How come you spoke to him
in both Hindi and English?

1629
01:26:31,813 --> 01:26:33,480
You'd better tell me the truth.
How far are you educated?

1630
01:26:33,730 --> 01:26:34,646
Speak up!

1631
01:26:35,105 --> 01:26:36,605
- B.A.
- Who's PA?

1632
01:26:37,521 --> 01:26:39,355
{\an8}- B.A. English Literature.
- What?!

1633
01:26:42,230 --> 01:26:43,895
{\an8}B.A. English Literature, she says.

1634
01:26:43,896 --> 01:26:46,980
{\an8}Hail, Padma!

1635
01:26:54,438 --> 01:26:57,020
- Sweetie!
- Hi, Dad, how are you?

1636
01:26:57,021 --> 01:26:58,771
I'm doing well. How are you?

1637
01:26:59,021 --> 01:27:00,937
I'm doing okay. Did you eat?

1638
01:27:00,938 --> 01:27:01,980
I ate! What about you?

1639
01:27:02,188 --> 01:27:04,813
I ate four <i>idlis.</i>

1640
01:27:05,605 --> 01:27:06,563
Hey…

1641
01:27:07,896 --> 01:27:09,230
<i>Did you finish your homework?</i>

1642
01:27:10,938 --> 01:27:12,188
Who is she speaking to?

1643
01:27:12,438 --> 01:27:14,021
She's speaking to her classmate, Vinoth.

1644
01:27:15,855 --> 01:27:17,688
- I'll call you later.
<i>- What happened?</i>

1645
01:27:19,646 --> 01:27:20,521
Come here.

1646
01:27:27,313 --> 01:27:28,188
Hand me the phone.

1647
01:27:29,771 --> 01:27:30,646
Hand it over right now.

1648
01:27:31,188 --> 01:27:32,063
Hand it, Mathi.

1649
01:27:32,730 --> 01:27:34,021
- Come on!
- Give it to me.

1650
01:27:37,021 --> 01:27:38,896
I told you right. It's Vinoth.

1651
01:27:39,146 --> 01:27:40,646
I've been checking on her daily.

1652
01:27:41,438 --> 01:27:43,396
Come on, dear, tell your mother.

1653
01:27:45,855 --> 01:27:48,271
When your mother asks,
you must hand it over right away.

1654
01:27:54,563 --> 01:27:56,271
Why did you hang up?
Was your uncle around you?

1655
01:27:56,896 --> 01:27:59,271
- Oh, no, you girl!
<i>- Hello? Hello?</i>

1656
01:28:00,188 --> 01:28:01,063
Sweetie!

1657
01:28:01,688 --> 01:28:02,563
Hello?

1658
01:28:04,438 --> 01:28:06,230
Is this how you check on her?

1659
01:28:08,646 --> 01:28:09,938
How long has this been going on?

1660
01:28:11,563 --> 01:28:13,354
I'm speaking to you.
How long has this been going on?

1661
01:28:13,355 --> 01:28:14,312
Speak up!

1662
01:28:14,313 --> 01:28:16,646
I'm talking to my father.
How does it bother you?

1663
01:28:17,021 --> 01:28:18,230
How does it bother me?

1664
01:28:18,730 --> 01:28:21,855
For what your father did to me,
I should've divorced him.

1665
01:28:22,063 --> 01:28:23,855
First, divorce me.

1666
01:28:23,980 --> 01:28:26,063
I don't like to live with you anymore.

1667
01:28:27,730 --> 01:28:29,021
You don't like to live with me?

1668
01:28:30,146 --> 01:28:32,562
- Did you see how insensitive she is?
- You're right.

1669
01:28:32,563 --> 01:28:33,604
It's all because of this phone.

1670
01:28:33,605 --> 01:28:35,105
I'll see how you're going to speak now.

1671
01:28:35,396 --> 01:28:37,230
Oh, no! Hey!

1672
01:28:40,230 --> 01:28:42,271
Hey! Little devil!

1673
01:28:44,480 --> 01:28:48,646
<i>The number you're trying to call
is currently not reachable. Please try--</i>

1674
01:28:53,938 --> 01:28:54,813
Get off the bike.

1675
01:28:58,688 --> 01:28:59,563
{\an8}Bye.

1676
01:29:01,146 --> 01:29:02,021
{\an8}Mathi!

1677
01:29:12,230 --> 01:29:13,105
Sweetie!

1678
01:29:15,313 --> 01:29:16,396
Dad!

1679
01:29:18,230 --> 01:29:19,313
Hey, what happened?

1680
01:29:21,313 --> 01:29:23,395
Hey, what happened?
Why are you crying?

1681
01:29:23,396 --> 01:29:25,229
Mom and I got into a fight.

1682
01:29:25,230 --> 01:29:26,605
And Mom beat me.

1683
01:29:26,813 --> 01:29:28,645
- Did she beat you?
- Yes!

1684
01:29:28,646 --> 01:29:30,854
I called you last night, remember.

1685
01:29:30,855 --> 01:29:33,063
So, she broke the phone.

1686
01:29:33,188 --> 01:29:34,145
Oh, no!

1687
01:29:34,146 --> 01:29:36,230
It's Uncle's phone, so don't bother.

1688
01:29:36,605 --> 01:29:38,771
I'm not going back to Mom anymore.

1689
01:29:38,896 --> 01:29:40,979
You come and get me
in the evening after school.

1690
01:29:40,980 --> 01:29:43,021
Just a few days, dear.
Everything will be alright.

1691
01:29:43,980 --> 01:29:46,604
Then, take me out somewhere.

1692
01:29:46,605 --> 01:29:48,312
I want to spend time with you.

1693
01:29:48,313 --> 01:29:49,812
Now? What about school?

1694
01:29:49,813 --> 01:29:50,979
Let's bunk school!

1695
01:29:50,980 --> 01:29:52,480
- Bunk?
- Who's bunking school?

1696
01:29:52,980 --> 01:29:53,855
Teacher!

1697
01:29:54,813 --> 01:29:57,230
Teacher, you see,
she and her mother got into a fight.

1698
01:29:57,438 --> 01:29:59,355
- She's very upset--
- So?

1699
01:30:01,855 --> 01:30:03,729
If you grant her half a day permission

1700
01:30:03,730 --> 01:30:06,313
I'll take her out, calm her down,
and bring her back during the lunch break.

1701
01:30:07,480 --> 01:30:08,480
Please, Teacher.

1702
01:30:11,438 --> 01:30:13,646
- Fine, bring her back soon.
- Thank you, Teacher.

1703
01:30:54,605 --> 01:30:58,021
<i>My sweet little darling
Smiles and dances playfully</i>

1704
01:30:58,438 --> 01:31:01,521
<i>The thunderous sky joins the rhythm</i>

1705
01:31:01,980 --> 01:31:05,188
<i>Her little feet
Hopping along in delight</i>

1706
01:31:05,563 --> 01:31:08,563
<i>Even the breeze sings a folk tune</i>

1707
01:31:08,813 --> 01:31:12,188
<i>You're the moonlight of this home</i>

1708
01:31:12,355 --> 01:31:15,937
<i>You're the rainbow
That walked into my life</i>

1709
01:31:15,938 --> 01:31:19,479
<i>You're my mirror image, my love</i>

1710
01:31:19,480 --> 01:31:23,062
<i>The magic in your eyes lingers on me</i>

1711
01:31:23,063 --> 01:31:26,438
<i>My daughter, my treasure</i>

1712
01:31:26,605 --> 01:31:30,021
<i>Let's leap with joy and share stories</i>

1713
01:31:30,146 --> 01:31:33,480
<i>My daughter, my treasure</i>

1714
01:31:33,730 --> 01:31:37,271
<i>Let's leap with joy
And share stories</i>

1715
01:31:51,438 --> 01:31:54,855
<i>The moment hunger strikes,
She starts demanding attention</i>

1716
01:31:55,021 --> 01:31:58,313
<i>Challenge her, she'll fight back</i>

1717
01:31:58,605 --> 01:32:02,021
<i>One moment, and it's all forgotten</i>

1718
01:32:02,146 --> 01:32:05,563
<i>A mother's warmth by my side</i>

1719
01:32:05,730 --> 01:32:09,105
<i>Resting in the comfort of my lap</i>

1720
01:32:09,313 --> 01:32:12,605
<i>Curled up there from dawn to dusk</i>

1721
01:32:12,813 --> 01:32:16,230
<i>Playful toes upon my forehead</i>

1722
01:32:16,396 --> 01:32:19,730
<i>She cheers me on
When I'm down</i>

1723
01:32:19,938 --> 01:32:23,355
<i>You're my mirror image, my love</i>

1724
01:32:23,480 --> 01:32:27,062
<i>The magic in your eyes lingers on me</i>

1725
01:32:27,063 --> 01:32:30,562
<i>My daughter, my treasure</i>

1726
01:32:30,563 --> 01:32:34,021
<i>Let's leap with joy
And share stories</i>

1727
01:32:34,146 --> 01:32:37,563
<i>My daughter, my treasure</i>

1728
01:32:37,688 --> 01:32:41,230
<i>Let's leap with joy
And share stories</i>

1729
01:32:56,063 --> 01:32:57,563
Daughters are always a father's pet.

1730
01:32:57,938 --> 01:32:59,105
That's how they'll react.

1731
01:32:59,605 --> 01:33:02,396
Don't overthink.
Wash your hands, and we'll have lunch.

1732
01:33:03,313 --> 01:33:04,188
Go!

1733
01:33:04,563 --> 01:33:08,271
She was angry, so I don't know if she ate.

1734
01:33:08,605 --> 01:33:10,438
Let me feed her and console her.

1735
01:33:10,605 --> 01:33:11,813
If I don't, I'll feel terrible.

1736
01:33:12,355 --> 01:33:13,980
- You carry on.
- Okay.

1737
01:33:27,271 --> 01:33:28,313
Auntie!

1738
01:33:28,730 --> 01:33:30,646
Mathi did not attend the class today.

1739
01:33:31,063 --> 01:33:32,646
- She was absent.
- What do you mean?

1740
01:33:32,980 --> 01:33:35,396
I went to her class
during the second period

1741
01:33:35,646 --> 01:33:37,104
but she was not in the classroom.

1742
01:33:37,105 --> 01:33:39,021
I dropped her off myself in the morning.

1743
01:33:39,480 --> 01:33:41,521
Please call her class teacher, Meenu.

1744
01:33:47,105 --> 01:33:49,521
Did her daughter, Mathi Malar
make it to school today?

1745
01:33:50,271 --> 01:33:52,855
- You see…
- Why are you hesitating?

1746
01:33:54,105 --> 01:33:55,438
She did come to school, Ma'am.

1747
01:33:55,980 --> 01:33:57,229
But she did not attend any classes.

1748
01:33:57,230 --> 01:33:59,896
What do you mean by that?
Where the hell did she go?

1749
01:34:28,480 --> 01:34:29,979
So, you let her go with her Dad?

1750
01:34:29,980 --> 01:34:32,438
Ma'am, she was very upset and dull.

1751
01:34:32,813 --> 01:34:35,313
- So…
- It doesn't matter how she is feeling.

1752
01:34:35,605 --> 01:34:37,230
Are you her mother, or am I?

1753
01:34:37,688 --> 01:34:39,938
- Ma'am--
- Keerthi, I insisted on taking her out.

1754
01:34:40,105 --> 01:34:41,188
It's not her fault.

1755
01:34:42,605 --> 01:34:44,230
I dropped her off at the school.

1756
01:34:44,605 --> 01:34:46,146
Who gave her the right
to send her off with him?

1757
01:34:46,480 --> 01:34:48,187
Is this how you run your school?

1758
01:34:48,188 --> 01:34:49,563
Ma'am, don't be loose with your words.

1759
01:34:49,813 --> 01:34:52,730
She did not send her off
with some stranger.

1760
01:34:53,105 --> 01:34:55,063
It's her father who took her out.

1761
01:34:55,563 --> 01:34:58,021
Keep your familial fights
limited to your family.

1762
01:34:58,188 --> 01:34:59,730
Please don't drag it to school.

1763
01:35:01,855 --> 01:35:03,605
- Mathi, let's go.
- I'm not coming.

1764
01:35:03,813 --> 01:35:05,521
Mathi, please come with me.
Don't get me worked up.

1765
01:35:05,688 --> 01:35:07,688
I won't come with you.
You'll beat me.

1766
01:35:08,021 --> 01:35:09,313
I won't beat you. Come with me.

1767
01:35:09,688 --> 01:35:11,187
You sound very angry.

1768
01:35:11,188 --> 01:35:12,938
I'm not angry. Come with me.

1769
01:35:13,063 --> 01:35:14,313
I'm going with Dad.

1770
01:35:14,605 --> 01:35:16,188
- Go with your Mom.
- I won't go with her.

1771
01:35:16,521 --> 01:35:18,479
- Keerthi, I'll bring her. You leave.
- You better come with me.

1772
01:35:18,480 --> 01:35:19,645
- Didn't I tell you earlier?
- I'll bring her Keerthi.

1773
01:35:19,646 --> 01:35:21,020
- Not to leave the school.
- I'll bring her.

1774
01:35:21,021 --> 01:35:22,520
- Why did you go out?
- Why are you beating her?

1775
01:35:22,521 --> 01:35:23,687
- Why did you go out?
- Don't beat her.

1776
01:35:23,688 --> 01:35:25,062
Don't beat, Keerthi.
Please don't beat her.

1777
01:35:25,063 --> 01:35:26,520
- Hey, Keerthi!
- Are you coming with me or not?

1778
01:35:26,521 --> 01:35:28,521
Keerthi, don't beat her.
Don't you hear me?

1779
01:35:32,396 --> 01:35:33,271
Keerth--

1780
01:35:34,688 --> 01:35:35,563
Kee--

1781
01:35:36,521 --> 01:35:37,521
Sorry.

1782
01:36:05,605 --> 01:36:07,438
<i>You slapped her in front of many people.</i>

1783
01:36:09,521 --> 01:36:10,646
I did not do it on purpose.

1784
01:36:11,146 --> 01:36:12,188
She was beating our daughter.

1785
01:36:12,563 --> 01:36:15,063
I couldn't control myself
and raise my hand at her.

1786
01:36:15,230 --> 01:36:16,521
It's her daughter
and she has every right to.

1787
01:36:16,855 --> 01:36:18,188
That does not give you the right
to slap her.

1788
01:36:18,521 --> 01:36:19,896
What you did isn't justified.

1789
01:36:20,521 --> 01:36:23,021
He hit his wife.
What's wrong with it?

1790
01:36:23,438 --> 01:36:25,605
Isn't he her husband?
What if she slaps him back?

1791
01:36:27,938 --> 01:36:29,730
Do you think she can't?

1792
01:36:29,896 --> 01:36:32,187
- Isn't she a wrestler?
- Why not?

1793
01:36:32,188 --> 01:36:33,480
Time have changed.

1794
01:36:34,730 --> 01:36:35,688
Wait a minute.

1795
01:36:36,355 --> 01:36:39,146
I don't want lunch.
Make it just for yourself.

1796
01:36:41,688 --> 01:36:43,355
I'll be done with the meeting
only in the evening.

1797
01:36:43,896 --> 01:36:47,105
Crisps are drying on the terrace.
Bring them down before it rains.

1798
01:36:47,313 --> 01:36:49,146
Also, bring water to the cows.

1799
01:36:49,688 --> 01:36:52,438
Most importantly,
don't sleep with the doors open.

1800
01:36:52,646 --> 01:36:53,730
Stray dogs will enter the house.

1801
01:37:00,230 --> 01:37:01,854
<i>Auntie will be the President for namesake.</i>

1802
01:37:01,855 --> 01:37:03,271
<i>But you will be calling the shots.</i>

1803
01:37:05,521 --> 01:37:08,313
{\an8}Veera, come with me.
I want to talk to you.

1804
01:37:10,021 --> 01:37:12,105
Go, go!
You've already ruined it for me.

1805
01:37:15,563 --> 01:37:16,438
Go!

1806
01:37:16,563 --> 01:37:17,563
To hell with him!

1807
01:37:20,605 --> 01:37:23,021
I wonder when she learned to drive.

1808
01:37:23,855 --> 01:37:26,563
I'm not sure what else I have to
endure in my life.

1809
01:37:27,896 --> 01:37:30,105
He slapped our daughter in public.

1810
01:37:30,396 --> 01:37:32,438
Does he think no one would question him?

1811
01:37:34,896 --> 01:37:36,396
Your daughter is crying her eyes out.

1812
01:37:36,563 --> 01:37:38,355
But you're sitting idle
like a statue out here.

1813
01:37:39,896 --> 01:37:42,563
Mom, she's not crying
because her husband slapped her.

1814
01:37:42,730 --> 01:37:44,355
She's crying because she hit her daughter.

1815
01:37:46,980 --> 01:37:48,605
I shouldn't have hit her.

1816
01:37:50,563 --> 01:37:53,146
I was angry with my husband
and took it out on her.

1817
01:37:54,355 --> 01:37:55,438
Poor thing, Mathi.

1818
01:37:56,438 --> 01:37:58,063
She must be in pain.

1819
01:38:03,563 --> 01:38:06,855
The conflict between you two
began over how to raise your child.

1820
01:38:06,980 --> 01:38:08,605
Now you have blew up the problem.

1821
01:38:10,021 --> 01:38:13,230
The biggest challenge for parents
is raising a child.

1822
01:38:13,605 --> 01:38:16,646
But if you don't raise the child right…

1823
01:38:17,146 --> 01:38:19,771
all the parents drown in guilt.

1824
01:38:20,271 --> 01:38:21,895
That we did not raise the children well.

1825
01:38:21,896 --> 01:38:23,438
We pampered them too much.

1826
01:38:23,730 --> 01:38:26,437
{\an8}To avoid those regrets,
parents raise them strictly.

1827
01:38:26,438 --> 01:38:28,355
{\an8}VILLAGE HEAD
KEELA AMBUR PANCHAYAT

1828
01:38:33,105 --> 01:38:34,105
Listen, Veera.

1829
01:38:34,855 --> 01:38:35,855
I don't have children.

1830
01:38:36,688 --> 01:38:39,355
If I had,
I would've raised it the way Keerthi is.

1831
01:38:40,021 --> 01:38:41,980
In today's world, we must raise
our daughters to be strong.

1832
01:38:42,605 --> 01:38:45,980
We should start teaching them martial arts
or wrestling when they're 6 years old.

1833
01:38:46,438 --> 01:38:48,230
We see a lot of news day in and out.

1834
01:38:48,563 --> 01:38:51,313
While going to study,
or work, or going out

1835
01:38:51,730 --> 01:38:54,563
every day, women face danger
in many forms.

1836
01:38:55,563 --> 01:38:58,021
Parents can't accompany them everywhere.

1837
01:38:58,271 --> 01:39:00,146
The Police won't be
at guard everywhere, either.

1838
01:39:00,396 --> 01:39:02,063
Women have to save themselves.

1839
01:39:03,021 --> 01:39:06,021
Anyone who learns Karate during
childhood doesn't become a master in it.

1840
01:39:06,355 --> 01:39:07,521
It's just for self defense.

1841
01:39:07,730 --> 01:39:09,021
Similarly, wrestling.

1842
01:39:09,230 --> 01:39:11,354
Once she grows up,
if she feels wrestling is not her calling

1843
01:39:11,355 --> 01:39:13,063
she can move on to pursue something else.

1844
01:39:13,521 --> 01:39:16,813
But the wrestling she learned
will protect her for life.

1845
01:39:28,563 --> 01:39:31,105
Dad, why are you not sleeping?

1846
01:39:31,730 --> 01:39:34,063
Nothing much, dear.

1847
01:39:34,521 --> 01:39:38,355
You seemed happy
when you came to see me at school.

1848
01:39:38,563 --> 01:39:43,437
I'm here with you now,
but you don't seem happy.

1849
01:39:43,438 --> 01:39:44,313
Why?

1850
01:39:44,980 --> 01:39:48,938
I'm happy, dear.
But Mom will be sad without you.

1851
01:39:49,188 --> 01:39:50,855
She won't be suffering, though.

1852
01:39:51,105 --> 01:39:53,813
She does not like me.
I'm sure she must be having fun.

1853
01:39:55,021 --> 01:39:56,063
Do you think so?

1854
01:39:59,480 --> 01:40:00,854
Shall I tell you a story?

1855
01:40:00,855 --> 01:40:03,355
Is it a story of a lion or a fox?

1856
01:40:04,230 --> 01:40:05,105
It's neither!

1857
01:40:05,521 --> 01:40:07,895
It's a story about a Dora Baby like you.

1858
01:40:07,896 --> 01:40:09,646
Dora Baby? Please tell me.

1859
01:40:11,938 --> 01:40:14,146
Dora Baby was five years old.

1860
01:40:14,313 --> 01:40:15,771
How does she look?

1861
01:40:15,980 --> 01:40:19,063
She is beautiful and cute like you.

1862
01:40:23,980 --> 01:40:26,521
<i>That baby was very interested in wrestling
at that young age.</i>

1863
01:40:27,396 --> 01:40:28,855
79

1864
01:40:30,355 --> 01:40:32,021
<i>She had her first match at 10 years old.</i>

1865
01:40:33,063 --> 01:40:34,813
<i>At 15 she was a school champion.</i>

1866
01:40:35,355 --> 01:40:36,895
Hereafter, you should not
take part in wrestling.

1867
01:40:36,896 --> 01:40:39,230
- Focus on your studies.
<i>- Her father restricted her.</i>

1868
01:40:39,813 --> 01:40:41,021
But she did not pay heed to her father.

1869
01:40:41,480 --> 01:40:44,146
<i>She started wrestling in college
without her parents' knowledge.</i>

1870
01:40:48,480 --> 01:40:49,771
<i>She was old enough for marriage.</i>

1871
01:40:50,355 --> 01:40:51,438
<i>But could not find a match.</i>

1872
01:40:51,605 --> 01:40:53,605
<i>They rejected her
because she is a wrestler.</i>

1873
01:40:55,813 --> 01:40:58,855
For the women of our country,
family comes first.

1874
01:40:59,855 --> 01:41:02,855
On seeing her father's health,
she quit wrestling and got married.

1875
01:41:05,271 --> 01:41:06,771
<i>Her husband was not understanding.</i>

1876
01:41:08,730 --> 01:41:10,854
Once he knew she was a wrestler,
he asked her to leave.

1877
01:41:10,855 --> 01:41:11,730
Dear, listen--

1878
01:41:12,896 --> 01:41:15,480
<i>Later, he challenged her
to a wrestling match.</i>

1879
01:41:17,896 --> 01:41:20,896
<i>Only then did he realize
wrestling is a tough sport.</i>

1880
01:41:21,646 --> 01:41:23,980
<i>And how much she has
sacrificed in her life.</i>

1881
01:41:27,313 --> 01:41:31,855
Despite having no support from her family,
she excelled in wrestling.

1882
01:41:32,355 --> 01:41:33,605
It must not go to waste, right?

1883
01:41:34,938 --> 01:41:37,563
So, he decided to support her dreams.

1884
01:41:38,980 --> 01:41:41,105
That's when she gave birth to a child.

1885
01:41:44,855 --> 01:41:47,646
After giving birth,
continuing wrestling is tough.

1886
01:41:48,896 --> 01:41:50,480
<i>The body and health won't be the same.</i>

1887
01:41:52,188 --> 01:41:54,063
<i>Still, she overcame it
and continued to pursue wrestling.</i>

1888
01:41:55,980 --> 01:41:58,396
The child had mother's milk for 2 years.

1889
01:41:59,771 --> 01:42:03,730
She used to pump milk into the
feeding bottle and head to training.

1890
01:42:06,438 --> 01:42:09,230
<i>She once went to Chandigarh
for a two-month training camp.</i>

1891
01:42:11,146 --> 01:42:12,021
Bye!

1892
01:42:14,480 --> 01:42:16,771
<i>Back home the child was crying
without mother's milk.</i>

1893
01:42:17,188 --> 01:42:19,230
<i>During training,
she suffered from breast engorgement.</i>

1894
01:42:21,105 --> 01:42:23,770
To cope with the engorgement,

1895
01:42:23,771 --> 01:42:25,480
she would express her breast milk
in the bathroom and resume training.

1896
01:42:26,355 --> 01:42:27,438
I am going to quit wrestling.

1897
01:42:28,313 --> 01:42:29,896
I can't stop thinking about our daughter.

1898
01:42:30,063 --> 01:42:31,480
You must not waste your talent.

1899
01:42:31,771 --> 01:42:34,855
You continue to train.
I'll take responsibility of our child.

1900
01:42:38,521 --> 01:42:40,104
<i>Poor thing, that mother.</i>

1901
01:42:40,105 --> 01:42:43,605
She must've suffered
being away from her child.

1902
01:42:45,563 --> 01:42:48,521
Where are the mother and child now?

1903
01:42:49,730 --> 01:42:51,313
Mom Dora is at her house.

1904
01:42:51,980 --> 01:42:54,021
And Baby Dora is with me right here.

1905
01:42:55,063 --> 01:42:59,146
Wait, were you telling me
my mother's story all along?

1906
01:43:10,771 --> 01:43:15,313
<i>My golden girl,
The treasure of my heart</i>

1907
01:43:15,730 --> 01:43:19,771
<i>I long to see your innocent face</i>

1908
01:43:21,313 --> 01:43:25,896
<i>My precious girl, my treasure!</i>

1909
01:43:26,355 --> 01:43:30,980
<i>I long to hear
Your sweet, endearing voice</i>

1910
01:43:31,980 --> 01:43:33,938
<i>Oh, dear! Oh, dear!</i>

1911
01:43:34,313 --> 01:43:39,105
<i>My dear friend who playfully quarrels
With me every day</i>

1912
01:43:39,688 --> 01:43:42,063
<i>My dear friend</i>

1913
01:43:42,646 --> 01:43:44,480
<i>Oh, dear! Oh, dear!</i>

1914
01:43:45,063 --> 01:43:51,938
<i>You're the sweet friend who defeats me
Without even saying a word</i>

1915
01:43:53,438 --> 01:43:57,813
<i>Tears surge within me like the sea</i>

1916
01:43:58,146 --> 01:44:03,313
<i>Come be the shore
That brings me home</i>

1917
01:44:04,063 --> 01:44:08,563
<i>The night scorches the sky within me</i>

1918
01:44:08,730 --> 01:44:13,771
<i>Come, little moon,
And shine beside me</i>

1919
01:44:33,605 --> 01:44:34,605
Ma'am, courier!

1920
01:44:39,105 --> 01:44:40,105
What is this?

1921
01:44:44,396 --> 01:44:45,938
You wanted me to quit wrestling.

1922
01:44:46,230 --> 01:44:47,188
I did not listen to you.

1923
01:44:48,396 --> 01:44:50,938
Now, I'm pushing my daughter
to pursue wrestling.

1924
01:44:51,355 --> 01:44:52,688
But she is refusing it.

1925
01:44:52,855 --> 01:44:54,105
And she's interested in dancing.

1926
01:44:55,105 --> 01:44:59,646
It is the duty of parents to understand
what their child is passionate about.

1927
01:45:00,563 --> 01:45:04,438
Not to impose our passion on to our child

1928
01:45:04,855 --> 01:45:06,730
I learnt it from you, my dear.

1929
01:45:07,271 --> 01:45:08,188
But you,

1930
01:45:10,230 --> 01:45:12,771
Sports gave me everything I have today.

1931
01:45:15,938 --> 01:45:19,188
My self confidence, happiness,

1932
01:45:20,230 --> 01:45:22,730
I wanted my child to enjoy
the same opportunities.

1933
01:45:23,563 --> 01:45:25,480
That's why I sent her
to train in wrestling.

1934
01:45:27,646 --> 01:45:29,188
But when I think about it now…

1935
01:45:31,313 --> 01:45:34,146
whether I did the right thing or not…

1936
01:45:35,063 --> 01:45:35,938
I'm not sure!

1937
01:45:37,355 --> 01:45:41,313
Parents can guide children
only up to the age of 14 or 15.

1938
01:45:41,855 --> 01:45:45,146
After 14 or 15,
children start making their own choices.

1939
01:45:46,396 --> 01:45:49,605
Until then, it's enough to teach them
the difference between right and wrong.

1940
01:45:50,313 --> 01:45:53,021
As parents that's our duty.

1941
01:45:55,980 --> 01:45:58,855
- Good morning!
- Good morning!

1942
01:46:03,771 --> 01:46:05,146
<i>Why isn't Mathi coming to school?</i>

1943
01:46:05,313 --> 01:46:07,937
Teacher, she's not herself, lately.

1944
01:46:07,938 --> 01:46:09,563
So, she refuses to come to school.

1945
01:46:13,771 --> 01:46:15,646
- Mom, do you like this serial?
- People!

1946
01:46:15,896 --> 01:46:17,895
He did not send Mathi to school
for 4 days.

1947
01:46:17,896 --> 01:46:18,854
Matter needs attention.

1948
01:46:18,855 --> 01:46:21,813
If you don't question him
he'll destroy her life, too.

1949
01:46:23,896 --> 01:46:27,188
Listen, the only way to get our
child back is through legal means.

1950
01:46:27,521 --> 01:46:29,063
I spoke to the lawyer, already.

1951
01:46:29,313 --> 01:46:31,187
Let's end this circus.

1952
01:46:31,188 --> 01:46:32,229
Hey, shut up!

1953
01:46:32,230 --> 01:46:33,771
It's not even a month
since they got separated.

1954
01:46:33,896 --> 01:46:35,145
And you want to consult a lawyer.

1955
01:46:35,146 --> 01:46:36,645
Let's meet him and discuss further.

1956
01:46:36,646 --> 01:46:39,229
Are you going to question him
why he slapped Keerthi?

1957
01:46:39,230 --> 01:46:40,105
We must question him!

1958
01:46:40,230 --> 01:46:42,813
In the past 6 years
he has never slapped her.

1959
01:46:42,938 --> 01:46:45,355
If he slapped her now
there must be a reason.

1960
01:46:45,688 --> 01:46:48,563
So, if there's a reason you'd slap her.

1961
01:46:49,105 --> 01:46:50,313
That's not what I meant.

1962
01:46:50,896 --> 01:46:54,230
The way she's upset for hitting her child

1963
01:46:54,396 --> 01:46:57,938
similarly, son-in-law
must be upset for hitting her.

1964
01:46:59,021 --> 01:47:02,063
Let's all go together
and discuss this matter further.

1965
01:47:03,146 --> 01:47:06,230
{\an8}Why are you being stubborn?
Please get in the car.

1966
01:47:06,938 --> 01:47:10,520
Do you really think they're upset
because I'm not with them?

1967
01:47:10,521 --> 01:47:11,605
How would they not?

1968
01:47:11,896 --> 01:47:13,770
The way this situation upsets you

1969
01:47:13,771 --> 01:47:17,980
your child and your husband
will feel that pain twice as much.

1970
01:47:19,438 --> 01:47:22,146
You'd believe me only
when you see it for yourself.

1971
01:47:22,521 --> 01:47:23,438
Get in!

1972
01:47:25,021 --> 01:47:26,688
I can't believe you're paying heed to me.

1973
01:47:26,813 --> 01:47:27,813
One important matter.

1974
01:47:28,063 --> 01:47:29,729
No one should utter a word
when we get there.

1975
01:47:29,730 --> 01:47:30,938
- Why?
- I'll speak to him.

1976
01:47:31,480 --> 01:47:32,480
Start the vehicle.

1977
01:47:35,105 --> 01:47:37,605
She's upset all the time.
She's not smiling.

1978
01:47:38,646 --> 01:47:40,480
Making a child smile isn't a big deal.

1979
01:47:45,896 --> 01:47:46,771
Step aside!

1980
01:48:01,688 --> 01:48:02,730
Class Teacher.

1981
01:48:07,313 --> 01:48:08,896
Why aren't you coming to school?

1982
01:48:14,063 --> 01:48:14,938
Here you go.

1983
01:48:16,188 --> 01:48:17,313
You don't want it?

1984
01:48:21,771 --> 01:48:22,646
I don't want it.

1985
01:49:25,563 --> 01:49:26,438
Hello!

1986
01:50:50,480 --> 01:50:51,813
First, put them down.

1987
01:50:53,146 --> 01:50:54,063
Did you notice

1988
01:50:54,521 --> 01:50:55,938
who he is letting down first.

1989
01:50:56,563 --> 01:50:57,730
When are you going to get her off?

1990
01:51:07,271 --> 01:51:08,980
<i>The way this situation upsets you</i>

1991
01:51:09,146 --> 01:51:13,396
<i>your child and your husband
will feel that pain twice as much.</i>

1992
01:51:17,146 --> 01:51:20,605
You asked us not to utter word
and claimed to handle the situation.

1993
01:51:20,938 --> 01:51:23,063
But you're not talking now.

1994
01:51:23,355 --> 01:51:24,230
Didn't you see what happened?

1995
01:51:27,438 --> 01:51:28,687
There's nothing left to say.

1996
01:51:28,688 --> 01:51:30,271
Son-in-law put up show for us.

1997
01:51:30,480 --> 01:51:31,938
It's not what you think it is.

1998
01:51:32,188 --> 01:51:33,605
What do you mean?

1999
01:51:34,021 --> 01:51:35,688
Were you planning to use another step?

2000
01:51:36,355 --> 01:51:37,855
It's my fault I had faith in you.

2001
01:51:38,521 --> 01:51:41,563
Before you got here
we were truly sad.

2002
01:51:41,813 --> 01:51:43,021
I don't get it, though.

2003
01:51:43,146 --> 01:51:45,271
The song you were dancing to
is not meant for sad situations.

2004
01:51:47,771 --> 01:51:50,354
Any husband away from his wife
tends to dance with joy.

2005
01:51:50,355 --> 01:51:54,355
That doesn't mean
you should be dancing with such joy.

2006
01:51:54,646 --> 01:51:57,396
Coming here opened our eyes to the truth.

2007
01:51:58,896 --> 01:52:00,646
- Let's leave.
- Disgusting.

2008
01:52:03,688 --> 01:52:05,105
What are you waiting for?

2009
01:52:05,396 --> 01:52:07,355
Next is legal route.
Let's go!

2010
01:52:07,521 --> 01:52:08,396
Keerthi…

2011
01:52:09,146 --> 01:52:10,021
Keerthi!

2012
01:52:10,938 --> 01:52:11,813
{\an8}Keerthi!

2013
01:52:12,605 --> 01:52:13,563
I'm doomed!

2014
01:52:20,188 --> 01:52:22,688
Look at this, Uncle.
She has sent me a divorce notice.

2015
01:52:22,938 --> 01:52:24,687
Why would she go this far?

2016
01:52:24,688 --> 01:52:27,021
You're handing it to him
as if he knows English!

2017
01:52:28,105 --> 01:52:29,438
I had to read it out to you.

2018
01:52:29,688 --> 01:52:32,104
Veera, if we go to court,

2019
01:52:32,105 --> 01:52:33,770
they will rule that the daughter
must live with her mother.

2020
01:52:33,771 --> 01:52:34,895
That's why they sent you
the divorce notice.

2021
01:52:34,896 --> 01:52:35,937
That's not fair.

2022
01:52:35,938 --> 01:52:37,854
So, when you withdraw cash from an ATM,

2023
01:52:37,855 --> 01:52:40,396
does it belong to the machine
or the person who withdrew it?

2024
01:52:40,646 --> 01:52:41,604
Gosh!

2025
01:52:41,605 --> 01:52:44,312
Brother, don't talk nonsense
in court like you do here.

2026
01:52:44,313 --> 01:52:45,605
The judge will get you arrested.

2027
01:52:46,480 --> 01:52:48,604
Veera, there's no point in getting angry.

2028
01:52:48,605 --> 01:52:50,104
The court demands evidence.

2029
01:52:50,105 --> 01:52:52,395
Only if you produce
the Ayurvedic doctor in court

2030
01:52:52,396 --> 01:52:53,980
can you prove your innocence.

2031
01:52:54,355 --> 01:52:56,396
I'm not sure where he's hiding.

2032
01:52:56,605 --> 01:52:57,855
He's not opening his clinic either.

2033
01:53:06,521 --> 01:53:08,855
What the hell?
We could've easily won.

2034
01:53:10,063 --> 01:53:11,771
- It's okay, Coach.
- We'll make it up next time.

2035
01:53:15,313 --> 01:53:17,230
Doctor, over here!

2036
01:53:18,313 --> 01:53:21,480
You can reopen the clinic now.
He won't come looking for you.

2037
01:53:22,563 --> 01:53:26,438
He'll be running back and forth
between court and home.

2038
01:53:34,063 --> 01:53:36,771
Doctor, why is your face swollen?

2039
01:53:49,855 --> 01:53:51,896
He somehow sought me out from hiding.

2040
01:53:56,146 --> 01:53:58,479
<i>Only if you present
the Ayurveda Doctor in the court</i>

2041
01:53:58,480 --> 01:54:00,063
<i>can you prove yourself innocent.</i>

2042
01:54:03,105 --> 01:54:04,313
{\an8}<i>It's 3,500 rupees for the medicine.</i>

2043
01:54:05,521 --> 01:54:06,771
{\an8}<i>You met them at the temple, is it?</i>

2044
01:54:08,105 --> 01:54:10,313
<i>Only after visiting
other rituals would follow.</i>

2045
01:54:10,896 --> 01:54:12,020
<i>Let me know how you got lucky.</i>

2046
01:54:12,021 --> 01:54:13,480
<i>I've been trying for 15 years.</i>

2047
01:54:17,480 --> 01:54:18,896
Bless me, God!

2048
01:54:25,105 --> 01:54:27,021
Hey, please don't harm me.

2049
01:54:27,230 --> 01:54:28,521
The Coach is the
cause of all the problems.

2050
01:54:29,188 --> 01:54:30,146
The Coach?

2051
01:54:31,521 --> 01:54:32,396
I ought to!

2052
01:54:35,771 --> 01:54:37,188
I blindly trusted you.

2053
01:54:39,146 --> 01:54:41,980
Wrestling is a sport
that you play face to face.

2054
01:54:44,730 --> 01:54:47,270
You're not fit to be
called a sportsperson.

2055
01:54:47,271 --> 01:54:49,813
You're right!
I shouldn't be in the field of sports.

2056
01:54:50,105 --> 01:54:51,605
Only your wife deserves to be in sports.

2057
01:54:51,938 --> 01:54:55,063
Only she plays, wins medals,
and gets promotions.

2058
01:54:55,188 --> 01:54:56,188
But I should be just sitting ducks.

2059
01:54:58,146 --> 01:55:00,021
Neither they respect me at the office.

2060
01:55:00,355 --> 01:55:02,521
Nor do they respect me at the Academy.
In fact,

2061
01:55:03,896 --> 01:55:05,854
I don't get respect even at my home.

2062
01:55:05,855 --> 01:55:08,521
The other day, she said,
"My husband is the reason for my success."

2063
01:55:10,021 --> 01:55:11,355
Just because you cook three meals a day

2064
01:55:11,521 --> 01:55:12,771
doesn't mean you're the reason
for her success.

2065
01:55:13,105 --> 01:55:14,480
That's not what she meant.

2066
01:55:18,521 --> 01:55:19,396
I'm the Coach!

2067
01:55:20,146 --> 01:55:21,980
Giving me some credit
wouldn't make her any less.

2068
01:55:22,146 --> 01:55:23,313
- That's why…
- Stop!

2069
01:55:23,521 --> 01:55:26,313
I wanted to defeat her
in wrestling this time.

2070
01:55:29,021 --> 01:55:30,271
Just defeating her won't be enough.

2071
01:55:31,188 --> 01:55:34,063
So, I decided to drive her
out of the field altogether.

2072
01:55:35,730 --> 01:55:37,938
Now her career has been destroyed.

2073
01:56:37,063 --> 01:56:39,063
Keerthi! Keerthi!

2074
01:56:42,230 --> 01:56:43,105
Keerthi!

2075
01:56:44,355 --> 01:56:45,230
Keerthi!

2076
01:56:46,521 --> 01:56:48,230
Do you know who's behind all our problems?

2077
01:56:48,813 --> 01:56:49,813
It's the Coach, right?

2078
01:56:51,396 --> 01:56:52,313
How did you know?

2079
01:56:53,521 --> 01:56:54,521
The Coach told himself.

2080
01:56:57,563 --> 01:57:00,480
<i>Keerthi, look at what your husband
has done to me.</i>

2081
01:57:01,813 --> 01:57:03,937
<i>He's threatening
me into telling you</i>

2082
01:57:03,938 --> 01:57:05,813
<i>that I influenced him
to give you the meds.</i>

2083
01:57:05,938 --> 01:57:08,355
<i>I refused to say it, and I got beaten up.</i>

2084
01:57:08,855 --> 01:57:09,812
He's lying!

2085
01:57:09,813 --> 01:57:12,521
I'm going to wait and see what else
you would do to hide your mistakes.

2086
01:57:12,688 --> 01:57:14,062
- Keerthi--
- You beat him up mercilessly.

2087
01:57:14,063 --> 01:57:15,688
Trust me, Keerthi. He's lying!

2088
01:57:16,438 --> 01:57:18,188
- I swear he asked me to give you the meds.
- Don't say anything.

2089
01:57:18,605 --> 01:57:19,854
Please don't say anything.

2090
01:57:19,855 --> 01:57:21,271
- Trust me, Keerthi.
- I trusted you enough.

2091
01:57:21,396 --> 01:57:22,771
If you have anything to say,
say it in court.

2092
01:57:22,938 --> 01:57:24,355
I don't wish to talk to you anymore.

2093
01:57:25,313 --> 01:57:26,813
Keerthi! Keerthi!

2094
01:57:27,980 --> 01:57:28,980
You believe in his words.

2095
01:57:29,313 --> 01:57:30,480
But you're refusing to believe me.

2096
01:57:30,938 --> 01:57:34,271
Being uneducated,
I foolishly trusted everything he told me.

2097
01:57:34,521 --> 01:57:37,105
Aren't you educated?
But you're a bigger fool than me.

2098
01:57:37,771 --> 01:57:39,230
Going to court won't fix our problems.

2099
01:57:40,438 --> 01:57:42,896
I don't know
how else to make you understand.

2100
01:57:51,480 --> 01:57:52,730
Dad, Mom's out there.

2101
01:58:12,313 --> 01:58:15,729
- Sir, Judge Vishwanathan is on leave.
- Who is replacing him?

2102
01:58:15,730 --> 01:58:16,896
Raja Rajeshwari.

2103
01:58:17,063 --> 01:58:18,646
Oh, no, not her!

2104
01:58:19,021 --> 01:58:20,438
{\an8}PRINCIPAL DISTRICT JUDGE
COIMBATORE

2105
01:58:27,480 --> 01:58:28,980
It's our bad luck she's the judge today.

2106
01:58:29,105 --> 01:58:30,021
What happened, sir?

2107
01:58:30,230 --> 01:58:31,730
That Judge won't let the lawyers argue.

2108
01:58:31,855 --> 01:58:33,563
She'll speak for herself,
whatever the lawyer has to say.

2109
01:58:33,896 --> 01:58:36,730
If she questions you be straight forward
and ask for divorce.

2110
01:58:37,021 --> 01:58:38,771
She's a very tricky person.

2111
01:58:52,855 --> 01:58:56,771
Lately, in our country, divorce cases are
on the rise more than theft and murder.

2112
01:58:57,105 --> 01:58:58,313
Not sure where it's headed.

2113
01:59:03,646 --> 01:59:04,521
Proceed!

2114
01:59:04,688 --> 01:59:10,188
HMOP 1520/2026 Veera - Keerthi.

2115
01:59:12,063 --> 01:59:13,895
Your Honor, my client--

2116
01:59:13,896 --> 01:59:16,021
Why should there be a 3rd party
between a husband and wife.

2117
01:59:16,813 --> 01:59:18,230
Didn't they get married?

2118
01:59:18,480 --> 01:59:21,021
- Madam, I'm a lawyer.
- Even lawyer shouldn't interfere.

2119
01:59:21,396 --> 01:59:22,271
Sit down!

2120
01:59:27,063 --> 01:59:27,938
Please proceed, dear.

2121
01:59:29,021 --> 01:59:31,188
- What do you want?
- I want my daughter.

2122
01:59:32,646 --> 01:59:34,146
I want my father.

2123
01:59:35,396 --> 01:59:36,605
I want my wife.

2124
01:59:40,480 --> 01:59:41,730
Then what am I doing here?

2125
01:59:42,646 --> 01:59:44,396
What are client's demand?

2126
01:59:44,730 --> 01:59:46,271
That's what I was trying to
tell you earlier.

2127
01:59:46,896 --> 01:59:48,646
Why wouldn't you tell now?

2128
01:59:48,896 --> 01:59:49,813
Sure, My Lord!

2129
01:59:51,063 --> 01:59:54,980
My client's husband has been working
as a house husband for the past 7 years.

2130
01:59:55,271 --> 01:59:57,146
They had their differences.

2131
01:59:57,271 --> 01:59:59,562
And the reason was a disagreement
over how to raise the child.

2132
01:59:59,563 --> 02:00:04,020
Envious of my client's achievements
in wrestling,

2133
02:00:04,021 --> 02:00:05,813
Veera, a house husband,

2134
02:00:05,980 --> 02:00:10,146
plotted repeatedly to ensure her defeat.

2135
02:00:10,646 --> 02:00:15,771
So, I request that he be
sentenced to death, Your Honor.

2136
02:00:18,896 --> 02:00:20,855
Enough! I'm not surprised
because you brought this lawyer to us.

2137
02:00:21,105 --> 02:00:22,188
- What's happening, Sattam?
- Hey!

2138
02:00:26,105 --> 02:00:28,355
Sorry, Your Honor, I said it in a flow.

2139
02:00:28,563 --> 02:00:30,521
Pegs himself to be Tiger Dayanidhi.
Sit down, damn it!

2140
02:00:35,188 --> 02:00:38,062
If you didn't like to
remain a house husband,

2141
02:00:38,063 --> 02:00:39,563
why didn't you tell your wife?

2142
02:00:39,771 --> 02:00:40,896
Why did you spoil her life?

2143
02:00:42,563 --> 02:00:44,938
- Your Honor, my client--
- Don't you see I'm talking to him?

2144
02:00:45,313 --> 02:00:46,813
Stop interfering! Sit down!

2145
02:00:50,688 --> 02:00:51,563
Go ahead!

2146
02:00:51,771 --> 02:00:55,105
The respect I received
when I was lurking like a loafer

2147
02:00:55,480 --> 02:00:58,105
I did not receive it
when I became a house husband.

2148
02:00:58,730 --> 02:01:01,980
That being said, even my uncle
has not spoken to me for years now.

2149
02:01:05,563 --> 02:01:07,145
A man should do household chores.

2150
02:01:07,146 --> 02:01:10,105
And sharing other work with your wife
is what society preaches.

2151
02:01:10,355 --> 02:01:12,480
But mock the men who do household chores.

2152
02:01:13,063 --> 02:01:16,313
It's because we have never
respected a housewife.

2153
02:01:17,730 --> 02:01:20,271
We keep pointing out that
they stay at home idle, doing nothing.

2154
02:01:20,730 --> 02:01:22,313
People go out to do a job.

2155
02:01:22,563 --> 02:01:27,313
But for the ones who stay home,
they work from dawn till dusk.

2156
02:01:27,480 --> 02:01:30,563
They don't have holidays
or weekends to relax and enjoy.

2157
02:01:31,146 --> 02:01:32,396
All days are the same to them.

2158
02:01:32,521 --> 02:01:34,270
TRUTH ALONE TRIUMPHS

2159
02:01:34,271 --> 02:01:38,146
If a man is achieving in his career,
then his wife is behind his success.

2160
02:01:38,646 --> 02:01:40,271
Many don't realize it.

2161
02:01:41,813 --> 02:01:45,021
There's a woman behind
every man's success.

2162
02:01:45,230 --> 02:01:47,563
Imagine if there's a man behind
a woman's success

2163
02:01:47,688 --> 02:01:48,813
and it's the husband.

2164
02:01:49,146 --> 02:01:51,521
That woman would be
the happiest in the world.

2165
02:01:53,021 --> 02:01:54,980
I wish to be that man in Keerthi's life.

2166
02:01:56,730 --> 02:01:58,146
You spoke a lot.

2167
02:01:58,355 --> 02:02:00,230
Then, why did you poison her food?

2168
02:02:01,063 --> 02:02:02,855
I did not poison her. It was medicine.

2169
02:02:02,980 --> 02:02:04,521
That's what I meant.
Why did you do it?

2170
02:02:05,105 --> 02:02:06,646
May I ask you one question, Madam?

2171
02:02:07,688 --> 02:02:11,021
- Proceed!
- Madam, what is toughest job in the world?

2172
02:02:11,188 --> 02:02:12,188
Why don't you answer it yourself?

2173
02:02:12,396 --> 02:02:14,105
- It's being a husband.
- What?

2174
02:02:14,480 --> 02:02:15,396
I'm telling the truth, Madam.

2175
02:02:15,896 --> 02:02:18,938
Being a husband is tough job
than being a Judge.

2176
02:02:19,355 --> 02:02:21,396
You had to graduate to become a Judge.

2177
02:02:21,563 --> 02:02:23,480
Because there books to learn about law.

2178
02:02:23,855 --> 02:02:25,563
So, you know what to do and when.

2179
02:02:25,688 --> 02:02:28,938
But there is no study material or degree
that teaches you how to be a husband.

2180
02:02:29,146 --> 02:02:31,521
There's no specific book available
that teaches you to be one.

2181
02:02:31,646 --> 02:02:33,855
We're clueless in what to do and when.

2182
02:02:34,021 --> 02:02:36,063
Day in and day out,
we get yelled at by our wives.

2183
02:02:37,271 --> 02:02:39,355
I've made plenty of mistakes
in my role as a husband.

2184
02:02:39,480 --> 02:02:40,355
I am not denying it.

2185
02:02:41,021 --> 02:02:43,063
But I'm slowly rectifying it
one after another.

2186
02:02:44,063 --> 02:02:45,605
Please give me some time.

2187
02:02:46,105 --> 02:02:47,605
Not divorce me.

2188
02:02:50,855 --> 02:02:54,105
Do you think any husband would
go to such lengths to plead as he did?

2189
02:02:54,355 --> 02:02:55,813
Find a way to work out your differences.

2190
02:02:56,271 --> 02:02:58,563
Ma'am he ruined everything.

2191
02:02:58,730 --> 02:03:00,938
Just speaking modestly
won't make him a good man.

2192
02:03:05,396 --> 02:03:06,813
Please ask them to play this.

2193
02:03:07,938 --> 02:03:08,938
What is this?

2194
02:03:30,021 --> 02:03:32,480
- Uncle, why are you recording?
- For proof!

2195
02:03:38,313 --> 02:03:39,313
Who's that woman?

2196
02:03:40,563 --> 02:03:41,813
She's my daughter's Class Teacher.

2197
02:03:42,313 --> 02:03:44,813
While going to pick up our daughter,
he picked up the teacher as well.

2198
02:03:48,438 --> 02:03:51,021
What's the guarantee
that she won't be my daughter's stepmom?

2199
02:03:51,188 --> 02:03:53,146
Then, my daughter would
have to endure stepmom tortures.

2200
02:03:53,271 --> 02:03:55,396
I don't want that for my daughter.
Please give me a divorce.

2201
02:03:56,521 --> 02:03:59,104
Mister, you did everything possible

2202
02:03:59,105 --> 02:04:01,938
but churning our dialogues
about supporting your wife.

2203
02:04:03,771 --> 02:04:05,062
Bloody rascal!

2204
02:04:05,063 --> 02:04:06,063
- It's not what it looks like--
- Shut up!

2205
02:04:08,563 --> 02:04:09,438
Please come here.

2206
02:04:09,771 --> 02:04:10,730
Come here!

2207
02:04:15,063 --> 02:04:16,813
Your husband has put you through a lot.

2208
02:04:17,521 --> 02:04:19,480
Do you want him to be happy
or be worried all his life?

2209
02:04:20,563 --> 02:04:21,563
He should be worried all his life.

2210
02:04:25,813 --> 02:04:27,063
Then don't divorce him.

2211
02:04:28,105 --> 02:04:30,730
What if he resumes dancing
with the teacher after the divorce?

2212
02:04:31,146 --> 02:04:32,063
Keep him with you.

2213
02:04:32,563 --> 02:04:33,980
Only then will he be on his toes
all the time.

2214
02:04:35,146 --> 02:04:36,521
I'm speaking out of experience.

2215
02:04:37,146 --> 02:04:38,688
I don't get what you're saying.

2216
02:04:40,313 --> 02:04:43,605
My husband did the same thing
as your husband did.

2217
02:04:44,813 --> 02:04:46,396
Do you see the typist sitting out there?

2218
02:04:49,480 --> 02:04:51,187
- He had an affair with her.
- Oh, no!

2219
02:04:51,188 --> 02:04:53,438
I told him to stay home
and not come to the court.

2220
02:04:53,813 --> 02:04:55,563
I could've chased him out of the house.

2221
02:04:55,855 --> 02:04:56,813
But I didn't do it.

2222
02:04:57,021 --> 02:04:58,855
Instead, keep him beside you
and make his life hell.

2223
02:04:59,021 --> 02:05:00,146
I don't think so, Ma'am.

2224
02:05:01,146 --> 02:05:02,938
Let him dance with whomever he wants to.

2225
02:05:03,313 --> 02:05:04,855
I don't care a damn about it.

2226
02:05:05,188 --> 02:05:08,105
Please give me a divorce right away
and give my daughter back.

2227
02:05:08,271 --> 02:05:10,230
- Please!
- What do you think of yourself?

2228
02:05:11,855 --> 02:05:13,520
You're repeating like a broken record.

2229
02:05:13,521 --> 02:05:15,896
You want me,
but you don't want Dad, is it?

2230
02:05:18,313 --> 02:05:21,313
Dear, you must not yell inside the court.

2231
02:05:21,730 --> 02:05:24,437
If you run your court properly,
why would I be screaming?

2232
02:05:24,438 --> 02:05:25,313
Mathi!

2233
02:05:25,688 --> 02:05:27,480
You're asking only what they both want.

2234
02:05:27,605 --> 02:05:31,021
I'm their daughter.
Why aren't you asking me?

2235
02:05:31,896 --> 02:05:33,063
You have a point, dear.

2236
02:05:34,021 --> 02:05:34,896
Fine.

2237
02:05:35,771 --> 02:05:36,646
Now, tell me.

2238
02:05:36,938 --> 02:05:39,646
With whom do you like to live
after your parents get divorced?

2239
02:05:39,813 --> 02:05:42,146
Husband and wife can divorce each other.

2240
02:05:42,438 --> 02:05:43,896
That's their wish.

2241
02:05:44,105 --> 02:05:46,605
But my parents must not divorce.

2242
02:05:46,730 --> 02:05:48,021
That's my wish!

2243
02:05:51,605 --> 02:05:53,146
The child's approval
is very important in this case.

2244
02:05:54,855 --> 02:05:56,271
I'm giving you both some time.

2245
02:05:56,855 --> 02:05:58,813
The next hearing will be after 3 months.

2246
02:05:59,146 --> 02:06:01,980
Until then, I order you both
to attend family counseling.

2247
02:06:02,563 --> 02:06:03,771
This is my decree!

2248
02:06:04,105 --> 02:06:05,605
And my decree is law!

2249
02:06:08,355 --> 02:06:10,605
Ma'am, this is not a kingdom?

2250
02:06:10,730 --> 02:06:12,021
To churn out punchlines.

2251
02:06:12,146 --> 02:06:13,938
I cannot wait for three months.

2252
02:06:14,188 --> 02:06:16,396
Please let me take my daughter home.

2253
02:06:17,813 --> 02:06:19,271
How dare you bark orders at me?

2254
02:06:19,938 --> 02:06:21,563
Who's the judge here, you or me?

2255
02:06:23,271 --> 02:06:25,396
I can't pass a verdict
at your convenience.

2256
02:06:25,563 --> 02:06:27,438
Only now has this dispute
been brought before the court.

2257
02:06:27,688 --> 02:06:29,105
It's not a mutual divorce, either.

2258
02:06:29,313 --> 02:06:31,730
Until you are divorced, who would have
the custody of your daughter

2259
02:06:31,855 --> 02:06:34,021
is something
the family must discuss and decide.

2260
02:06:35,563 --> 02:06:37,896
My head is spinning
after listening to you people speak.

2261
02:06:39,146 --> 02:06:40,605
I'm stepping out to have a cup of tea.

2262
02:06:40,896 --> 02:06:42,271
And when I return,
I'll tell you when the next hearing is.

2263
02:06:42,396 --> 02:06:44,438
Velu, bring the flask to my chamber.

2264
02:06:45,521 --> 02:06:47,770
Hey, I'm talking to you.
Come with me.

2265
02:06:47,771 --> 02:06:48,646
- Yes, Madam!
- Go.

2266
02:06:48,771 --> 02:06:49,896
Hey, keep moving.
Stop being lazy.

2267
02:06:53,396 --> 02:06:55,896
How dare you yell at the Judge?

2268
02:06:56,521 --> 02:06:57,938
Can't you maintain discipline?

2269
02:06:58,146 --> 02:06:59,270
Who taught you this behavior?

2270
02:06:59,271 --> 02:07:00,730
We come from a brave bloodline.

2271
02:07:01,896 --> 02:07:04,146
Tell her that we are not afraid
of the court or the Judge.

2272
02:07:04,271 --> 02:07:05,688
Please keep this nonsense to yourself.

2273
02:07:05,813 --> 02:07:07,105
Don't influence my daughter.

2274
02:07:07,855 --> 02:07:08,980
What do you mean?

2275
02:07:09,313 --> 02:07:11,646
She's our blood.

2276
02:07:12,063 --> 02:07:15,313
I hate these words, blood and legacy.

2277
02:07:15,480 --> 02:07:16,646
Just because you don't like it

2278
02:07:17,063 --> 02:07:18,146
we can't do anything about it.

2279
02:07:18,688 --> 02:07:20,063
I don't care, Bro!

2280
02:07:20,646 --> 02:07:22,105
Why are you
running your mouth unnecessarily?

2281
02:07:22,271 --> 02:07:24,479
- What?
- Have you forgotten the slap

2282
02:07:24,480 --> 02:07:25,938
that you got for speaking nonsense?

2283
02:07:26,396 --> 02:07:27,521
Would you like another slap from her?

2284
02:07:30,646 --> 02:07:34,896
My nephew returned that slap
with interest that very moment.

2285
02:07:36,605 --> 02:07:38,480
Just because you're stronger
doesn't mean you beat up everyone.

2286
02:07:38,646 --> 02:07:41,729
If she's a wrestler,
my nephew is a wrestler too.

2287
02:07:41,730 --> 02:07:43,271
- Oh, God!
- Got it?

2288
02:07:43,438 --> 02:07:45,980
Bro, we're having
a serious discussion here.

2289
02:07:46,146 --> 02:07:48,896
But you're joking in court
by calling him a wrestler.

2290
02:07:49,021 --> 02:07:50,105
Joking?

2291
02:07:50,313 --> 02:07:53,271
My nephew would've kicked her
like a football in the Palakkad match.

2292
02:07:53,438 --> 02:07:55,895
She escaped because she got pregnant.

2293
02:07:55,896 --> 02:07:57,187
Who was saved on that day,

2294
02:07:57,188 --> 02:07:58,438
- your nephew or me?
- It's you!

2295
02:07:58,688 --> 02:08:00,730
The people saw my nephew's match.

2296
02:08:01,271 --> 02:08:03,480
Do you even know who he won against?

2297
02:08:03,855 --> 02:08:05,980
Coach! A male Coach!

2298
02:08:06,355 --> 02:08:09,188
Compared to the Coach,
you're an ordinary player.

2299
02:08:09,438 --> 02:08:10,980
That too, you're a women player.

2300
02:08:11,188 --> 02:08:12,396
- Are you going to shut up or not?
- Uncle!

2301
02:08:12,646 --> 02:08:14,104
Please stop talking unnecessarily.

2302
02:08:14,105 --> 02:08:15,062
Why did we come to court?

2303
02:08:15,063 --> 02:08:17,437
She's been challenging,
yet you're asking me to back down.

2304
02:08:17,438 --> 02:08:18,521
Indeed, I'm a woman player.

2305
02:08:18,896 --> 02:08:20,980
But I'm ready to fight again.

2306
02:08:21,230 --> 02:08:23,479
Why don't you check
if your male player is ready?

2307
02:08:23,480 --> 02:08:24,479
Now you're talking, my girl.

2308
02:08:24,480 --> 02:08:26,187
- Keerthi, what's this nonsense?
- What did I do?

2309
02:08:26,188 --> 02:08:27,188
I'll speak now!

2310
02:08:27,980 --> 02:08:29,230
My father is ready to fight you.

2311
02:08:29,813 --> 02:08:32,105
Hey, sweetie, please stay quiet.

2312
02:08:32,355 --> 02:08:34,020
Why are you dragging me into this?

2313
02:08:34,021 --> 02:08:37,812
We can beat her only
if we play her game.

2314
02:08:37,813 --> 02:08:39,771
Please don't say anything
for a while and stand out there.

2315
02:08:40,355 --> 02:08:41,687
Go! Go and stand out there.

2316
02:08:41,688 --> 02:08:43,146
I'm not blowing up this problem.

2317
02:08:43,771 --> 02:08:44,980
I don't know what you have in mind.

2318
02:08:45,813 --> 02:08:46,854
Go!

2319
02:08:46,855 --> 02:08:48,812
- It'll be humiliating for us.
- How do we get our child back?

2320
02:08:48,813 --> 02:08:52,730
My father did not train for 15 years
to become a wrestler.

2321
02:08:52,855 --> 02:08:54,813
He only trained for 15 days.

2322
02:08:55,021 --> 02:08:56,563
Yet he wont the match.

2323
02:08:57,063 --> 02:08:59,896
Your father won once in his lifetime.

2324
02:09:00,271 --> 02:09:02,520
That's called luck not talent.

2325
02:09:02,521 --> 02:09:05,063
My father took part in only one match.

2326
02:09:05,230 --> 02:09:07,105
Yet he won that match.

2327
02:09:07,271 --> 02:09:08,563
- Hey, Baby--
- Hey!

2328
02:09:08,688 --> 02:09:10,521
We're discussing about wrestling.

2329
02:09:10,813 --> 02:09:12,563
You have nothing to do with it.

2330
02:09:12,813 --> 02:09:15,230
Hey, you're going overboard.
Apologize to him.

2331
02:09:15,480 --> 02:09:16,771
Why should I apologize to him?

2332
02:09:16,896 --> 02:09:18,895
What does he know about wrestling?

2333
02:09:18,896 --> 02:09:20,646
Hey, fake candy.

2334
02:09:21,063 --> 02:09:23,605
All these years, you fooled people
by calling yourself a wrestler.

2335
02:09:23,813 --> 02:09:25,895
But a young kid smeared you
with dung and humiliated you.

2336
02:09:25,896 --> 02:09:27,896
Had it been me,
I would have killed myself.

2337
02:09:28,188 --> 02:09:30,980
You claim
that my client won by luck, right?

2338
02:09:31,188 --> 02:09:32,979
We'll prove it wrong.
When is the match?

2339
02:09:32,980 --> 02:09:34,355
- Sattam!
- We'll have it tomorrow.

2340
02:09:35,271 --> 02:09:37,355
- But one condition.
- What's the condition?

2341
02:09:38,355 --> 02:09:39,730
If he wins the match…

2342
02:09:40,230 --> 02:09:41,396
Mathi can live with him.

2343
02:09:41,646 --> 02:09:42,938
But if I win…

2344
02:09:43,396 --> 02:09:44,646
you should send Mathi with me.

2345
02:09:48,396 --> 02:09:51,355
- That's not right. Pick something else.
- Now, I challenge you to talk.

2346
02:09:52,688 --> 02:09:54,855
What? Are you scared?

2347
02:09:55,105 --> 02:09:56,563
My father is ready for the competition.

2348
02:09:57,355 --> 02:09:59,563
But there's a change in the condition.

2349
02:09:59,771 --> 02:10:00,646
What change?

2350
02:10:00,855 --> 02:10:03,979
If you win, I'll come with you.
Okay!

2351
02:10:03,980 --> 02:10:07,813
But if my father wins,
you should come with us.

2352
02:10:09,355 --> 02:10:11,438
Sweetie, stop talking nonsense.

2353
02:10:11,813 --> 02:10:14,438
I don't want a competition.
Let her go with her.

2354
02:10:14,646 --> 02:10:15,770
I don't have any qualms about it.

2355
02:10:15,771 --> 02:10:17,438
I don't want your charity.

2356
02:10:17,646 --> 02:10:19,438
I'll win in the competition
and then take her

2357
02:10:19,730 --> 02:10:20,937
You, people, fix the venue.

2358
02:10:20,938 --> 02:10:22,605
We'll conduct at the Temple ground.

2359
02:10:22,896 --> 02:10:24,355
Uncle, why are you doing this?

2360
02:10:25,063 --> 02:10:28,313
If you insist let's conduct it
inside our house.

2361
02:10:28,521 --> 02:10:29,479
Not at a ground.

2362
02:10:29,480 --> 02:10:32,438
Oh, he is avoid the humiliation
in front of the people.

2363
02:10:32,605 --> 02:10:34,313
Uncle, this is a family matter.

2364
02:10:34,480 --> 02:10:36,437
It won't look good
if we fight in public.

2365
02:10:36,438 --> 02:10:39,313
Didn't you fight your wife
in front of people before?

2366
02:10:39,438 --> 02:10:40,521
- What happened now?
- How dare you?

2367
02:10:40,855 --> 02:10:42,437
You're disrespecting him.

2368
02:10:42,438 --> 02:10:43,770
You better speak with respect.

2369
02:10:43,771 --> 02:10:44,771
This is how I speak.

2370
02:10:44,896 --> 02:10:46,562
Are you trying to cheat
by holding the match inside the house?

2371
02:10:46,563 --> 02:10:47,896
The match will take place
at the ground.

2372
02:10:48,146 --> 02:10:49,104
No one can change it--

2373
02:10:49,105 --> 02:10:50,645
- Sattam, please make them understand.
- Be respectful!

2374
02:10:50,646 --> 02:10:52,479
- Ask him to keep quiet.
- Please be quiet.

2375
02:10:52,480 --> 02:10:53,563
Uncle, please!

2376
02:10:53,771 --> 02:10:55,145
Please hear me out.

2377
02:10:55,146 --> 02:10:56,313
- Please don't yell inside the court.
- We'll talk it out.

2378
02:10:57,063 --> 02:10:58,145
Everyone, please calm down.

2379
02:10:58,146 --> 02:10:59,437
- Lawyer, tell them to keep quiet.
- He is going on and on!

2380
02:10:59,438 --> 02:11:00,980
- How can I keep quiet?
- Order! Order! Order!

2381
02:11:02,146 --> 02:11:03,813
Do you think you're in a court
or a market?

2382
02:11:04,771 --> 02:11:06,355
What did I instruct you people to do?

2383
02:11:07,480 --> 02:11:08,813
Did you discuss and come to a decision?

2384
02:11:09,313 --> 02:11:10,646
Who's taking the kid?

2385
02:11:10,896 --> 02:11:12,105
We're not going to discuss
to make a decision, Ma'am.

2386
02:11:13,146 --> 02:11:14,480
Instead, we're going to
play against each other.

2387
02:11:15,521 --> 02:11:17,021
Play against each other, you say?

2388
02:11:18,605 --> 02:11:20,646
- What game?
- Wrestling!

2389
02:11:21,396 --> 02:11:23,813
Whoever wins can get the child's custody.

2390
02:11:25,480 --> 02:11:28,355
Never before have I passed
such an unusual verdict.

2391
02:11:31,230 --> 02:11:33,313
You should officiate this competition.

2392
02:11:33,438 --> 02:11:34,855
They will cheat us.

2393
02:11:35,230 --> 02:11:36,896
There's no space for such a decision.

2394
02:11:39,313 --> 02:11:41,146
You may conduct the competition.

2395
02:11:42,896 --> 02:11:44,313
I'll come there as an audience.

2396
02:11:45,563 --> 02:11:48,021
I have a long standing wish
to watch a wrestling match live.

2397
02:11:49,646 --> 02:11:52,230
And if the match is between
a husband and a wife…

2398
02:11:53,146 --> 02:11:54,229
…quite exciting!

2399
02:11:54,230 --> 02:11:55,563
I'm also excited, Madam.

2400
02:11:59,355 --> 02:12:00,355
Case dismissed!

2401
02:12:13,563 --> 02:12:15,688
THE HUSBAND OR THE WIFE?

2402
02:12:18,271 --> 02:12:19,562
{\an8}NOT JUST IN INDIAN HISTORY!
THIS IS A FIRST IN WORLD HISTORY!

2403
02:12:19,563 --> 02:12:21,730
OPEN WRESTLING MATCH
BETWEEN HUSBAND AND WIFE

2404
02:12:40,313 --> 02:12:42,270
Why are you charging 100 bucks
to watch a husband and wife fight?

2405
02:12:42,271 --> 02:12:43,146
How's this fair?

2406
02:12:43,271 --> 02:12:44,813
It's 100 bucks when
you buy at the counter.

2407
02:12:44,938 --> 02:12:45,895
If you're late by half an hour

2408
02:12:45,896 --> 02:12:47,438
it'll be sold in black for 500 bucks.
Scoot!

2409
02:12:47,563 --> 02:12:48,813
- Come on, pay up.
- Three tickets.

2410
02:12:49,563 --> 02:12:50,730
Give me a 140ml.

2411
02:12:50,896 --> 02:12:53,104
140? The ticket cost is only 100 bucks.

2412
02:12:53,105 --> 02:12:54,437
Lining up immediately
looking at the queue.

2413
02:12:54,438 --> 02:12:57,063
Oh, he mistook it for another shop.

2414
02:12:57,646 --> 02:12:58,855
Are you happy now?

2415
02:12:59,313 --> 02:13:01,271
I wanted to finish this competition
without anyone's knowledge.

2416
02:13:01,646 --> 02:13:04,813
You suggested temple ground and
now see the crowd it has gathered.

2417
02:13:04,980 --> 02:13:06,020
Sorry, Son.

2418
02:13:06,021 --> 02:13:07,646
We didn't expect
so many people to show up.

2419
02:13:07,855 --> 02:13:09,646
How did everyone come to know about it?

2420
02:13:10,105 --> 02:13:12,813
Sattam told his wife all about
what happened in court.

2421
02:13:13,021 --> 02:13:15,937
She's an admin of four
or five WhatsApp group.

2422
02:13:15,938 --> 02:13:16,813
She put out a broadcast message.

2423
02:13:17,021 --> 02:13:18,855
People won't spread the good news.

2424
02:13:18,980 --> 02:13:21,355
But if it's a bad news
they'll compete to spread the message.

2425
02:13:21,563 --> 02:13:23,146
But why are you selling tickets?

2426
02:13:23,396 --> 02:13:25,563
Or else we won't be able to
control the crowd.

2427
02:13:25,980 --> 02:13:28,188
I'm not going to take this money.
Look over there.

2428
02:13:29,438 --> 02:13:31,812
- Who are they?
- Cheers girls!

2429
02:13:31,813 --> 02:13:35,437
No game can be held without cheer girls,
as per the new Government rule.

2430
02:13:35,438 --> 02:13:37,688
There are a group of fans for cheer girls.

2431
02:13:37,813 --> 02:13:40,521
Look, the Judge is also eager
to watch the fight.

2432
02:13:46,021 --> 02:13:46,980
Greetings, Madam Judge.

2433
02:13:47,313 --> 02:13:49,521
I reckon you'll win this match.

2434
02:13:50,980 --> 02:13:52,188
What are you thinking about?

2435
02:13:52,438 --> 02:13:54,480
Your daughter has faith in you
and have placed bets.

2436
02:13:55,188 --> 02:13:57,688
Win this fight
and bring the family back together.

2437
02:13:59,396 --> 02:14:01,438
- Show me your ticket!
- Hey, it's the Judge!

2438
02:14:02,855 --> 02:14:04,020
I'll handle you when
you come to the court.

2439
02:14:04,021 --> 02:14:05,063
Oh, no, please don't Madam.

2440
02:14:18,396 --> 02:14:20,813
Hey, Sweetie, are you ready
to watch Mom and Dad's match?

2441
02:14:23,188 --> 02:14:26,020
Don't forget you're up against
a State Champion.

2442
02:14:26,021 --> 02:14:28,813
The same State Champion trained with me
to spar with her.

2443
02:14:29,271 --> 02:14:30,813
I know her all movements.

2444
02:14:31,355 --> 02:14:33,938
Dad, speaking about it here
is not important.

2445
02:14:34,063 --> 02:14:35,146
It should reflect in the ring.

2446
02:14:35,563 --> 02:14:38,020
Dad, please manage to win the match.

2447
02:14:38,021 --> 02:14:39,062
I will, dear.

2448
02:14:39,063 --> 02:14:42,730
Don't say you'd try your best.
So, make a promise.

2449
02:14:42,896 --> 02:14:44,896
And prove that my Dad is a Hero.

2450
02:14:48,230 --> 02:14:49,230
Please do it, Dad.

2451
02:14:50,605 --> 02:14:52,521
Promise! For you!

2452
02:14:52,896 --> 02:14:56,313
The most anticipated competition
is about to begin!

2453
02:14:56,438 --> 02:14:58,438
- I'm going in. Take care.
- You carry on.

2454
02:14:58,563 --> 02:15:00,021
Uncle, please hand me your phone.

2455
02:15:00,230 --> 02:15:02,063
My phone? Here you go.

2456
02:15:04,230 --> 02:15:06,188
- Who are you calling?
- Meenu Teacher.

2457
02:15:06,480 --> 02:15:08,687
- I'm inviting her to watch the match.
- Oh, no!

2458
02:15:08,688 --> 02:15:10,271
You're going to mess everything up.

2459
02:15:10,563 --> 02:15:13,521
As it is your mother is going to
knead your father to ground.

2460
02:15:13,688 --> 02:15:17,146
If your teacher shows up
then your father will be a minced parotta.

2461
02:15:17,396 --> 02:15:21,355
Cricket commentators
were once successful players.

2462
02:15:21,480 --> 02:15:25,229
So, to begin this match
and to render commentary…

2463
02:15:25,230 --> 02:15:27,105
we welcome former Punjab Wrestler,
Balbir Singh.

2464
02:15:27,230 --> 02:15:30,063
Please give him a warm welcome.

2465
02:15:35,438 --> 02:15:38,562
<i>He's the direct successor of
Undertaker from the world of wrestling.</i>

2466
02:15:38,563 --> 02:15:40,730
<i>No one calls him
but he claims it himself.</i>

2467
02:15:41,813 --> 02:15:43,355
Greetings to all!

2468
02:15:43,938 --> 02:15:46,937
A group is waiting to watch
if the husband would beat up the wife.

2469
02:15:46,938 --> 02:15:49,396
Another group is waiting to watch
if the wife would beat up the husband.

2470
02:15:50,063 --> 02:15:52,688
In fact, to see other families
fight with each other

2471
02:15:52,980 --> 02:15:55,313
all of you are here to enjoy the match.

2472
02:15:56,396 --> 02:15:58,188
You shouldn't be applauding
but feel ashamed.

2473
02:15:59,855 --> 02:16:00,730
Bring them out!

2474
02:16:16,396 --> 02:16:17,812
You're going to fight
with your wife, right?

2475
02:16:17,813 --> 02:16:19,021
Then, why are you hyping it up?

2476
02:16:19,146 --> 02:16:20,146
Don't bother about it.

2477
02:16:20,521 --> 02:16:22,770
You seem like a true bred Tamilian.

2478
02:16:22,771 --> 02:16:23,980
But they're calling you a Punjab wrestler.

2479
02:16:24,271 --> 02:16:25,646
Dinesh Karthick plays for Bengaluru.

2480
02:16:25,813 --> 02:16:27,396
Even Nataraj plays for Delhi.

2481
02:16:27,605 --> 02:16:29,979
What's wrong if I go to Punjab to wrestle?

2482
02:16:29,980 --> 02:16:31,687
Are you here to fight
or to interview me?

2483
02:16:31,688 --> 02:16:32,646
Call out your wife!

2484
02:16:36,855 --> 02:16:38,896
Oh! She's not even wearing a track suit.

2485
02:16:40,188 --> 02:16:42,105
I think she believes she can
take you down even in a saree.

2486
02:16:53,438 --> 02:16:56,438
Hey, I know what's running on your mind.

2487
02:16:56,605 --> 02:16:58,063
Why is she wearing a saree?

2488
02:16:58,396 --> 02:17:00,313
She's going to sprinkle you
like the dung on the wall.

2489
02:17:02,146 --> 02:17:04,145
Posing won't help you win the match.

2490
02:17:04,146 --> 02:17:05,187
Just because I was posing,

2491
02:17:05,188 --> 02:17:07,270
the Biharis beat me up,
stripping me down to underwear.

2492
02:17:07,271 --> 02:17:08,730
I'm helping you get away.
Escape on the bike.

2493
02:17:08,855 --> 02:17:09,813
I won't!

2494
02:17:10,855 --> 02:17:11,896
Fate has never spared anyone.

2495
02:17:12,188 --> 02:17:14,563
He won't back down, it seems.
Woman, hurry up.

2496
02:17:14,771 --> 02:17:17,355
Keerthi! Keerthi!

2497
02:17:19,146 --> 02:17:22,188
Keerthi! Keerthi!

2498
02:17:22,646 --> 02:17:23,605
Welcome, Dear!

2499
02:17:26,313 --> 02:17:27,521
I think she just did push ups.

2500
02:17:28,313 --> 02:17:30,688
The only request I would like to
put forward to the Government is…

2501
02:17:30,813 --> 02:17:32,896
It's simple.
Conduct husband and wife fights…

2502
02:17:33,063 --> 02:17:37,146
on a stage yearly like a IPL match

2503
02:17:37,438 --> 02:17:39,812
they wouldn't have to go to court
and save up on lawyer's fee.

2504
02:17:39,813 --> 02:17:42,646
The Judge Madam
should approve this request.

2505
02:17:43,105 --> 02:17:44,605
He keeps yapping nonsense!

2506
02:17:44,730 --> 02:17:46,938
In today's 20-20 wrestling match

2507
02:17:47,230 --> 02:17:49,479
whoever scores 20 points first

2508
02:17:49,480 --> 02:17:50,813
they will be the winner of the match.

2509
02:17:50,980 --> 02:17:53,355
Red colour cheer girls support Keerthi.

2510
02:17:53,980 --> 02:17:56,396
Blue colour cheer girls support Veera.

2511
02:17:57,021 --> 02:17:59,187
Hey, I'm red too. Same family.

2512
02:17:59,188 --> 02:18:01,313
Hey, the colour on
the side of the jersey is yours.

2513
02:18:01,646 --> 02:18:03,521
You don't even know the basics and you're
here to fight wearing a swimming costume.

2514
02:18:03,813 --> 02:18:05,105
Ready, first round.

2515
02:18:05,313 --> 02:18:06,730
Come on, break his jaw.

2516
02:18:09,188 --> 02:18:10,105
Is she taking his blessings?

2517
02:18:11,688 --> 02:18:14,938
Like she dusted her hands,
she's about to dust off her husband…

2518
02:18:15,105 --> 02:18:16,437
I'm giving you the warrior princess.

2519
02:18:16,438 --> 02:18:18,187
Hey, you too pull up a stance.

2520
02:18:18,188 --> 02:18:19,520
Why are you standing idle
like you're waiting for a bus?

2521
02:18:19,521 --> 02:18:20,521
Huh! People!

2522
02:18:20,855 --> 02:18:22,105
Shout out your cheers!

2523
02:18:22,855 --> 02:18:23,730
Come on, cheer!

2524
02:18:24,480 --> 02:18:25,355
Oh, God!

2525
02:18:26,646 --> 02:18:28,521
Fight your wife, damn it.
Not me!

2526
02:18:29,063 --> 02:18:29,938
Ready!

2527
02:18:30,230 --> 02:18:32,105
It's a wonderful spectacle to watch.

2528
02:18:32,313 --> 02:18:34,230
This is what you call a great fight.

2529
02:18:38,063 --> 02:18:40,562
Hey, instead of fighting,
why are you giving her weird looks?

2530
02:18:40,563 --> 02:18:43,645
Woman, hit him so hard that
he should not stand up for his life.

2531
02:18:43,646 --> 02:18:44,521
Oh, God!

2532
02:18:45,063 --> 02:18:46,855
Since he got in the ring,
he's only been beating me.

2533
02:19:05,563 --> 02:19:09,063
His gaze it not a fighter's gaze.

2534
02:19:09,730 --> 02:19:12,938
He must fight and explain his gaze.

2535
02:19:13,105 --> 02:19:15,230
Woman, do a somersault.
Damn you!

2536
02:19:15,730 --> 02:19:18,938
Instead of fighting each other
they're throwing sand at me.

2537
02:19:19,063 --> 02:19:21,145
Hey, stop! First round over.

2538
02:19:21,146 --> 02:19:23,563
I shall go up to the stage
to continue the commentary.

2539
02:19:30,730 --> 02:19:32,396
- How's my game, Sattam?
- Super, Veera!

2540
02:19:34,938 --> 02:19:36,521
I underestimated you.

2541
02:19:36,730 --> 02:19:38,105
You haven't lost touch.

2542
02:19:51,771 --> 02:19:53,230
Second round, start!

2543
02:19:56,688 --> 02:19:57,771
Veera, keep it up!

2544
02:20:10,063 --> 02:20:10,938
That's it!

2545
02:20:14,896 --> 02:20:16,813
Twist his arms.
Don't spare him.

2546
02:20:22,438 --> 02:20:24,230
Just like you flip a parotta…

2547
02:20:24,396 --> 02:20:26,438
she flipped her husband in the air.

2548
02:20:26,730 --> 02:20:27,605
Wonderful shot!

2549
02:20:27,980 --> 02:20:29,979
- 4 points!
- Dad!

2550
02:20:29,980 --> 02:20:32,521
Hey, get up.
You're lying down as if you're chilling.

2551
02:20:48,563 --> 02:20:50,895
Hey, is he an old fighter?

2552
02:20:50,896 --> 02:20:52,813
You can't teach him.
Take him away.

2553
02:21:07,230 --> 02:21:08,479
She's thrashing him like washing clothes.

2554
02:21:08,480 --> 02:21:09,563
- Oh, no!
- Hey!

2555
02:21:09,771 --> 02:21:12,980
No man has ever won a battle
against his wife.

2556
02:21:18,271 --> 02:21:20,187
Mathi, do you think your father will win?

2557
02:21:20,188 --> 02:21:21,938
I'm clueless just like you, Ma'am.

2558
02:21:29,105 --> 02:21:31,021
Yeah, Keerthi, that's it.
That's super!

2559
02:21:38,271 --> 02:21:40,188
Second rounds, ends.

2560
02:21:40,855 --> 02:21:43,438
I pity the blue colour cheer girls.

2561
02:21:44,771 --> 02:21:46,979
He's not going to
give you the opportunity to dance.

2562
02:21:46,980 --> 02:21:48,813
Please have your food
and sleep at home.

2563
02:21:49,938 --> 02:21:50,813
Have it.

2564
02:21:51,813 --> 02:21:54,646
Damn, she exhausted her husband
by the second round.

2565
02:21:54,855 --> 02:21:56,271
And he's shamelessly drinking water.

2566
02:21:57,855 --> 02:21:59,687
I wonder if in the third round he would
drink water again

2567
02:21:59,688 --> 02:22:01,520
or ride in the ambulance.

2568
02:22:01,521 --> 02:22:03,187
Hey, stop with the yapping.

2569
02:22:03,188 --> 02:22:04,145
I don't need it anymore.

2570
02:22:04,146 --> 02:22:05,730
Hey, Veera,
I'm giving you a second chance.

2571
02:22:05,896 --> 02:22:06,896
Escape from here.

2572
02:22:07,063 --> 02:22:09,354
They're trolling you.
Next round thrash her.

2573
02:22:09,355 --> 02:22:10,813
Uncle, be careful, it's hurting.

2574
02:22:10,938 --> 02:22:13,104
Why aren't you thrashing her?

2575
02:22:13,105 --> 02:22:14,354
She's using a new technique.

2576
02:22:14,355 --> 02:22:16,188
- You can do it!
- He has started to shiver in pain.

2577
02:22:16,521 --> 02:22:18,604
- Don't give up, Veera.
- Come on! Come on!

2578
02:22:18,605 --> 02:22:19,812
He's only full of theatrics.

2579
02:22:19,813 --> 02:22:22,021
Either way, he's going to get beaten up.

2580
02:22:35,521 --> 02:22:36,438
What just happened?

2581
02:22:37,021 --> 02:22:38,355
He scored a point!

2582
02:22:40,021 --> 02:22:40,896
Hey!

2583
02:23:10,980 --> 02:23:11,980
How's my game now?

2584
02:23:12,230 --> 02:23:14,688
You just scored two points
didn't win the match yet.

2585
02:23:14,896 --> 02:23:17,230
She has scored 12 points.
You need 10 more to level with her.

2586
02:23:25,063 --> 02:23:27,396
That's like it, my boy!

2587
02:23:40,771 --> 02:23:42,563
Hey, Keerthi!

2588
02:23:42,688 --> 02:23:44,105
That was a wonderful shot!

2589
02:23:44,230 --> 02:23:45,438
Keerthi back to form!

2590
02:23:56,521 --> 02:23:57,396
Come on!

2591
02:24:05,813 --> 02:24:07,563
This fight is not circumstantial.

2592
02:24:07,771 --> 02:24:12,312
It was years of suppressed anger
that Keerthi finally let out on him.

2593
02:24:12,313 --> 02:24:14,063
Dad, come on, get up!

2594
02:24:16,396 --> 02:24:17,396
Oh, God!

2595
02:24:26,855 --> 02:24:28,230
Third round, ends.

2596
02:24:37,105 --> 02:24:38,521
Dad must win.

2597
02:24:38,646 --> 02:24:39,938
Dad must win.

2598
02:24:40,438 --> 02:24:41,771
Dad must win.

2599
02:24:42,146 --> 02:24:43,521
Dad must win.

2600
02:24:43,896 --> 02:24:45,271
Dad must win.

2601
02:24:45,563 --> 02:24:47,105
Dad must win.

2602
02:24:47,313 --> 02:24:48,645
Dad must win.

2603
02:24:48,646 --> 02:24:50,563
<i>My father is also a…</i>

2604
02:24:51,396 --> 02:24:52,354
<i>…wrestler!</i>

2605
02:24:52,355 --> 02:24:54,480
<i>My father is a wrestler, just like you.</i>

2606
02:24:54,688 --> 02:24:56,313
<i>He won against a coach.</i>

2607
02:24:56,813 --> 02:24:58,230
Dad must win.

2608
02:24:58,438 --> 02:25:00,480
<i>Prove that you're a Hero.</i>

2609
02:25:04,396 --> 02:25:06,771
Dad must win.
Dad must win.

2610
02:25:13,855 --> 02:25:15,355
Dad must win.

2611
02:25:21,688 --> 02:25:23,605
Fourth round, start!

2612
02:25:24,063 --> 02:25:26,020
You need to score only one more point.

2613
02:25:26,021 --> 02:25:27,021
Finish him off!

2614
02:25:46,271 --> 02:25:47,396
4 points!

2615
02:26:30,021 --> 02:26:31,480
What happened?

2616
02:26:33,521 --> 02:26:34,688
What is wrong with her?

2617
02:26:38,021 --> 02:26:39,980
Aren't you ashamed
to score points like this?

2618
02:26:40,271 --> 02:26:42,563
Among husband and wife,
it doesn't matter who scores first.

2619
02:26:54,146 --> 02:26:55,271
Keep it coming!

2620
02:27:04,730 --> 02:27:06,480
Veera was weak
in all the previous rounds.

2621
02:27:07,146 --> 02:27:10,521
But how is he performing so well
in the last round?

2622
02:27:11,021 --> 02:27:13,355
Even I, a heavyweight wrestler,
don't understand it.

2623
02:27:23,480 --> 02:27:24,355
Dad!

2624
02:27:29,230 --> 02:27:30,480
19-19, equal!

2625
02:27:37,771 --> 02:27:39,271
Why is she stepping back?

2626
02:27:39,730 --> 02:27:41,854
Is Veera using a new technique?

2627
02:27:41,855 --> 02:27:44,895
Keerthi, come on, come on!
Ready, ready, ready!

2628
02:27:44,896 --> 02:27:45,937
One more point to win.

2629
02:27:45,938 --> 02:27:47,980
Time is running out.
Don't miss it.

2630
02:27:55,188 --> 02:27:57,104
That's it. Cross the line!

2631
02:27:57,105 --> 02:27:58,562
One more point. Cross the line.

2632
02:27:58,563 --> 02:27:59,979
Quit fooling around and cross the line!

2633
02:27:59,980 --> 02:28:01,271
He's back in the ring.

2634
02:28:06,688 --> 02:28:08,230
- Keerthi!
- Why did she faint?

2635
02:28:09,063 --> 02:28:09,938
Keerthi!

2636
02:28:14,646 --> 02:28:15,813
Kee-- Keerthi!

2637
02:28:17,646 --> 02:28:18,771
{\an8}Keerthi, what happened?

2638
02:28:20,980 --> 02:28:21,855
Keerthi!

2639
02:28:23,313 --> 02:28:24,605
Hey, Sattam!

2640
02:28:24,813 --> 02:28:25,771
Mom!

2641
02:28:25,896 --> 02:28:27,479
- Keerthi!
- What happened to Mom?

2642
02:28:27,480 --> 02:28:28,355
Mom!

2643
02:28:28,855 --> 02:28:30,355
- Mom!
- She was playing well.

2644
02:28:31,021 --> 02:28:31,896
Dear!

2645
02:28:32,230 --> 02:28:34,355
I suspect Veera has something
to do with it.

2646
02:28:34,980 --> 02:28:38,312
Was he actually playing a fair match?
Or was he resorting to tricks?

2647
02:28:38,313 --> 02:28:40,145
Oh, God! Don't just stand there.
Help me!

2648
02:28:40,146 --> 02:28:41,854
Lift her.
Let's take her to the hospital.

2649
02:28:41,855 --> 02:28:44,313
Wait a minute.
Let me check what's wrong.

2650
02:28:50,855 --> 02:28:52,395
Nothing to worry.

2651
02:28:52,396 --> 02:28:53,813
It's good news!

2652
02:28:54,146 --> 02:28:55,188
She's pregnant.

2653
02:28:58,480 --> 02:28:59,438
What does that mean?

2654
02:28:59,896 --> 02:29:01,771
You're going to have a baby brother, dear.

2655
02:29:03,730 --> 02:29:04,730
She's pregnant?!

2656
02:29:05,105 --> 02:29:06,063
Why are you anxious?

2657
02:29:06,396 --> 02:29:07,979
He wouldn't go to work
when they had only one child.

2658
02:29:07,980 --> 02:29:09,020
Now they're having another!

2659
02:29:09,021 --> 02:29:10,645
I think I must quit my job.

2660
02:29:10,646 --> 02:29:11,521
Pregnant?

2661
02:29:12,230 --> 02:29:15,229
Bloody sinners!
In my years of wrestling experience,

2662
02:29:15,230 --> 02:29:18,230
this is the first time someone has
gotten pregnant during a fight.

2663
02:29:19,230 --> 02:29:20,687
You two were in this together,

2664
02:29:20,688 --> 02:29:22,937
and you still had the audacity
to file for divorce!

2665
02:29:22,938 --> 02:29:24,563
Bloody rascals!

2666
02:29:25,938 --> 02:29:27,229
No matter how big the problem is,

2667
02:29:27,230 --> 02:29:29,395
my nephew solves it
by getting her pregnant.

2668
02:29:29,396 --> 02:29:30,437
Hey, Uncle!

2669
02:29:30,438 --> 02:29:31,355
Guys!

2670
02:29:31,896 --> 02:29:34,645
First they wrestled in bed,

2671
02:29:34,646 --> 02:29:36,312
then came here to wrestle in the ring.

2672
02:29:36,313 --> 02:29:38,063
We must learn something from this.

2673
02:29:38,938 --> 02:29:42,646
A quarrel between husband and wife
isn't a third person's business.

2674
02:29:42,980 --> 02:29:44,730
That's the moral of this story.

2675
02:29:45,188 --> 02:29:46,688
Everyone, get going! Leave!

2676
02:29:52,813 --> 02:29:53,730
Are you happy?

2677
02:30:07,896 --> 02:30:08,771
{\an8}Two babies?

2678
02:30:09,605 --> 02:30:10,896
{\an8}I only asked for one.

2679
02:30:11,313 --> 02:30:12,355
{\an8}Another one is a bonus.

2680
02:30:15,896 --> 02:30:18,104
{\an8}You promised to make me
the Mary Kom of sports.

2681
02:30:18,105 --> 02:30:21,063
{\an8}Instead, you gave me three kids
and turned me into a homemaker Mary Kom.

2682
02:30:27,105 --> 02:30:28,480
{\an8}I won't go back on my word.

2683
02:30:29,021 --> 02:30:31,271
{\an8}I won't rest until I make you
the Mary Kom of sports.

2684
02:30:31,730 --> 02:30:33,688
{\an8}I swear on my three children.

2685
02:30:37,813 --> 02:30:42,146
{\an8}Since you're pregnant,
I didn't want to hide the truth from you.

2686
02:30:43,105 --> 02:30:46,771
{\an8}The coach devised a plan to defeat you.

2687
02:30:49,396 --> 02:30:50,605
{\an8}Today, I may have won.

2688
02:30:51,563 --> 02:30:54,355
{\an8}But this victory belongs to you.

2689
02:30:57,146 --> 02:31:00,271
{\an8}I was in love with a guy for four years.

2690
02:31:00,896 --> 02:31:04,605
{\an8}He said, "I don't like you wearing
this costume and playing this game."

2691
02:31:05,146 --> 02:31:08,438
{\an8}"It makes me uncomfortable
when other men look at you."

2692
02:31:09,063 --> 02:31:12,980
{\an8}He said, "Please quit wrestling
after we get married."

2693
02:31:14,730 --> 02:31:18,105
{\an8}I told him, "I don't mind leaving you,
but I can't quit wrestling."

2694
02:31:19,771 --> 02:31:23,105
{\an8}He was well-educated,
but his thinking was flawed.

2695
02:31:24,021 --> 02:31:26,813
{\an8}But your husband is uneducated.

2696
02:31:28,105 --> 02:31:32,605
{\an8}Even after you gave birth,
he wanted you to succeed in wrestling.

2697
02:31:33,980 --> 02:31:35,063
{\an8}Don't miss this opportunity.

2698
02:31:53,146 --> 02:31:54,063
Wow!

2699
02:31:57,188 --> 02:31:58,563
Come on, Keerthi!

2700
02:31:59,938 --> 02:32:01,438
- Cheer for Mom.
- Mom!

2701
02:32:03,146 --> 02:32:04,730
Hey, Mom is looking at you guys.

